window.COURSE_DATA_JS = {"chapters":[{"id":"js01","title":"Fundamentals","emoji":"🟡","lessons":[{"title":"What is JavaScript?","html":"\n<p><b>JavaScript<\/b> is a lightweight, interpreted (or JIT-compiled)\nprogramming language with <b>first-class functions<\/b>. MDN describes it\nas prototype-based, garbage-collected, and dynamically typed — supporting\nimperative, functional and object-oriented paradigms. Despite the name,\nit has nothing to do with Java.<\/p>\n\n<p>The three core web technologies, per MDN:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>HTML<\/b> — structure and meaning<\/li>\n<li><b>CSS<\/b> — presentation and layout<\/li>\n<li><b>JavaScript<\/b> — <i>interactivity and dynamic behaviour<\/i><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>JS runs in browsers (making pages interactive) and outside them too\n(Node.js for servers, tools, and more). It's standardized as\n<b>ECMAScript<\/b> (ECMA-262), with new features added every year.<\/p>\n\n<p>This course runs your code in the browser's own engine — the same\nV8/SpiderMonkey that powers real websites. Press Run and see the\nconsole output.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Welcome to the JS Tutor! 🟡\n// Everything after // is a comment — the browser ignores it.\n\nconsole.log(\"Hello, JavaScript!\");\n\n// Variables hold values\nconst name = \"Ada\";\nlet year = 2026;\n\n// Template literals embed values with ${}\nconsole.log(`Hello, ${name}! Welcome to ${year}.`);\n\n// Math works as expected\nconsole.log(\"2 + 3 =\", 2 + 3);\n","title_fa":"جاوااسکریپت چیست؟","html_fa":"\n<p><b>جاوااسکریپت (JavaScript)<\/b> یک زبان برنامه‌نویسی سبک، تفسیری (یا\nبا کامپایل لحظه‌ای) با <b>توابع درجه‌یک<\/b> است. MDN آن را مبتنی بر\nprototype، garbage-collected و با تایپِ پویا توصیف می‌کند — و پشتیبان\nسه پارادایم: امری، تابعی و شیءگرا. با وجود اسمش، ربطی به جاوا\nندارد.<\/p>\n\n<p>سه تکنولوژی اصلی وب، طبق MDN:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>HTML<\/b> — ساختار و معنا<\/li>\n<li><b>CSS<\/b> — نمایش و چیدمان<\/li>\n<li><b>JavaScript<\/b> — <i>تعامل و رفتار پویا<\/i><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>JS در مرورگرها اجرا می‌شود (صفحه‌ها را تعاملی می‌کند) و بیرون از\nآنها هم (Node.js برای سرورها، ابزارها و بیشتر). استانداردش\n<b>ECMAScript<\/b> (ECMA-262) است و هر سال قابلیت‌های تازه\nمی‌گیرد.<\/p>\n\n<p>این دوره کدهایت را در موتور خودِ مرورگر اجرا می‌کند — همان\nV8/SpiderMonkey که وب‌سایت‌های واقعی را می‌رانَد. Run را بزن و خروجیِ\nconsole را ببین.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Syntax & Comments","html":"\n<p>JS statements end with a semicolon (optional but recommended),\nblocks wrap in curly braces, and comments come in two flavours:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// single-line comment\n\n/* multi-line\n   comment */<\/pre>\n\n<p>JavaScript is <b>case-sensitive<\/b>: <code>myVar<\/code> and\n<code>myvar<\/code> are different variables. Statements execute top to\nbottom unless control flow redirects them. Whitespace is mostly\ninsignificant — but consistent indentation makes code readable.<\/p>\n\n<p>MDN's strict mode (<code>\"use strict\"<\/code>) opts into stricter\nparsing: it catches silent errors like assigning to undeclared\nvariables. Modern modules and classes are always in strict mode — you\nrarely need to type it manually anymore.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Case-sensitive!\nlet greeting = \"hello\";\nlet Greeting = \"HELLO\";\nconsole.log(greeting, Greeting);   // different variables!\n\n// Semicolons separate statements\nlet a = 1; let b = 2;\nconsole.log(a + b);\n\n/* Multi-line comment:\n   this whole block is ignored */\nconsole.log(\"done\");\n","title_fa":"نحو و کامنت‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p>جمله‌های JS با نقطه‌ویرگول تمام می‌شوند (اختیاری اما توصیه‌شده)،\nبلوک‌ها در آکولاد می‌پیچند و کامنت‌ها دو طعم دارند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// single-line comment\n\n/* multi-line\n   comment */<\/pre>\n\n<p>جاوااسکریپت <b>حساس به بزرگی حروف<\/b> است: <code>myVar<\/code> و\n<code>myvar<\/code> دو متغیر متفاوت‌اند. جمله‌ها از بالا به پایین اجرا\nمی‌شوند مگر اینکه کنترل جریان تغییرشان بدهد. فاصله‌ها عمدتاً بی‌معنا\nهستند — اما تورفتگیِ یکدست کد را خوانا می‌کند.<\/p>\n\n<p>حالت سخت‌گیرانه (strict mode) که MDN مستند کرده، پارسِ سخت‌گیرانه‌تری\nرا فعال می‌کند: خطاهای بی‌صدای مثل انتساب به متغیرِ اعلام‌نشده را\nمی‌گیرد. ماژول‌ها و کلاس‌های مدرن همیشه در strict mode هستند — دیگر\nبه‌ندرت لازم است دستی بنویسی‌اش.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Variables: let, const, var","html":"\n<p>Three keywords declare variables — and the differences matter:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const PI = 3.14159;    // cannot be reassigned\nlet count = 0;          // can be reassigned, block-scoped\nvar old = \"legacy\";     // function-scoped, hoisted — avoid in new code<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b><code>const<\/code><\/b> — the default choice. The binding can't be\nreassigned (though objects/arrays assigned to const can still be\n<i>mutated<\/i>)<\/li>\n<li><b><code>let<\/code><\/b> — when you know the value will change\n(counters, accumulators)<\/li>\n<li><b><code>var<\/code><\/b> — the legacy keyword; function-scoped and\nhoisted (accessible before its line!), which causes subtle bugs. Modern\ncode uses let/const exclusively<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = { name: \"Ada\" };\nuser.name = \"Grace\";     // ✓ mutation is fine — same object\n// user = {};            // ✗ TypeError: assignment to constant<\/pre>\n\n<p>Block scoping: <code>let<\/code>/<code>const<\/code> only exist inside\ntheir <code>{ }<\/code> block; <code>var<\/code> leaks to the function\nlevel. This is why <code>var<\/code> in loops caused bugs for\nyears.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const name = \"Ada\";\nlet score = 0;\n\nscore = score + 10;    // let CAN be reassigned\nconsole.log(`${name}: ${score}`);\n\n// const objects can be mutated (not reassigned)\nconst prefs = { theme: \"light\" };\nprefs.theme = \"dark\";    // ✓ fine\nconsole.log(\"theme:\", prefs.theme);\n\n// block scoping with let\nif (true) {\n  let inner = \"only visible inside this block\";\n  console.log(inner);\n}\n// console.log(inner);  // ← would throw ReferenceError!\n","title_fa":"متغیرها: let، const و var","html_fa":"\n<p>سه کلیدواژه متغیر اعلام می‌کنند — و تفاوت‌شان مهم است:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const PI = 3.14159;    // cannot be reassigned\nlet count = 0;          // can be reassigned, block-scoped\nvar old = \"legacy\";     // function-scoped, hoisted — avoid in new code<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b><code>const<\/code><\/b> — انتخابِ پیش‌فرض. پیوندش دوباره تعریف\nنمی‌شود (البته object/arrayهای منتسب‌شده به const هنوز قابل\n<i>تغییر<\/i>اند)<\/li>\n<li><b><code>let<\/code><\/b> — وقتی می‌دانی مقدار عوض می‌شود (شمارنده‌ها،\nانباشتگرها)<\/li>\n<li><b><code>var<\/code><\/b> — کلیدواژهٔ قدیمی؛ سطح-تابع و hoistشده\n(قبل از خطش قابل دسترس!) که باگ‌های ظریف می‌سازد. کد مدرن فقط\nlet/const<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = { name: \"Ada\" };\nuser.name = \"Grace\";     // ✓ mutation is fine — same object\n// user = {};            // ✗ TypeError: assignment to constant<\/pre>\n\n<p>سطحِ بلوک: <code>let<\/code>/<code>const<\/code> فقط داخل بلوکِ\n<code>{ }<\/code> خودشان وجود دارند؛ <code>var<\/code> تا سطح تابع\nنشت می‌کند. برای همین var در حلقه‌ها سال‌ها باگ\nساخت.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Data Types","html":"\n<p>JavaScript has <b>8 data types<\/b> — 7 primitives and 1 object\ntype:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Number<\/b> — integers and floats: <code>42<\/code>,\n<code>3.14<\/code>, <code>NaN<\/code>, <code>Infinity<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>String<\/b> — text: <code>\"hello\"<\/code>,\n<code>'world'<\/code>, <code>`template`<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Boolean<\/b> — <code>true<\/code> / <code>false<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>undefined<\/b> — a variable declared but not yet assigned<\/li>\n<li><b>null<\/b> — intentional absence of value<\/li>\n<li><b>BigInt<\/b> — arbitrary precision integers:\n<code>123n<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Symbol<\/b> — unique identifiers: <code>Symbol(\"id\")<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Object<\/b> — everything else: arrays, functions, dates... (the\nonly non-primitive type)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>The <code>typeof<\/code> operator reveals a value's type at runtime —\nwith one famous quirk: <code>typeof null<\/code> returns\n<code>\"object\"<\/code> (a bug from 1995 that can't be fixed without\nbreaking the web).<\/p>\n\n<p>JS is <b>dynamically typed<\/b>: variables have no fixed type — the\n<i>value<\/i> has the type. A variable can hold a number, then a string,\nthen an object. Flexibility with responsibility.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// typeof reveals the type of a VALUE\nconsole.log(typeof 42);           // \"number\"\nconsole.log(typeof \"hello\");      // \"string\"\nconsole.log(typeof true);         // \"boolean\"\nconsole.log(typeof undefined);    // \"undefined\"\nconsole.log(typeof null);         // \"object\" (the famous bug!)\nconsole.log(typeof Symbol());    // \"symbol\"\nconsole.log(typeof 123n);         // \"bigint\"\nconsole.log(typeof {});           // \"object\"\nconsole.log(typeof []);           // \"object\" (arrays are objects!)\nconsole.log(typeof function(){}); // \"function\"\n\n// Dynamic typing: same variable, different types\nlet x = 42;\nconsole.log(typeof x);    // \"number\"\nx = \"now a string\";\nconsole.log(typeof x);    // \"string\"\n","title_fa":"انواع داده","html_fa":"\n<p>جاوااسکریپت <b>۸ نوع داده<\/b> دارد — ۷ primitive و یک object:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Number<\/b> — اعداد صحیح و اعشاری: <code>42<\/code>،\n<code>3.14<\/code>، <code>NaN<\/code>، <code>Infinity<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>String<\/b> — متن: <code>\"hello\"<\/code>،\n<code>'world'<\/code>، <code>`template`<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Boolean<\/b> — <code>true<\/code> / <code>false<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>undefined<\/b> — متغیرِ اعلام‌شده اما هنوز مقدارنگرفته<\/li>\n<li><b>null<\/b> — نبودِ عمدیِ مقدار<\/li>\n<li><b>BigInt<\/b> — اعداد صحیح با دقت نامحدود: <code>123n<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Symbol<\/b> — شناسه‌های یکتا: <code>Symbol(\"id\")<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Object<\/b> — همهٔ بقیه: آرایه‌ها، توابع، تاریخ‌ها... (تنها نوع\nغیر-primitive)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>عملگر <code>typeof<\/code> نوعِ یک مقدار را در زمان اجرا لو می‌دهد —\nبا یک عارضهٔ معروف: <code>typeof null<\/code> مقدار\n<code>\"object\"<\/code> برمی‌گرداند (باگی از ۱۹۹۵ که بدون شکستنِ وب\nنمی‌شود درستش کرد).<\/p>\n\n<p>JS <b>پویاتایپ<\/b> است: متغیرها نوعِ ثابت ندارند — <i>مقدار<\/i>\nنوع دارد. یک متغیر می‌تواند اول عدد بگیرد، بعد رشته، بعد شیء.\nانعطاف با مسئولیت.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Numbers & Strings","html":"\n<p><b>Numbers<\/b> are 64-bit floating point (there's no separate int\ntype). Special values: <code>NaN<\/code> (\"Not a Number\" — the result of\ninvalid math), <code>Infinity<\/code>, <code>-Infinity<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">42 + 1        // 43\n3.14 * 2      // 6.28\n10 / 3        // 3.3333...\n10 / 0        // Infinity\n0 / 0         // NaN\nparseInt(\"42\")  // 42\nparseFloat(\"3.14\")  // 3.14\n(42.5678).toFixed(2)  // \"42.57\"<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Strings<\/b> are sequences of characters, immutable (methods\nreturn new strings). Key methods:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">\"hello\".length          // 5\n\"hello\".toUpperCase()   // \"HELLO\"\n\"hello\".slice(1, 3)     // \"el\"\n\"a,b,c\".split(\",\")      // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n\"  hi  \".trim()         // \"hi\"\n\"abc\".includes(\"b\")     // true\n\"abc\".replace(\"a\", \"X\") // \"Xbc\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>Numbers and strings convert: <code>String(42) → \"42\"<\/code>,\n<code>Number(\"42\") → 42<\/code>, <code>+\"42\" → 42<\/code>. But\n<code>Number(\"abc\") → NaN<\/code> — always check!<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Numbers\nconsole.log(10 / 3);            // division\nconsole.log(10 % 3);            // remainder\nconsole.log(2 ** 10);           // exponent: 1024\nconsole.log(0.1 + 0.2);         // 0.30000000000000004 (floating point!)\nconsole.log((0.1 + 0.2).toFixed(2)); // \"0.30\"\nconsole.log(parseInt(\"42abc\")); // 42 (parses the leading number)\nconsole.log(NaN === NaN);       // false — NaN is never equal to itself!\n\n// Strings\nconst s = \"JavaScript\";\nconsole.log(s.length);          // 10\nconsole.log(s.toUpperCase());   // \"JAVASCRIPT\"\nconsole.log(s.slice(0, 4));     // \"Java\"\nconsole.log(s.includes(\"Script\")); // true\nconsole.log(s.replace(\"Java\", \"Type\")); // \"TypeScript\"\nconsole.log(\"a,b,c\".split(\",\"));  // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n","title_fa":"اعداد و رشته‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>اعداد<\/b> اعشاریِ ۶۴ بیتی‌اند (نوعِ صحیحِ جداگانه‌ای نیست).\nمقادیر ویژه: <code>NaN<\/code> («عدد نیست» — نتیجهٔ ریاضیِ نامعتبر)،\n<code>Infinity<\/code> و <code>-Infinity<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">42 + 1        // 43\n3.14 * 2      // 6.28\n10 / 3        // 3.3333...\n10 / 0        // Infinity\n0 / 0         // NaN\nparseInt(\"42\")  // 42\nparseFloat(\"3.14\")  // 3.14\n(42.5678).toFixed(2)  // \"42.57\"<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>رشته‌ها<\/b> دنباله‌ای از نویسه‌ها هستند، تغییرناپذیر (متدها\nرشتهٔ جدید برمی‌گردانند). متدهای کلیدی:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">\"hello\".length          // 5\n\"hello\".toUpperCase()   // \"HELLO\"\n\"hello\".slice(1, 3)     // \"el\"\n\"a,b,c\".split(\",\")      // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n\"  hi  \".trim()         // \"hi\"\n\"abc\".includes(\"b\")     // true\n\"abc\".replace(\"a\", \"X\") // \"Xbc\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>اعداد و رشته‌ها تبدیل می‌شوند: <code>String(42) → \"42\"<\/code>،\n<code>Number(\"42\") → 42<\/code>. اما <code>Number(\"abc\") → NaN<\/code> —\nهمیشه چک کن!<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Booleans, null & undefined","html":"\n<p><b>Booleans<\/b> are <code>true<\/code> and <code>false<\/code> — but\nJS also has <b>truthy<\/b> and <b>falsy<\/b> values that coerce to\nbooleans in conditions:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Falsy (6 total):<\/b> <code>false<\/code>, <code>0<\/code>,\n<code>\"\"<\/code>, <code>null<\/code>, <code>undefined<\/code>,\n<code>NaN<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Truthy:<\/b> everything else — including <code>\"0\"<\/code>,\n<code>[]<\/code>, <code>{}<\/code>, <code>\" \"<\/code> (space!)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p><b>null vs undefined<\/b> — the two \"absence\" values:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>undefined<\/code> — a variable declared but not assigned; a\nfunction that doesn't return; an object property that doesn't exist.\nJS's way of saying \"not set yet\"<\/li>\n<li><code>null<\/code> — <i>you<\/i> set it, intentionally, to mean \"no\nvalue\". It's a deliberate assignment<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">let a;           // undefined\nlet b = null;    // null (intentional)\n\nconsole.log(a == b);    // true (loose: both \"empty\")\nconsole.log(a === b);   // false (strict: different types!)<\/pre>\n\n<p>The <code>!!<\/code> double-negation converts any value to its boolean\nequivalent — a common idiom: <code>!!\"hello\" → true<\/code>,\n<code>!!0 → false<\/code>.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Falsy values (all 6)\nconsole.log(!!false);     // false\nconsole.log(!!0);         // false\nconsole.log(!!\"\");        // false\nconsole.log(!!null);      // false\nconsole.log(!!undefined); // false\nconsole.log(!!NaN);       // false\n\n// Truthy surprises\nconsole.log(!!\"0\");       // true (non-empty string!)\nconsole.log(!![]);        // true (empty array is truthy!)\nconsole.log(!!{});        // true (empty object is truthy!)\n\n// null vs undefined\nlet a;\nlet b = null;\nconsole.log(a, b);        // undefined null\nconsole.log(typeof a);   // \"undefined\"\nconsole.log(typeof b);   // \"object\" (the bug)\nconsole.log(a == b);     // true (loose)\nconsole.log(a === b);    // false (strict)\n","title_fa":"بولی‌ها، null و undefined","html_fa":"\n<p><b>بولی‌ها<\/b> <code>true<\/code> و <code>false<\/code> هستند — اما JS\nهمچنین مقادیر <b>truthy<\/b> و <b>falsy<\/b> دارد که در شرط‌ها به بولی\nتبدیل می‌شوند:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>falsy (جمعاً ۶ تا):<\/b> <code>false<\/code>، <code>0<\/code>،\n<code>\"\"<\/code>، <code>null<\/code>، <code>undefined<\/code>،\n<code>NaN<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>truthy:<\/b> همهٔ بقیه — شامل <code>\"0\"<\/code>،\n<code>[]<\/code>، <code>{}<\/code> و <code>\" \"<\/code> (فاصله!)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p><b>null در برابر undefined<\/b> — دو مقدارِ «نبود»:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>undefined<\/code> — متغیرِ اعلام‌شده بدون مقدار؛ تابعی که\nبرنمی‌گرداند؛ ویژگیِ شیء که وجود ندارد. راهِ JS برای گفتنِ «هنوز ست\nنشده»<\/li>\n<li><code>null<\/code> — <i>خودت<\/i> عمداً ستش کرده‌ای تا بگویی «مقدار\nندارد». انتسابی آگاهانه<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">let a;           // undefined\nlet b = null;    // null (intentional)\n\nconsole.log(a == b);    // true (loose: both \"empty\")\nconsole.log(a === b);   // false (strict: different types!)<\/pre>\n\n<p>دو بار نقیض (<code>!!<\/code>) هر مقداری را به معادل بولی‌اش تبدیل\nمی‌کند — اصطلاحی رایج: <code>!!\"hello\" → true<\/code>،\n<code>!!0 → false<\/code>.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Type Conversion","html":"\n<p>JS converts types <i>all the time<\/i> — sometimes when you don't\nexpect it. <b>Explicit<\/b> conversion is when you call the conversion\nyourself; <b>implicit<\/b> (coercion) is when JS does it behind your\nback:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// explicit\nNumber(\"42\")       // 42\nString(42)         // \"42\"\nBoolean(1)         // true\n(42).toString()    // \"42\"\nparseInt(\"3.14\")   // 3 (integer part)\n\n// implicit coercion — the tricky ones!\n\"5\" + 3      // \"53\"   (number → string, concatenation)\n\"5\" - 3      // 2      (string → number, subtraction)\n\"5\" * \"2\"    // 10     (both → numbers)\n1 + true     // 2      (true → 1)\n[] + []      // \"\"     (both → \"\", concatenated)\n[] + {}      // \"[object Object]\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>The <code>+<\/code> operator is unique: it prefers string\nconcatenation if either operand is a string. Every other math operator\ncoerces to number. This asymmetry causes real bugs:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// form inputs are always strings!\nconst val = \"10\";\nval + 5     // \"105\" — concatenation, not addition!\nNumber(val) + 5  // 15 — convert first!<\/pre>\n\n<p>Modern operators avoid coercion: <code>===<\/code> (strict equality),\n<code>??<\/code> (nullish coalescing), and\n<code>Object.is()<\/code> never surprise you.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Explicit conversion\nconsole.log(Number(\"42\"));      // 42\nconsole.log(String(42));        // \"42\"\nconsole.log(Boolean(0));        // false\nconsole.log(parseInt(\"3.14\")); // 3\nconsole.log(parseFloat(\"3.14\")); // 3.14\n\n// Implicit coercion — the weird ones\nconsole.log(\"5\" + 3);     // \"53\" (string concat)\nconsole.log(\"5\" - 3);     // 2 (number subtract)\nconsole.log(\"5\" * \"2\");   // 10\nconsole.log(1 + true);   // 2\nconsole.log([] + []);    // \"\" (empty string!)\n\n// The form-input gotcha\nconst input = \"10\";  // like reading from an <input>\nconsole.log(input + 5);        // \"105\" — NOT 15!\nconsole.log(Number(input) + 5); // 15 — convert first!\n","title_fa":"تبدیل نوع","html_fa":"\n<p>JS مدام نوع‌ها را تبدیل می‌کند — گاهی وقتی انتظارش را نداری.\nتبدیل <b>صریح<\/b> یعنی خودت تابع تبدیل را صدا بزنی؛ <b>ضمنی<\/b>\n(coercion) یعنی JS پشت‌پشت انجامش بدهد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// explicit\nNumber(\"42\")       // 42\nString(42)         // \"42\"\nBoolean(1)         // true\n(42).toString()    // \"42\"\nparseInt(\"3.14\")   // 3 (integer part)\n\n// implicit coercion — the tricky ones!\n\"5\" + 3      // \"53\"   (number → string, concatenation)\n\"5\" - 3      // 2      (string → number, subtraction)\n\"5\" * \"2\"    // 10     (both → numbers)\n1 + true     // 2      (true → 1)\n[] + []      // \"\"     (both → \"\", concatenated)\n[] + {}      // \"[object Object]\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>عملگر <code>+<\/code> یکتاست: اگر یکی از طرف‌ها رشته باشد، الحاقِ\nرشته‌ای را ترجیح می‌دهد. هر عملگر ریاضیِ دیگری به عدد تبدیل می‌کند.\nاین عدم‌تقارن باگ واقعی می‌سازد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// form inputs are always strings!\nconst val = \"10\";\nval + 5     // \"105\" — concatenation, not addition!\nNumber(val) + 5  // 15 — convert first!<\/pre>\n\n<p>عملگرهای مدرن از coercion می‌گریزند: <code>===<\/code> (برابری\nسخت‌گیرانه)، <code>??<\/code> (الحاقِ هیچ‌گرا) و\n<code>Object.is()<\/code> هرگز غافلگیرت نمی‌کنند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Operators & Comparisons","html":"\n<p>JS operators, grouped by purpose:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Arithmetic:<\/b> <code>+ - * / % **<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Assignment:<\/b> <code>= += -= *= /= %= **= &amp;&amp;= ||= ??=<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Comparison:<\/b> <code>&gt; &lt; &gt;= &lt;=<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Equality:<\/b> <code>==<\/code> (loose), <code>===<\/code>\n(strict), <code>!=<\/code>, <code>!==<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Logical:<\/b> <code>&amp;&amp;<\/code> (AND), <code>||<\/code>\n(OR), <code>!<\/code> (NOT), <code>??<\/code> (nullish)<\/li>\n<li><b>Ternary:<\/b> <code>condition ? a : b<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Optional chaining:<\/b> <code>obj?.prop<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Increment/Decrement:<\/b> <code>++i<\/code>, <code>i--<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>The logical operators are <i>short-circuiting<\/i>: they return the\nvalue that decides the result, not just true/false. This enables\npowerful patterns:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">name = name || \"Anonymous\";   // default value (old style)\nname = name ?? \"Anonymous\";   // default (only for null/undefined, not 0 or \"\")\n\nisReady && start();            // only call if isReady is truthy\nvalue = mayBeNull?.property;   // no crash if mayBeNull is null<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>==<\/code> vs <code>===<\/code> deserves its own lesson (next!),\nbut the rule is simple: <b>always use ===<\/b>. The loose ==\nperforms type coercion that produces surprising results.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Short-circuit evaluation\nconst name = \"\" || \"Anonymous\";     // \"\" is falsy → \"Anonymous\"\nconsole.log(name);\n\nconst count = 0 ?? 99;              // 0 is NOT null/undefined → stays 0\nconsole.log(count);\n\nconst user = { profile: { email: \"ada@x.io\" } };\nconsole.log(user?.profile?.email);  // \"ada@x.io\"\nconsole.log(user?.missing?.deep);   // undefined (no crash!)\n\n// Ternary\nconst age = 20;\nconst status = age >= 18 ? \"adult\" : \"minor\";\nconsole.log(status);\n\n// Chained assignment operators\nlet n = 10;\nn += 5;   // 15\nn *= 2;   // 30\nn -= 5;   // 25\nconsole.log(n);\n","title_fa":"عملگرها و مقایسه‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p>عملگرهای JS، گروه‌بندی‌شده بر اساس هدف:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>حسابی:<\/b> <code>+ - * / % **<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>انتساب:<\/b> <code>= += -= *= /= %= **= &amp;&amp;= ||= ??=<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>مقایسه:<\/b> <code>&gt; &lt; &gt;= &lt;=<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>برابری:<\/b> <code>==<\/code> (شل)، <code>===<\/code>\n(سخت‌گیرانه)، <code>!=<\/code>، <code>!==<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>منطقی:<\/b> <code>&amp;&amp;<\/code> (و)، <code>||<\/code> (یا)،\n<code>!<\/code> (نقیض)، <code>??<\/code> (نیش‌دار)<\/li>\n<li><b>سه‌تایی:<\/b> <code>condition ? a : b<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>زنجیرهٔ اختیاری:<\/b> <code>obj?.prop<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>افزایش/کاهش:<\/b> <code>++i<\/code>، <code>i--<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>عملگرهای منطقی <i>مدارِ کوتاه<\/i> دارند: مقداری را برمی‌گردانند که\nنتیجه را تعیین می‌کند، نه فقط true/false. همین، الگوهای قدرتمند\nمی‌سازد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">name = name || \"Anonymous\";   // default value (old style)\nname = name ?? \"Anonymous\";   // default (only for null/undefined, not 0 or \"\")\n\nisReady && start();            // only call if isReady is truthy\nvalue = mayBeNull?.property;   // no crash if mayBeNull is null<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>==<\/code> در برابر <code>===<\/code> درسِ خودش را می‌خواهد — اما\nقاعده ساده است: <b>همیشه ===<\/b>. == شل، coercion می‌کند و نتیجه‌های\nغافلگیرکننده می‌دهد.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Equality: == vs ===","html":"\n<p>The single most important distinction for JS beginners:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>==<\/code> (loose equality) — converts both sides to the same\ntype, <i>then<\/i> compares. Convenient but full of traps<\/li>\n<li><code>===<\/code> (strict equality) — compares value AND type. No\nconversion. Always predictable<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">1 == \"1\"      // true  (string → number)\n1 === \"1\"     // false (different types!)\n\nnull == undefined   // true\nnull === undefined  // false\n\nNaN == NaN     // false (NaN never equals itself!)\nNaN === NaN    // false\n\n0 == false     // true\n0 === false    // false<\/pre>\n\n<p>The rules for <code>==<\/code> are so complex that MDN recommends\n<b>never using it<\/b>. The only valid use case:\n<code>x == null<\/code> checks for both null AND undefined at\nonce.<\/p>\n\n<p><code>Object.is()<\/code> is a third comparison that's like\n<code>===<\/code> but treats <code>NaN === NaN<\/code> as true and\n<code>+0 !== -0<\/code>. It's what <code>Object.is()<\/code> is\nfor.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// The traps of ==\nconsole.log(1 == \"1\");          // true (coerced!)\nconsole.log(0 == \"\");           // true (\"\" → 0)\nconsole.log(null == undefined); // true\nconsole.log([] == false);       // true ([] → \"\" → 0!)\n\n// === is always predictable\nconsole.log(1 === \"1\");         // false\nconsole.log(0 === \"\");          // false\nconsole.log(null === undefined);// false\n\n// Object.is — edge cases\nconsole.log(Object.is(NaN, NaN));     // true (!)\nconsole.log(NaN === NaN);             // false\nconsole.log(Object.is(0, -0));       // false\nconsole.log(0 === -0);               // true\n\n// The ONE valid use of ==\nconst x = null;\nconsole.log(x == null);     // true — checks null OR undefined\nconsole.log(x === null);    // true — but only null\nconsole.log(x === undefined); // false\n","title_fa":"برابری: == در برابر ===","html_fa":"\n<p>مهم‌ترین تمایز برای تازه‌کارهای JS:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>==<\/code> (برابری شل) — هر دو طرف را به یک نوع تبدیل می‌کند،\n<i>بعد<\/i> مقایسه. راحت اما پر از تله<\/li>\n<li><code>===<\/code> (برابری سخت‌گیرانه) — مقدار و نوع را مقایسه می‌کند.\nبدون تبدیل. همیشه قابل پیش‌بینی<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">1 == \"1\"      // true  (string → number)\n1 === \"1\"     // false (different types!)\n\nnull == undefined   // true\nnull === undefined  // false\n\nNaN == NaN     // false (NaN never equals itself!)\nNaN === NaN    // false\n\n0 == false     // true\n0 === false    // false<\/pre>\n\n<p>قواعد <code>==<\/code> آن‌قدر پیچیده‌اند که MDN توصیه می‌کند\n<b>هرگز استفاده‌اش نکنی<\/b>. تنها موردِ معتبر: <code>x == null<\/code>\nکه هم null و هم undefined را یک‌جا چک می‌کند.<\/p>\n\n<p><code>Object.is()<\/code> مقایسهٔ سومی است که مثل\n<code>===<\/code> است اما <code>NaN === NaN<\/code> را true می‌داند و\n<code>+0 !== -0<\/code>. برای همین وجود دارد.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Template Literals","html":"\n<p>Template literals use <b>backticks<\/b> (<code>`<\/code>) instead of\nquotes and unlock three superpowers that regular strings don't\nhave:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Interpolation:<\/b> embed any expression with\n<code>${expression}<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>Multi-line<\/b>: line breaks are preserved, no <code>\\n<\/code>\nneeded<\/li>\n<li><b>Tagged templates<\/b>: functions can process the template (how\nstyled-components works)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const name = \"Ada\";\nconst score = 95;\n\n// interpolation — no more string concatenation!\nconsole.log(`${name} scored ${score}%`);\nconsole.log(`Next year: ${score + 5}%`);\n\n// multi-line — natural formatting\nconst html = `\n  &lt;div class=\"card\"&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;${name}&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Score: ${score}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n`;\n\n// expressions inside ${}\nconsole.log(`Double: ${score * 2}`);\nconsole.log(`Upper: ${name.toUpperCase()}`);\nconsole.log(`Conditional: ${score >= 90 ? \"pass\" : \"fail\"}`);<\/pre>\n\n<p>Any expression works inside <code>${}<\/code> — function calls,\nternaries, even nested template literals. This is the modern way to\nbuild strings; string concatenation with <code>+<\/code> is\nlegacy.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const name = \"Ada\";\nconst items = [\"sword\", \"shield\", \"potion\"];\nconst gold = 150;\n\n// Interpolation\nconsole.log(`${name} has ${gold} gold and ${items.length} items.`);\n\n// Multi-line HTML\nconst html = `\n  <div class=\"inventory\">\n    <h3>${name}'s Bag<\/h3>\n    <ul>\n      ${items.map(i => `<li>${i}<\/li>`).join(\"\\n\")}\n    <\/ul>\n    <p>Gold: ${gold >= 100 ? \"rich 💰\" : \"broke 😅\"}<\/p>\n  <\/div>\n`;\nconsole.log(html);\n\n// Expressions inside ${}\nconsole.log(`${items[0].toUpperCase()} costs ${Math.round(gold / 3)}g`);\n","title_fa":"قالب‌های متنی (Template Literals)","html_fa":"\n<p>قالب‌های متنی با <b>بک‌تیک<\/b> (<code>`<\/code>) نوشته می‌شوند و سه\nابرقودگی دارند که رشته‌های معمولی ندارند:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>درون‌یابی:<\/b> هر عبارتی را با <code>${expression}<\/code> جاسازی\nکن<\/li>\n<li><b>چندخطی:<\/b> شکست خط‌ها حفظ می‌شوند، بدون <code>\\n<\/code><\/li>\n<li><b>قالب‌های برچسب‌خورده:<\/b> توابع می‌توانند قالب را پردازش کنند\n(همین‌طور styled-components کار می‌کند)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const name = \"Ada\";\nconst score = 95;\n\n// interpolation — no more string concatenation!\nconsole.log(`${name} scored ${score}%`);\nconsole.log(`Next year: ${score + 5}%`);\n\n// multi-line — natural formatting\nconst html = `\n  &lt;div class=\"card\"&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;${name}&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Score: ${score}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n`;\n\n// expressions inside ${}\nconsole.log(`Double: ${score * 2}`);\nconsole.log(`Upper: ${name.toUpperCase()}`);\nconsole.log(`Conditional: ${score >= 90 ? \"pass\" : \"fail\"}`);<\/pre>\n\n<p>هر عبارتی داخل <code>${}<\/code> کار می‌کند — فراخوانی تابع، سه‌تایی،\nحتی قالبِ متنیِ تودرتو. این راهِ مدرنِ ساختِ رشته است؛ الحاق با\n<code>+<\/code> مالِ دورانِ قدیم است.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"Which keyword declares a variable that CANNOT be reassigned?","options":["let","var","const","static"],"answer":2,"explain":"const = constant binding. Objects assigned to const can still be mutated.","fa":{"question":"کدام کلیدواژه متغیری اعلام می‌کند که قابل انتسابِ مجدد نیست؟","options":["let","var","const","static"],"explain":"const = پیوندِ ثابت. شیءهای منتسب‌شده به const هنوز قابل تغییرند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"What does <code>typeof null<\/code> return?","options":["\"null\"","\"undefined\"","\"object\"","\"boolean\""],"answer":2,"explain":"typeof null returns \"object\" — a famous bug from 1995 that can't be fixed.","fa":{"question":"<code>typeof null<\/code> چه برمی‌گرداند؟","options":["\"null\"","\"undefined\"","\"object\"","\"boolean\""],"explain":"typeof null مقدار \"object\" می‌دهد — باگِ معروفِ ۱۹۹۵."}},{"type":"blank","question":"The template literal syntax for embedding an expression is <code>____<\/code>.","answers":["${}","${ }","${expression}"],"explain":"${} embeds any expression inside backtick strings.","fa":{"question":"نحوِ جاسازی عبارت در قالب متنی <code>____<\/code> است.","explain":"${} هر عبارتی را داخل رشتهٔ بک‌تیکی جاسازی می‌کند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"How many falsy values does JavaScript have?","options":["2","4","6","8"],"answer":2,"explain":"false, 0, \"\", null, undefined, NaN — exactly 6.","fa":{"question":"جاوااسکریپت چند مقدار falsy دارد؟","options":["۲","۴","۶","۸"],"explain":"false، 0، \"\"، null، undefined و NaN — دقیقاً ۶ تا."}},{"type":"mc","question":"What does <code>\"5\" + 3<\/code> evaluate to?","options":["8","\"53\"","NaN","Error"],"answer":1,"explain":"+ prefers string concatenation when either operand is a string.","fa":{"question":"حاصل <code>\"5\" + 3<\/code> چیست؟","options":["8","\"53\"","NaN","خطا"],"explain":"+ وقتی یکی از طرف‌ها رشته باشد الحاق را ترجیح می‌دهد."}},{"type":"mc","question":"The ONLY recommended use of == is:","options":["Comparing numbers","x == null (checks both null and undefined)","Comparing strings","Never — always use ==="],"answer":1,"explain":"x == null checks for both null and undefined in one expression.","fa":{"question":"تنها کاربردِ توصیه‌شدهٔ == این است:","options":["مقایسهٔ اعداد","x == null (هم null هم undefined را چک می‌کند)","مقایسهٔ رشته‌ها","هرگز — همیشه ==="],"explain":"x == null در یک عبارت هم null و هم undefined را می‌آزماید."}}],"title_fa":"مبانی"},{"id":"js02","title":"Control Flow","emoji":"🔀","lessons":[{"title":"if / else","html":"\n<p>The fundamental branching statement — run code only when a condition\nis truthy:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">if (temperature &gt; 30) {\n  console.log(\"hot\");\n} else if (temperature &gt; 20) {\n  console.log(\"nice\");\n} else {\n  console.log(\"cold\");\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>Conditions coerce to boolean — falsy values (0, \"\", null,\nundefined, NaN) are treated as <code>false<\/code>. Curly braces are\ntechnically optional for single statements, but always use them —\nomitting them causes real bugs. For simple conditionals, the ternary\noperator <code>condition ? a : b<\/code> is often cleaner.<\/p>\n\n<p>MDN also documents <code>if...else if...else<\/code> chains (which are\nreally nested ifs) — keep them shallow; deeply nested conditionals are\na code smell that early returns or lookup tables can fix.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const hour = 14;\n\nif (hour < 12) {\n  console.log(\"Good morning\");\n} else if (hour < 18) {\n  console.log(\"Good afternoon\");\n} else {\n  console.log(\"Good evening\");\n}\n\n// Falsy values in conditions\nconst name = \"\";   // empty string = falsy\nif (name) {\n  console.log(\"Hello,\", name);\n} else {\n  console.log(\"No name given\");\n}\n\n// Ternary for simple cases\nconst label = hour < 12 ? \"AM\" : \"PM\";\nconsole.log(label);\n","title_fa":"if / else","html_fa":"\n<p>جملهٔ بنیادیِ انشعاب — کد فقط وقتی اجرا شود که شرط truthy\nباشد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">if (temperature &gt; 30) {\n  console.log(\"hot\");\n} else if (temperature &gt; 20) {\n  console.log(\"nice\");\n} else {\n  console.log(\"cold\");\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>شرط‌ها به بولی تبدیل می‌شوند — مقادیر falsy (یعنی 0، \"\"، null،\nundefined و NaN) مثل <code>false<\/code> رفتار می‌کنند. آکولادها فنی‌اً\nبرای جمله‌های تک‌خطی اختیاری‌اند اما همیشه بگذارشان — جا انداختنشان\nباگ واقعی می‌سازد. برای شرط‌های ساده، عملگر سه‌تایی\n<code>condition ? a : b<\/code> اغلب تمیزتر است.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"switch","html":"\n<p><code>switch<\/code> compares a value against multiple cases —\ncleaner than long if-else chains:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">switch (fruit) {\n  case \"apple\":\n    console.log(\"red or green\");\n    break;                    // REQUIRED — prevents fall-through!\n  case \"banana\":\n  case \"plantain\":            // multiple cases, same body\n    console.log(\"yellow\");\n    break;\n  default:\n    console.log(\"unknown fruit\");\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>The <b>break<\/b> keyword exits the switch. Without it, execution\n<b>falls through<\/b> to the next case — sometimes useful\n(intentional fall-through for grouping), often a bug. The\n<b>default<\/b> case handles unmatched values.<\/p>\n\n<p>Important: switch uses <b>strict comparison<\/b> (===) —\n<code>switch(\"1\")<\/code> will NOT match <code>case 1:<\/code>. This\ncatches people off guard when working with form inputs.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const day = \"sat\";\n\nswitch (day.toLowerCase()) {\n  case \"sat\":\n  case \"sun\":\n    console.log(\"Weekend! 🎉\");\n    break;\n  case \"mon\":\n  case \"tue\":\n  case \"wed\":\n  case \"thu\":\n    console.log(\"Weekday\");\n    break;\n  case \"fri\":\n    console.log(\"Almost weekend!\");\n    break;\n  default:\n    console.log(\"Not a day:\", day);\n}\n\n// switch uses === (strict)\nconst num = \"1\";\nswitch (num) {\n  case 1:\n    console.log(\"number 1\");     // NOT reached — num is a string!\n    break;\n  case \"1\":\n    console.log(\"string \\\"1\\\"\");  // THIS matches\n    break;\n}\n","title_fa":"switch","html_fa":"\n<p><code>switch<\/code> یک مقدار را با چند case مقایسه می‌کند — تمیزتر\nاز زنجیره‌های بلند if-else:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">switch (fruit) {\n  case \"apple\":\n    console.log(\"red or green\");\n    break;                    // REQUIRED — prevents fall-through!\n  case \"banana\":\n  case \"plantain\":            // multiple cases, same body\n    console.log(\"yellow\");\n    break;\n  default:\n    console.log(\"unknown fruit\");\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>کلیدواژهٔ <b>break<\/b> از switch بیرون می‌آید. بدون آن، اجرا به\ncase بعدی <b>سقوط می‌کند<\/b> — گاهی مفید (سقوطِ عمدی برای گروه‌کردن)،\nاغلب باگ. case <b>default<\/b> مقدارهای بدون تطبیق را\nمی‌گیرد.<\/p>\n\n<p>مهم: switch از <b>مقایسهٔ سخت‌گیرانه<\/b> (===) استفاده می‌کند —\n<code>switch(\"1\")<\/code> با <code>case 1:<\/code> تطبیق <b>نمی‌کند<\/b>.\nوقتی با ورودی فرم‌ها کار می‌کنی غافلگیرت می‌کند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"while & do...while","html":"\n<p>Two loops that repeat while a condition is true:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// while: check condition FIRST (may run 0 times)\nlet count = 0;\nwhile (count &lt; 5) {\n  console.log(count);\n  count++;         // don't forget! Otherwise: infinite loop\n}\n\n// do...while: run body FIRST, then check (always runs ≥ 1 time)\nlet input;\ndo {\n  input = getNextGuess();\n} while (input !== \"correct\");<\/pre>\n\n<p>The critical difference: <code>while<\/code> checks before the first\niteration; <code>do...while<\/code> checks after — so do...while always\nexecutes at least once. Use <code>while<\/code> for \"repeat as long as\"\nand <code>do...while<\/code> for \"do at least once, then repeat\nif\".<\/p>\n\n<p>Infinite loops are the classic mistake — always ensure something in\nthe body moves toward the exit condition. The playground has a step\nlimit to protect you.<\/p>\n","tryit":"let countdown = 5;\nwhile (countdown > 0) {\n  console.log(\"T-minus\", countdown);\n  countdown--;\n}\nconsole.log(\"Liftoff! 🚀\");\n\n// do...while runs at least once, even if condition is false\nlet n = 100;\ndo {\n  console.log(\"runs once even though 100 > 10 is true\");\n  n++;\n} while (n < 10);  // false after first iteration\n\n// while with arrays\nconst stack = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"];\nwhile (stack.length > 0) {\n  console.log(\"popped:\", stack.pop());\n}\n","title_fa":"while و do...while","html_fa":"\n<p>دو حلقه که تا وقتی شرط true است تکرار می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// while: check condition FIRST (may run 0 times)\nlet count = 0;\nwhile (count &lt; 5) {\n  console.log(count);\n  count++;         // don't forget! Otherwise: infinite loop\n}\n\n// do...while: run body FIRST, then check (always runs ≥ 1 time)\nlet input;\ndo {\n  input = getNextGuess();\n} while (input !== \"correct\");<\/pre>\n\n<p>تفاوت حیاتی: <code>while<\/code> قبل از اولین تکرار شرط را چک\nمی‌کند؛ <code>do...while<\/code> بعدش — پس do...while همیشه دست‌کم یک\nبار اجرا می‌شود. <code>while<\/code> برای «تا وقتی که» و\n<code>do...while<\/code> برای «دست‌کم یک بار برو، بعد اگر شرط بود تکرار\nکن».<\/p>\n\n<p>حلقهٔ بی‌نهایت، اشتباهِ کلاسیک است — همیشه مطمئن شو چیزی در بدنه\nبه سمت شرطِ خروج حرکت می‌کند. playground برای محافظت از تو سقفِ گام\nدارد.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"for & for...of","html":"\n<p>The classic <code>for<\/code> loop and the modern\n<code>for...of<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// classic for: full control over the counter\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {\n  console.log(i);           // 0 1 2 3 4\n}\n\n// for...of: iterate VALUES of any iterable (arrays, strings, Maps...)\nconst fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];\nfor (const fruit of fruits) {\n  console.log(fruit);\n}\n\n// for...of with strings (iterates characters)\nfor (const ch of \"JS\") {\n  console.log(ch);          // \"J\" \"S\"\n}\n\n// for...of with entries() to get index + value\nfor (const [index, fruit] of fruits.entries()) {\n  console.log(index, fruit);\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>for...of is the modern way<\/b> to iterate arrays — no counter to\nmanage, no off-by-one errors. Use the classic <code>for<\/code> when you\nneed the index or need to skip/modify the counter. Use\n<code>for...of<\/code> when you just need each value.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Classic for: full control\nfor (let i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {\n  console.log(\"i =\", i);\n}\n\n// Nested for: multiplication table\nfor (let row = 1; row <= 3; row++) {\n  let line = \"\";\n  for (let col = 1; col <= 3; col++) {\n    line += (row * col).toString().padStart(3) + \" \";\n  }\n  console.log(line);\n}\n\n// for...of: the modern way\nconst langs = [\"JS\", \"Python\", \"C\"];\nfor (const lang of langs) {\n  console.log(`I'm learning ${lang}`);\n}\n\n// for...of with entries for index+value\nfor (const [i, lang] of langs.entries()) {\n  console.log(`${i + 1}. ${lang}`);\n}\n","title_fa":"for و for...of","html_fa":"\n<p>حلقهٔ کلاسیک <code>for<\/code> و <code>for...of<\/code>\nمدرن:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// classic for: full control over the counter\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {\n  console.log(i);           // 0 1 2 3 4\n}\n\n// for...of: iterate VALUES of any iterable (arrays, strings, Maps...)\nconst fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];\nfor (const fruit of fruits) {\n  console.log(fruit);\n}\n\n// for...of with strings (iterates characters)\nfor (const ch of \"JS\") {\n  console.log(ch);          // \"J\" \"S\"\n}\n\n// for...of with entries() to get index + value\nfor (const [index, fruit] of fruits.entries()) {\n  console.log(index, fruit);\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>for...of راه مدرن<\/b> تکرارِ آرایه‌هاست — نه شمارنده‌ای برای\nمدیریت، نه خطای مرزی. از for کلاسیک وقتی استفاده کن که اندیس می‌خواهی\nیا باید شمارنده را بپَری/تغییر بدهی. از <code>for...of<\/code> وقتی فقط\nمقدارِ هر عنصر را می‌خواهی.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"for...in","html":"\n<p><code>for...in<\/code> iterates over the <b>keys<\/b> (property names)\nof an object:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = { name: \"Ada\", age: 36, role: \"admin\" };\n\nfor (const key in user) {\n  console.log(key, user[key]);    // \"name\" \"Ada\", \"age\" 36, ...\n}\n\n// with Object.keys() — often preferred\nfor (const key of Object.keys(user)) {\n  console.log(key);\n}\n\n// Object.entries() for key+value pairs\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(user)) {\n  console.log(`${key}: ${value}`);\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>Important: <b>don't use for...in on arrays<\/b> — it iterates string\nindices (\"0\", \"1\"...) and may include inherited properties. Use\n<code>for...of<\/code> or array methods (<code>forEach<\/code>,\n<code>map<\/code>) instead. for...in is for <b>objects<\/b>.<\/p>\n\n<p>The modern preference is <code>Object.keys()<\/code>,\n<code>Object.values()<\/code>, or <code>Object.entries()<\/code> — they\nreturn real arrays you can use with map/filter/reduce.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const scores = { math: 95, science: 88, art: 92 };\n\n// for...in iterates keys\nfor (const subject in scores) {\n  console.log(`${subject}: ${scores[subject]}`);\n}\n\n// Object.entries() — the modern way\nfor (const [subject, score] of Object.entries(scores)) {\n  console.log(`${subject}: ${score >= 90 ? \"✓\" : \"✗\"} ${score}`);\n}\n\n// Object.keys() and Object.values()\nconsole.log(\"subjects:\", Object.keys(scores));\nconsole.log(\"scores:\", Object.values(scores));\n\n// find the best subject\nlet best = \"\";\nfor (const [subject, score] of Object.entries(scores)) {\n  if (score > (scores[best] || 0)) best = subject;\n}\nconsole.log(\"best subject:\", best);\n","title_fa":"for...in","html_fa":"\n<p><code>for...in<\/code> روی <b>کلیدها<\/b> (نام ویژگی‌ها) یک شیء حرکت\nمی‌کند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = { name: \"Ada\", age: 36, role: \"admin\" };\n\nfor (const key in user) {\n  console.log(key, user[key]);    // \"name\" \"Ada\", \"age\" 36, ...\n}\n\n// with Object.keys() — often preferred\nfor (const key of Object.keys(user)) {\n  console.log(key);\n}\n\n// Object.entries() for key+value pairs\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(user)) {\n  console.log(`${key}: ${value}`);\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>مهم: <b>روی آرایه‌ها for...in استفاده نکن<\/b> — روی اندیس‌های\nرشته‌ای (\"0\"، \"1\"...) تکرار می‌کند و ممکن است ویژگی‌های به‌ارث‌رسیده\nرا هم بیاورد. برای آرایه‌ها <code>for...of<\/code> یا متدها\n(<code>forEach<\/code>، <code>map<\/code>). for...in برای\n<b>شیءهاست<\/b>.<\/p>\n\n<p>ترجیحِ مدرن: <code>Object.keys()<\/code>،\n<code>Object.values()<\/code> و <code>Object.entries()<\/code> — آرایه‌های\nواقعی برمی‌گردانند که با map/filter/reduce کار می‌کنند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"break & continue","html":"\n<p>Two loop-control keywords that change the flow:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>break<\/b> — exit the loop entirely<\/li>\n<li><b>continue<\/b> — skip to the next iteration<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// break: stop when found\nconst nums = [3, 7, 12, 8, 15];\nfor (const n of nums) {\n  if (n &gt; 10) {\n    console.log(\"found:\", n);\n    break;               // stop here\n  }\n}\n\n// continue: skip odds\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++) {\n  if (i % 2 !== 0) continue;   // skip odd numbers\n  console.log(i);               // 0 2 4 6 8\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>In nested loops, <code>break<\/code>/<code>continue<\/code> affect only\nthe <b>innermost<\/b> loop. To exit an outer loop, use labeled\nstatements:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">outer: for (let i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n  for (let j = 0; j &lt; 3; j++) {\n    if (i * j === 2) break outer;   // exits BOTH loops\n    console.log(i, j);\n  }\n}<\/pre>\n","tryit":"// break: early exit\nconst passwords = [\"1234\", \"letmein\", \"correct-horse\", \"hack\"];\nfor (const pw of passwords) {\n  if (pw === \"correct-horse\") {\n    console.log(\"Found it:\", pw);\n    break;\n  }\n  console.log(\"tried:\", pw);\n}\n\n// continue: skip and keep going\nfor (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {\n  if (i % 3 === 0) continue;   // skip multiples of 3\n  console.log(i);              // 1 2 4 5 7 8 10\n}\n\n// labeled break for nested loops\nouter:\nfor (let row = 0; row < 5; row++) {\n  for (let col = 0; col < 5; col++) {\n    if (row * col > 6) {\n      console.log(`found at (${row}, ${col})`);\n      break outer;\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(\"done searching\");\n","title_fa":"break و continue","html_fa":"\n<p>دو کلیدواژهٔ کنترلِ حلقه که جریان را عوض می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>break<\/b> — کلاً از حلقه بیرون برو<\/li>\n<li><b>continue<\/b> — بپر به تکرارِ بعدی<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// break: stop when found\nconst nums = [3, 7, 12, 8, 15];\nfor (const n of nums) {\n  if (n &gt; 10) {\n    console.log(\"found:\", n);\n    break;               // stop here\n  }\n}\n\n// continue: skip odds\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++) {\n  if (i % 2 !== 0) continue;   // skip odd numbers\n  console.log(i);               // 0 2 4 6 8\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>در حلقه‌های تودرتو، <code>break<\/code>/<code>continue<\/code> فقط\n<b>داخلی‌ترین<\/b> حلقه را اثر می‌دهند. برای خروج از حلقهٔ بیرونی، از\nجمله‌های برچسب‌دار استفاده کن:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">outer: for (let i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n  for (let j = 0; j &lt; 3; j++) {\n    if (i * j === 2) break outer;   // exits BOTH loops\n    console.log(i, j);\n  }\n}<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Error Handling: try / catch / finally & throw","html":"\n<p>Errors happen — invalid input, network failures, missing data. JS\nhandles them with <code>try / catch / finally<\/code> and creates them\nwith <code>throw<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">try {\n  // code that might fail\n  const data = JSON.parse(invalidJson);\n} catch (error) {\n  // runs ONLY if an error occurred\n  console.error(\"Caught:\", error.message);\n} finally {\n  // ALWAYS runs (cleanup)\n  console.log(\"done trying\");\n}\n\n// creating your own errors\nfunction divide(a, b) {\n  if (b === 0) {\n    throw new Error(\"Cannot divide by zero!\");\n  }\n  return a / b;\n}\n\ntry {\n  divide(10, 0);\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);   // \"Cannot divide by zero!\"\n}<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>throw<\/b> — signal an error; you can throw anything, but always\nthrow <code>Error<\/code> instances<\/li>\n<li><b>catch(error)<\/b> — receives the thrown error object\n(<code>error.message<\/code>, <code>error.stack<\/code>)<\/li>\n<li><b>finally<\/b> — cleanup code that runs regardless of success or\nfailure<\/li>\n<li><b>Error types:<\/b> <code>TypeError<\/code>,\n<code>ReferenceError<\/code>, <code>SyntaxError<\/code>,\n<code>RangeError<\/code> — or make your own with\n<code>class MyError extends Error<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>Don't catch-and-ignore: an empty <code>catch {}<\/code> hides bugs.\nLog the error or re-throw it.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Basic try/catch\ntry {\n  const data = JSON.parse(\"not valid json\");\n  console.log(\"never reaches here\");\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(\"caught:\", error.message);\n} finally {\n  console.log(\"finally always runs\");\n}\n\n// throwing custom errors\nfunction validateAge(age) {\n  if (typeof age !== \"number\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"Age must be a number\");\n  }\n  if (age < 0 || age > 150) {\n    throw new RangeError(\"Age must be 0-150\");\n  }\n  return `${age} is valid`;\n}\n\ntry {\n  console.log(validateAge(25));\n  console.log(validateAge(-5));\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(`${e.constructor.name}: ${e.message}`);\n}\n\n// catch with different error types\ntry {\n  null.property;   // TypeError\n} catch (e) {\n  if (e instanceof TypeError) console.log(\"It's a TypeError!\");\n}\n","title_fa":"مدیریت خطا: try / catch / finally و throw","html_fa":"\n<p>خطاها اتفاق می‌افتند — ورودیِ نامعتبر، شکستِ شبکه، دادهٔ گم. JS\nبا <code>try / catch / finally<\/code> از آنها جانبی می‌دهد و با\n<code>throw<\/code> می‌سازدشان:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">try {\n  // code that might fail\n  const data = JSON.parse(invalidJson);\n} catch (error) {\n  // runs ONLY if an error occurred\n  console.error(\"Caught:\", error.message);\n} finally {\n  // ALWAYS runs (cleanup)\n  console.log(\"done trying\");\n}\n\n// creating your own errors\nfunction divide(a, b) {\n  if (b === 0) {\n    throw new Error(\"Cannot divide by zero!\");\n  }\n  return a / b;\n}\n\ntry {\n  divide(10, 0);\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);   // \"Cannot divide by zero!\"\n}<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>throw<\/b> — علامتِ خطا؛ هر چیزی را می‌توان throw کرد اما همیشه\nنمونهٔ <code>Error<\/code> پرتاب کن<\/li>\n<li><b>catch(error)<\/b> — شیءِ خطا را می‌گیرد\n(<code>error.message<\/code>، <code>error.stack<\/code>)<\/li>\n<li><b>finally<\/b> — کدِ پاک‌سازی که فارغ از موفقیت یا شکست اجرا\nمی‌شود<\/li>\n<li><b>انواع خطا:<\/b> <code>TypeError<\/code>،\n<code>ReferenceError<\/code>، <code>SyntaxError<\/code>،\n<code>RangeError<\/code> — یا با <code>class MyError extends\nError<\/code> خودت بساز<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>گرفتن-و-ردکردن نکن: یک <code>catch {}<\/code> خالی باگ را پنهان\nمی‌کند. خطا را لاگ کن یا دوباره پرتابش کن.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"What happens if you omit 'break' in a switch case?","options":["A syntax error","Execution falls through to the next case","The switch is skipped","It returns undefined"],"answer":1,"explain":"Without break, execution continues into the next case — sometimes useful, often a bug.","fa":{"question":"اگر break را در یک case جا بیندازی چه می‌شود؟","options":["خطای نحوی","اجرا به case بعدی سقوط می‌کند","switch رد می‌شود","undefined برمی‌گردد"],"explain":"بدون break، اجرا به case بعدی ادامه می‌یابد — گاهی مفید، اغلب باگ."}},{"type":"blank","question":"The loop that always runs at least once is <code>____...while<\/code>.","answers":["do","do..."],"explain":"do...while checks the condition after the first iteration.","fa":{"question":"حلقه‌ای که همیشه دست‌کم یک بار اجرا می‌شود <code>____...while<\/code> است.","explain":"do...while شرط را بعد از اولین تکرار چک می‌کند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"for...in iterates over:","options":["Values of an array","Keys of an object","Characters of a string","Elements of a Set"],"answer":1,"explain":"for...in yields property names (keys). Use for...of for values.","fa":{"question":"for...in روی چه چیزی تکرار می‌کند؟","options":["مقدارهای آرایه","کلیدهای شیء","نویسه‌های رشته","عنصرهای Set"],"explain":"for...in نام ویژگی‌ها (کلیدها) را می‌دهد. برای مقدارها for...of."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Which runs regardless of whether an error occurred?","options":["try","catch","finally","throw"],"answer":2,"explain":"finally always runs — it's for cleanup code.","fa":{"question":"کدام فارغ از وقوعِ خطا اجرا می‌شود؟","options":["try","catch","finally","throw"],"explain":"finally همیشه اجرا می‌شود — جای کدِ پاک‌سازی است."}},{"type":"mc","question":"In nested loops, 'break' exits:","options":["All loops","The innermost loop only","The outermost loop","The function"],"answer":1,"explain":"break affects the innermost loop; labeled break (break outer:) exits the labeled one.","fa":{"question":"در حلقه‌های تودرتو، break از کدام بیرون می‌رود؟","options":["همهٔ حلقه‌ها","فقط داخلی‌ترین حلقه","بیرونی‌ترین حلقه","تابع"],"explain":"break داخلی‌ترین حلقه را اثر می‌کند؛ break برچسب‌دار (break outer:) از حلقهٔ برچسب‌خورده."}}],"title_fa":"کنترل جریان"},{"id":"js03","title":"Functions","emoji":"🧩","lessons":[{"title":"Functions & Parameters","html":"\n<p>Functions package behaviour behind a name. JS functions are\n<b>first-class citizens<\/b> — they can be stored in variables, passed as\narguments, and returned from other functions:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// declaration\nfunction greet(name) {\n  return `Hello, ${name}!`;\n}\n\n// call it\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\"));     // \"Hello, Ada!\"\n\n// multiple parameters\nfunction add(a, b) {\n  return a + b;\n}\nconsole.log(add(2, 3));        // 5<\/pre>\n\n<p>Parameters are the named placeholders in the definition\n(<code>a, b<\/code>); arguments are the actual values passed in\n(<code>2, 3<\/code>). JS doesn't enforce parameter counts — missing\narguments become <code>undefined<\/code>, extras are ignored (but\naccessible via <code>arguments<\/code> or rest params).<\/p>\n","tryit":"function greet(name, greeting = \"Hello\") {\n  return `${greeting}, ${name}!`;\n}\n\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\"));\nconsole.log(greet(\"Grace\", \"Hi\"));\n\n// functions as values\nconst sayHi = greet;\nconsole.log(sayHi(\"Beej\"));\n\n// passing functions to functions\nfunction callTwice(fn, arg) {\n  console.log(fn(arg));\n  console.log(fn(arg));\n}\ncallTwice(greet, \"MDN\");\n","title_fa":"توابع و پارامترها","html_fa":"\n<p>توابع رفتار را پشت یک نام بسته‌بندی می‌کنند. توابع JS\n<b>شهروندِ درجه‌یک<\/b>ند — در متغیر ذخیره می‌شوند، به‌عنوان آرگومان\nداده می‌شوند و از توابع دیگر برگردانده می‌شوند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// declaration\nfunction greet(name) {\n  return `Hello, ${name}!`;\n}\n\n// call it\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\"));     // \"Hello, Ada!\"\n\n// multiple parameters\nfunction add(a, b) {\n  return a + b;\n}\nconsole.log(add(2, 3));        // 5<\/pre>\n\n<p>پارامترها جای‌نگهدارهای نامیِ تعریف‌اند (<code>a, b<\/code>)؛\nآرگومان‌ها مقدارهای واقعیِ داده‌شده‌اند (<code>2, 3<\/code>). JS تعدادِ\nپارامتر را اجبار نمی‌کند — آرگومانِ جاافتاده <code>undefined<\/code>\nمی‌شود و اضافه‌ها نادیده گرفته می‌شوند (اما با rest params قابل\nدسترس‌اند).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Return Values","html":"\n<p><code>return<\/code> sends a value back to the caller and exits the\nfunction immediately:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function add(a, b) {\n  return a + b;      // exits here\n  console.log(\"never runs\");\n}\n\nconsole.log(add(1, 2));   // 3\n\n// functions without return → undefined\nfunction log(msg) {\n  console.log(msg);\n  // no return → returns undefined\n}\nconsole.log(log(\"hi\"));  // undefined<\/pre>\n\n<p>Functions can return any type — including other functions, objects,\narrays. Multiple values come back as an object or array:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function getStats(numbers) {\n  return { min: Math.min(...numbers), max: Math.max(...numbers) };\n}\nconst { min, max } = getStats([3, 1, 4, 1, 5]);\nconsole.log(min, max);   // 1 5<\/pre>\n","tryit":"function calculateCircle(r) {\n  const area = Math.PI * r ** 2;\n  const circumference = 2 * Math.PI * r;\n  return { area: area.toFixed(2), circumference: circumference.toFixed(2) };\n}\n\nconst { area, circumference } = calculateCircle(5);\nconsole.log(\"area:\", area);\nconsole.log(\"circumference:\", circumference);\n\n// early return pattern\nfunction classify(n) {\n  if (n < 0) return \"negative\";\n  if (n === 0) return \"zero\";\n  return \"positive\";\n}\nconsole.log(classify(-5), classify(0), classify(7));\n","title_fa":"مقدارهای برگشتی","html_fa":"\n<p><code>return<\/code> مقداری را به فراخواننده پس می‌دهد و همان لحظه از\nتابع خارج می‌شود:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function add(a, b) {\n  return a + b;      // exits here\n  console.log(\"never runs\");\n}\n\nconsole.log(add(1, 2));   // 3\n\n// functions without return → undefined\nfunction log(msg) {\n  console.log(msg);\n  // no return → returns undefined\n}\nconsole.log(log(\"hi\"));  // undefined<\/pre>\n\n<p>توابع می‌توانند هر نوعی را برگردانند — حتی تابع، شیء و آرایه.\nمقدارهای چندگانه به‌صورت object یا array برمی‌گردند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function getStats(numbers) {\n  return { min: Math.min(...numbers), max: Math.max(...numbers) };\n}\nconst { min, max } = getStats([3, 1, 4, 1, 5]);\nconsole.log(min, max);   // 1 5<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Function Expressions & Arrow Functions","html":"\n<p>Functions can be <b>expressions<\/b> (assigned to variables) rather\nthan declarations. The modern arrow syntax is shorter and has a\ndifferent <code>this<\/code> binding:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// function expression\nconst double = function(n) { return n * 2; };\n\n// arrow function (same result, shorter)\nconst double2 = (n) => n * 2;\n\n// single parameter → parens optional\nconst triple = n => n * 3;\n\n// multiple parameters → parens required\nconst add = (a, b) => a + b;\n\n// no parameters → empty parens\nconst hello = () => \"hello!\";\n\n// multi-line body → braces + return\nconst process = (x) => {\n  const result = x * 2;\n  return result + 1;\n};\n\n// returning an object literal → wrap in parens\nconst makePair = (a, b) => ({ first: a, second: b });<\/pre>\n\n<p>Key difference: arrow functions don't have their own\n<code>this<\/code> — they inherit it from the surrounding scope. This\nmakes them perfect for callbacks where you want the outer\n<code>this<\/code>.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\n\n// arrow functions shine as callbacks\nconst doubled = nums.map(n => n * 2);\nconsole.log(\"doubled:\", doubled);\n\nconst evens = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0);\nconsole.log(\"evens:\", evens);\n\nconst sum = nums.reduce((acc, n) => acc + n, 0);\nconsole.log(\"sum:\", sum);\n\n// implicit return — no braces needed\nconst squares = nums.map(n => n ** 2);\nconsole.log(\"squares:\", squares);\n\n// multi-line with explicit return\nconst labeled = nums.map(n => {\n  const label = n % 2 === 0 ? \"even\" : \"odd\";\n  return `${n} is ${label}`;\n});\nconsole.log(labeled);\n","title_fa":"عبارت‌های تابعی و توابع پیکانی","html_fa":"\n<p>توابع می‌توانند <b>عبارت<\/b> باشند (منتسب به متغیر) نه اعلام.\nنحوِ پیکانیِ مدرن کوتاه‌تر است و اتصالِ <code>this<\/code> متفاوتی\nدارد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// function expression\nconst double = function(n) { return n * 2; };\n\n// arrow function (same result, shorter)\nconst double2 = (n) => n * 2;\n\n// single parameter → parens optional\nconst triple = n => n * 3;\n\n// multiple parameters → parens required\nconst add = (a, b) => a + b;\n\n// no parameters → empty parens\nconst hello = () => \"hello!\";\n\n// multi-line body → braces + return\nconst process = (x) => {\n  const result = x * 2;\n  return result + 1;\n};\n\n// returning an object literal → wrap in parens\nconst makePair = (a, b) => ({ first: a, second: b });<\/pre>\n\n<p>تفاوت کلیدی: توابع پیکانی <code>this<\/code> خودشان را ندارند — از\nscope اطراف به ارث می‌برند. برای همین برای callbackها، جایی که\n<code>this<\/code> بیرونی را می‌خواهی، عالی‌اند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Default & Rest Parameters","html":"\n<p><b>Default parameters<\/b> provide fallback values when an argument\nis <code>undefined<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function greet(name = \"guest\", greeting = \"Hello\") {\n  return `${greeting}, ${name}!`;\n}\nconsole.log(greet());           // \"Hello, guest!\"\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\"));     // \"Hello, Ada!\"\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\", \"Hi\")); // \"Hi, Ada!\"<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Rest parameters<\/b> (<code>...name<\/code>) collect remaining\narguments into a real array:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function sum(...numbers) {\n  return numbers.reduce((acc, n) => acc + n, 0);\n}\nconsole.log(sum(1, 2));           // 3\nconsole.log(sum(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)); // 15\n\n// mixed: named params first, rest last\nfunction introduce(greeting, ...names) {\n  return `${greeting}, ${names.join(\" and \")}!`;\n}\nconsole.log(introduce(\"Hi\", \"Ada\", \"Grace\"));<\/pre>\n\n<p>Rest parameters must be the <b>last<\/b> parameter. They replace the\nlegacy <code>arguments<\/code> object with a real array that has\n<code>map<\/code>, <code>filter<\/code>, etc.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Default parameters\nfunction power(base, exponent = 2) {\n  return base ** exponent;\n}\nconsole.log(power(3));     // 9 (default exponent = 2)\nconsole.log(power(3, 3));  // 27\n\n// Rest parameters\nfunction average(...scores) {\n  if (scores.length === 0) return 0;\n  return scores.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / scores.length;\n}\nconsole.log(average(90, 85, 92));  // average of 3 scores\nconsole.log(average());            // 0 (empty)\n\n// combining defaults + rest\nfunction createPost(title, tags = [\"general\"], ...meta) {\n  console.log(\"title:\", title);\n  console.log(\"tags:\", tags);\n  console.log(\"meta:\", meta);\n}\ncreatePost(\"Hello World\", \"js\", \"tutorial\", \"2026\");\n","title_fa":"پارامترهای پیش‌فرض و rest","html_fa":"\n<p><b>پارامترهای پیش‌فرض<\/b> وقتی آرگومانی <code>undefined<\/code> است\nمقدارِ جایگزین می‌دهند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function greet(name = \"guest\", greeting = \"Hello\") {\n  return `${greeting}, ${name}!`;\n}\nconsole.log(greet());           // \"Hello, guest!\"\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\"));     // \"Hello, Ada!\"\nconsole.log(greet(\"Ada\", \"Hi\")); // \"Hi, Ada!\"<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>پارامترهای rest<\/b> (<code>...name<\/code>) بقیهٔ آرگومان‌ها را در\nیک آرایهٔ واقعی جمع می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function sum(...numbers) {\n  return numbers.reduce((acc, n) => acc + n, 0);\n}\nconsole.log(sum(1, 2));           // 3\nconsole.log(sum(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)); // 15\n\n// mixed: named params first, rest last\nfunction introduce(greeting, ...names) {\n  return `${greeting}, ${names.join(\" and \")}!`;\n}\nconsole.log(introduce(\"Hi\", \"Ada\", \"Grace\"));<\/pre>\n\n<p>rest باید <b>آخرین<\/b> پارامتر باشد. با آرایه‌ای واقعی که\n<code>map<\/code> و <code>filter<\/code> دارد، جایگزینِ شیءِ قدیمی\n<code>arguments<\/code> شده است.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Spread Syntax","html":"\n<p>Spread (<code>...<\/code>) \"unpacks\" an iterable into individual\nelements — the mirror of rest parameters. It expands arrays, strings,\nand objects in places where multiple elements are expected:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// spread in function calls\nconst nums = [3, 1, 4];\nconsole.log(Math.max(...nums));    // 4 (not [3,1,4])\n\n// copy an array (shallow)\nconst copy = [...nums];\n\n// merge arrays\nconst a = [1, 2], b = [3, 4];\nconst merged = [...a, ...b];       // [1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n// spread in object literals\nconst defaults = { theme: \"light\", lang: \"en\" };\nconst user = { ...defaults, theme: \"dark\" };  // override theme\n// { theme: \"dark\", lang: \"en\" }<\/pre>\n\n<p>Spread creates <b>shallow<\/b> copies — nested objects are still\nshared references. For deep copies, use\n<code>structuredClone()<\/code>.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const arr1 = [1, 2, 3];\nconst arr2 = [4, 5, 6];\n\n// spread in function calls\nconsole.log(Math.max(...arr1, ...arr2));  // 6\n\n// array copy + merge\nconst combined = [...arr1, 0, ...arr2];\nconsole.log(combined);   // [1, 2, 3, 0, 4, 5, 6]\n\n// string spread (iterates characters)\nconsole.log([...\"abc\"]);  // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n\n// object spread: merge + override\nconst base = { a: 1, b: 2 };\nconst extended = { ...base, b: 99, c: 3 };\nconsole.log(extended);   // { a: 1, b: 99, c: 3 }\n\n// shallow copy caveat\nconst nested = { inner: { val: 1 } };\nconst copy = { ...nested };\ncopy.inner.val = 99;\nconsole.log(nested.inner.val);  // 99 — still shared!\n","title_fa":"نحوِ spread","html_fa":"\n<p>‏Spread (<code>...<\/code>) یک iterable را به عنصرهای جدا «باز\nمی‌کند» — آینهٔ rest. آرایه‌ها، رشته‌ها و شیءها را در جاهایی که چند\nعنصر انتظار می‌رود می‌گسترد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// spread in function calls\nconst nums = [3, 1, 4];\nconsole.log(Math.max(...nums));    // 4 (not [3,1,4])\n\n// copy an array (shallow)\nconst copy = [...nums];\n\n// merge arrays\nconst a = [1, 2], b = [3, 4];\nconst merged = [...a, ...b];       // [1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n// spread in object literals\nconst defaults = { theme: \"light\", lang: \"en\" };\nconst user = { ...defaults, theme: \"dark\" };  // override theme\n// { theme: \"dark\", lang: \"en\" }<\/pre>\n\n<p>‏Spread کپیِ <b>سطحی<\/b> می‌سازد — شیءهای تودرتو همچنان ارجاعِ مشترک\nهستند. برای کپی عمیق از <code>structuredClone()<\/code> استفاده\nکن.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Scope & Closures","html":"\n<p><b>Scope<\/b> determines where variables are visible. JS has:\n<b>global<\/b> scope, <b>function<\/b> scope, and <b>block<\/b> scope\n(let/const):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const global = \"everywhere\";\n\nfunction outer() {\n  const outerVar = \"visible in outer\";\n  function inner() {\n    console.log(global);    // ✓ can see global\n    console.log(outerVar);  // ✓ can see outer's variable\n  }\n  inner();\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>A <b>closure<\/b> is a function that remembers the variables from\nwhere it was created, even after that scope has exited. It's one of\nJS's most powerful features:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function makeCounter() {\n  let count = 0;              // private variable!\n  return function() {\n    count++;                  // closure captures count\n    return count;\n  };\n}\n\nconst counter = makeCounter();\nconsole.log(counter());   // 1\nconsole.log(counter());   // 2\nconsole.log(counter());   // 3 — count persists!\n\nconst counter2 = makeCounter();\nconsole.log(counter2());  // 1 — independent counter!<\/pre>\n\n<p>Closures enable <b>data privacy<\/b> (count is invisible from\noutside), <b>factories<\/b> (makeCounter creates independent\ninstances), and <b>partial application<\/b>. Every callback that\nreferences outer variables is using a closure.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Closure: a private counter\nfunction makeWallet(startingBalance) {\n  let balance = startingBalance;   // private!\n\n  return {\n    deposit(amount) { balance += amount; return balance; },\n    withdraw(amount) {\n      if (amount > balance) return \"insufficient funds\";\n      balance -= amount;\n      return balance;\n    },\n    getBalance() { return balance; },\n  };\n}\n\nconst wallet = makeWallet(100);\nconsole.log(wallet.deposit(50));   // 150\nconsole.log(wallet.withdraw(30));  // 120\nconsole.log(wallet.getBalance()); // 120\n// wallet.balance = 999999;       // doesn't work — it's private!\n\n// closure in a loop (the classic interview question)\nconst functions = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n  functions.push(() => i);   // let creates a new i per iteration\n}\nconsole.log(functions.map(f => f()));  // [0, 1, 2] — not [3, 3, 3]!\n","title_fa":"scope و closureها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>scope<\/b> تعیین می‌کند متغیرها کجا دیده می‌شوند. JS دارد:\nscope <b>سراسری<\/b>، <b>تابعی<\/b> و <b>بلوکی<\/b> (با\nlet/const):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const global = \"everywhere\";\n\nfunction outer() {\n  const outerVar = \"visible in outer\";\n  function inner() {\n    console.log(global);    // ✓ can see global\n    console.log(outerVar);  // ✓ can see outer's variable\n  }\n  inner();\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>یک <b>closure<\/b> تابعی است که متغیرهای محلِ ساخته‌شدنش را به یاد\nدارد، حتی بعد از خروج آن scope. یکی از قدرتمندترین قابلیت‌های\nJS:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function makeCounter() {\n  let count = 0;              // private variable!\n  return function() {\n    count++;                  // closure captures count\n    return count;\n  };\n}\n\nconst counter = makeCounter();\nconsole.log(counter());   // 1\nconsole.log(counter());   // 2\nconsole.log(counter());   // 3 — count persists!\n\nconst counter2 = makeCounter();\nconsole.log(counter2());  // 1 — independent counter!<\/pre>\n\n<p>closureها <b>حریمِ داده<\/b> (count از بیرون نامرئی است)،\n<b>کارخانه‌ها<\/b> (makeCounter نمونه‌های مستقل می‌سازد) و\n<b>اعمالِ جزئی<\/b> را ممکن می‌کنند. هر callbackی که به متغیرهای بیرونی\nارجاع می‌دهد دارد از closure استفاده می‌کند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Callbacks","html":"\n<p>A <b>callback<\/b> is a function passed as an argument to another\nfunction, to be called later. Callbacks are the foundation of\nevent handling, array methods, and async code:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// callback in array methods\nconst nums = [1, 2, 3];\nconst doubled = nums.map(n =&gt; n * 2);      // [2, 4, 6]\nconst evens = nums.filter(n =&gt; n % 2 === 0); // [2]\n\n// callback in setTimeout (async)\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"1 second later\");\n}, 1000);\n\n// custom function that accepts a callback\nfunction process(data, onSuccess, onError) {\n  if (data) onSuccess(data);\n  else onError(\"no data\");\n}\n\nprocess({ msg: \"hello\" },\n  (d) =&gt; console.log(\"got:\", d.msg),\n  (err) =&gt; console.log(\"error:\", err)\n);<\/pre>\n\n<p>Callbacks can be <b>synchronous<\/b> (called immediately, like in\nmap) or <b>asynchronous<\/b> (called later, like setTimeout). Nested\ncallbacks for sequential async operations lead to\n<b>callback hell<\/b> — the problem Promises solve (Async chapter).<\/p>\n","tryit":"// callbacks with array methods\nconst words = [\"hello\", \"world\", \"js\"];\n\nconst upper = words.map(w => w.toUpperCase());\nconsole.log(upper);\n\nconst long = words.filter(w => w.length > 4);\nconsole.log(\"long words:\", long);\n\n// custom higher-order function\nfunction repeat(times, fn) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < times; i++) fn(i);\n}\nrepeat(3, (i) => console.log(`iteration ${i + 1}`));\n\n// callback with error pattern\nfunction divide(a, b, callback) {\n  if (b === 0) {\n    callback(new Error(\"division by zero\"), null);\n    return;\n  }\n  callback(null, a / b);\n}\ndivide(10, 2, (err, result) => {\n  if (err) console.log(\"error:\", err.message);\n  else console.log(\"result:\", result);\n});\n","title_fa":"callbackها","html_fa":"\n<p>یک <b>callback<\/b> تابعی است که به‌عنوان آرگومان به تابع دیگری داده\nمی‌شود تا بعداً صدا زده شود. callbackها پایهٔ مدیریت رخدادها، متدهای\nآرایه و کد async هستند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// callback in array methods\nconst nums = [1, 2, 3];\nconst doubled = nums.map(n =&gt; n * 2);      // [2, 4, 6]\nconst evens = nums.filter(n =&gt; n % 2 === 0); // [2]\n\n// callback in setTimeout (async)\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"1 second later\");\n}, 1000);\n\n// custom function that accepts a callback\nfunction process(data, onSuccess, onError) {\n  if (data) onSuccess(data);\n  else onError(\"no data\");\n}\n\nprocess({ msg: \"hello\" },\n  (d) =&gt; console.log(\"got:\", d.msg),\n  (err) =&gt; console.log(\"error:\", err)\n);<\/pre>\n\n<p>callbackها می‌توانند <b>همگام<\/b> باشند (فوری صدا زده می‌شوند، مثل\nmap) یا <b>ناهمگام<\/b> (بعداً، مثل setTimeout). callbackهای تودرتو برای\nعملیات ترتیبی به <b>جهنمِ callback<\/b> می‌رسند — مشکلی که Promiseها\nحلش می‌کنند (فصل async).<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"What does an arrow function NOT have its own of?","options":["Parameters","Return value","this","Name"],"answer":2,"explain":"Arrow functions inherit this from the surrounding scope — that's their key feature.","fa":{"question":"تابع پیکانی مالِ خودش چه چیزی ندارد؟","options":["پارامتر","مقدار برگشتی","this","نام"],"explain":"توابع پیکانی this را از scope اطراف به ارث می‌برند — ویژگی کلیدی‌شان."}},{"type":"blank","question":"Rest parameters collect remaining arguments into a ____.","answers":["array","real array"],"explain":"function sum(...nums) — nums is a real array with map/filter/etc.","fa":{"question":"پارامترهای rest بقیهٔ آرگومان‌ها را داخل یک ____ جمع می‌کنند.","explain":"function sum(...nums) — یعنی nums آرایه‌ای واقعی با map/filter و... است."}},{"type":"mc","question":"What is a closure?","options":["A closed curly brace","A function that remembers variables from where it was created","A way to end a program","A type of loop"],"answer":1,"explain":"Closures capture outer variables, enabling data privacy and factories.","fa":{"question":"closure چیست؟","options":["یک آکولادِ بسته","تابعی که متغیرهای محلِ ساخته‌شدنش را به یاد دارد","راهی برای پایان دادن به برنامه","نوعی حلقه"],"explain":"closureها متغیرهای بیرونی را می‌گیرند و حریم داده و کارخانه می‌سازند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"The spread syntax ... does what to an array in a function call?","options":["Collects arguments","Unpacks elements as individual arguments","Copies the reference","Sorts it"],"answer":1,"explain":"Math.max(...[3,1,4]) becomes Math.max(3,1,4).","fa":{"question":"نحوِ spread ... در فراخوانی تابع با آرایه چه می‌کند؟","options":["آرگومان‌ها را جمع می‌کند","عنصرها را به‌صورت آرگومان جدا باز می‌کند","ارجاع را کپی می‌کند","مرتبش می‌کند"],"explain":"‏Math.max(...[3,1,4]) یعنی Math.max(3,1,4)."}}],"title_fa":"توابع"},{"id":"js04","title":"Arrays & Objects","emoji":"📦","lessons":[{"title":"Arrays","html":"\n<p>Arrays are ordered, zero-indexed collections. They can hold any mix\nof types and grow dynamically:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];\n\nfruits.length           // 3\nfruits[0]               // \"apple\" (first)\nfruits[fruits.length - 1]  // \"cherry\" (last)\n\nfruits.push(\"date\");    // add to end → 4\nfruits.pop();           // remove from end → \"date\"\nfruits.unshift(\"avocado\"); // add to start\nfruits.shift();          // remove from start\n\nfruits.indexOf(\"banana\") // 1\nfruits.includes(\"apple\") // true\n\n// slicing (doesn't modify original)\nfruits.slice(1, 3)       // [\"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\n// joining\nfruits.join(\", \")        // \"apple, banana, cherry\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>Arrays are actually objects with numeric keys —\n<code>typeof fruits<\/code> returns <code>\"object\"<\/code>. Use\n<code>Array.isArray()<\/code> to check.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const todo = [\"learn JS\", \"build projects\", \"get a job\"];\n\nconsole.log(\"length:\", todo.length);\nconsole.log(\"first:\", todo[0]);\nconsole.log(\"last:\", todo[todo.length - 1]);\n\n// mutate\ntodo.push(\"teach others\");\nconsole.log(\"after push:\", todo);\ntodo.shift();\nconsole.log(\"after shift:\", todo);\n\n// search\nconsole.log(\"has 'learn JS':\", todo.includes(\"learn JS\"));\nconsole.log(\"index of 'build':\", todo.indexOf(\"build projects\"));\n\n// slice (non-destructive)\nconst firstTwo = todo.slice(0, 2);\nconsole.log(\"sliced:\", firstTwo);\nconsole.log(\"original:\", todo);\n","title_fa":"آرایه‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p>آرایه‌ها مجموعه‌های مرتب و اندیس-صفر هستند. هر ترکیبی از انواع را\nمی‌گیرند و پویا رشد می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];\n\nfruits.length           // 3\nfruits[0]               // \"apple\" (first)\nfruits[fruits.length - 1]  // \"cherry\" (last)\n\nfruits.push(\"date\");    // add to end → 4\nfruits.pop();           // remove from end → \"date\"\nfruits.unshift(\"avocado\"); // add to start\nfruits.shift();          // remove from start\n\nfruits.indexOf(\"banana\") // 1\nfruits.includes(\"apple\") // true\n\n// slicing (doesn't modify original)\nfruits.slice(1, 3)       // [\"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n\n// joining\nfruits.join(\", \")        // \"apple, banana, cherry\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>آرایه‌ها در واقع شیءهایی با کلیدهای عددی‌اند —\n<code>typeof fruits<\/code> مقدار <code>\"object\"<\/code> می‌دهد. برای چک\nکردن از <code>Array.isArray()<\/code> استفاده کن.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Array Methods","html":"\n<p>The three essential array methods — <code>map<\/code>,\n<code>filter<\/code>, <code>reduce<\/code> — transform data without\nmutating the original:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\n\n// map: transform each element → new array\nconst doubled = nums.map(n =&gt; n * 2);       // [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\n\n// filter: keep elements that pass the test → new array\nconst evens = nums.filter(n =&gt; n % 2 === 0); // [2, 4]\n\n// reduce: boil down to a single value\nconst sum = nums.reduce((acc, n) =&gt; acc + n, 0); // 15\n\n// find: first matching element\nconst first = nums.find(n =&gt; n &gt; 3);        // 4\n\n// some/every: boolean checks\nnums.some(n =&gt; n &gt; 4);       // true (at least one)\nnums.every(n =&gt; n &gt; 0);      // true (all of them)\n\n// sort: MUTATES the original! Use [...arr].sort() to avoid\nconst sorted = [...nums].sort((a, b) =&gt; b - a);  // descending<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>map<\/code>, <code>filter<\/code>, and <code>reduce<\/code> are\nthe functional programming trio — they chain beautifully:\n<code>nums.filter(n =&gt; n &gt; 2).map(n =&gt; n * 10).reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b)<\/code><\/p>\n","tryit":"const products = [\n  { name: \"Laptop\", price: 999, inStock: true },\n  { name: \"Mouse\", price: 25, inStock: true },\n  { name: \"Keyboard\", price: 75, inStock: false },\n  { name: \"Monitor\", price: 300, inStock: true },\n];\n\n// map: extract names\nconst names = products.map(p => p.name);\nconsole.log(\"names:\", names);\n\n// filter: in-stock items\nconst available = products.filter(p => p.inStock);\nconsole.log(\"in stock:\", available.map(p => p.name));\n\n// reduce: total value of in-stock items\nconst total = products\n  .filter(p => p.inStock)\n  .reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.price, 0);\nconsole.log(\"total value:\", total);\n\n// find: first expensive item\nconst expensive = products.find(p => p.price > 200);\nconsole.log(\"first expensive:\", expensive?.name);\n\n// chaining\nconst result = products\n  .filter(p => p.inStock)\n  .map(p => `${p.name} ($${p.price})`)\n  .join(\", \");\nconsole.log(\"shopping list:\", result);\n","title_fa":"متدهای آرایه","html_fa":"\n<p>سه متدِ ضروریِ آرایه — <code>map<\/code>،\n<code>filter<\/code> و <code>reduce<\/code> — داده را بدون تغییرِ اصل\nتبدیل می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\n\n// map: transform each element → new array\nconst doubled = nums.map(n =&gt; n * 2);       // [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\n\n// filter: keep elements that pass the test → new array\nconst evens = nums.filter(n =&gt; n % 2 === 0); // [2, 4]\n\n// reduce: boil down to a single value\nconst sum = nums.reduce((acc, n) =&gt; acc + n, 0); // 15\n\n// find: first matching element\nconst first = nums.find(n =&gt; n &gt; 3);        // 4\n\n// some/every: boolean checks\nnums.some(n =&gt; n &gt; 4);       // true (at least one)\nnums.every(n =&gt; n &gt; 0);      // true (all of them)\n\n// sort: MUTATES the original! Use [...arr].sort() to avoid\nconst sorted = [...nums].sort((a, b) =&gt; b - a);  // descending<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>map<\/code>، <code>filter<\/code> و <code>reduce<\/code> سه‌نفرهٔ\nبرنامه‌نویسی تابعی‌اند — و زیبا زنجیر می‌شوند:<\/p>\n\n<p>همچنین <code>find<\/code> (اولین تطبیق)،\n<code>some<\/code>/<code>every<\/code> (چک‌های بولی) و\n<code>sort<\/code> (توجه: تغییر می‌دهد! با <code>[...arr].sort()<\/code>\nکپی کن).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Destructuring","html":"\n<p><b>Destructuring<\/b> unpacks values from arrays and objects into\ndistinct variables — cleaner than manual assignment:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// array destructuring\nconst [first, second] = [1, 2, 3];\nconsole.log(first, second);      // 1 2\n\n// skip elements\nconst [, third] = [1, 2, 3];    // 3\n\n// default values\nconst [a = 10, b = 20] = [1];   // a=1, b=20 (default)\n\n// swap variables\nlet x = 1, y = 2;\n[x, y] = [y, x];                 // x=2, y=1\n\n// object destructuring\nconst user = { name: \"Ada\", age: 36 };\nconst { name, age } = user;      // name=\"Ada\", age=36\n\n// rename\nconst { name: fullName } = user; // fullName=\"Ada\"\n\n// nested destructuring\nconst config = { db: { host: \"localhost\", port: 5432 } };\nconst { db: { host, port } } = config;<\/pre>\n\n<p>Destructuring also works in function parameters — the pattern for\noptions objects:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function connect({ host = \"localhost\", port = 3000 }) {\n  console.log(`${host}:${port}`);\n}\nconnect({ port: 8080 });   // \"localhost:8080\"<\/pre>\n","tryit":"// Array destructuring\nconst rgb = [255, 128, 0];\nconst [red, green, blue] = rgb;\nconsole.log(`R:${red} G:${green} B:${blue}`);\n\n// Skip + default\nconst [first, , third = \"default\"] = [\"a\", \"b\"];\nconsole.log(first, third);\n\n// Swap without a temp variable\nlet x = 1, y = 2;\n[x, y] = [y, x];\nconsole.log(\"x:\", x, \"y:\", y);\n\n// Object destructuring in function params\nfunction printUser({ name, role = \"user\", email }) {\n  console.log(`${name} (${role}) — ${email}`);\n}\nprintUser({ name: \"Ada\", email: \"ada@x.io\" });\nprintUser({ name: \"Admin\", role: \"admin\", email: \"admin@x.io\" });\n","title_fa":"destructuring","html_fa":"\n<p><b>destructuring<\/b> مقدارها را از آرایه‌ها و شیءها به متغیرهای\nجدا باز می‌کند — تمیزتر از انتسابِ دستی:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// array destructuring\nconst [first, second] = [1, 2, 3];\nconsole.log(first, second);      // 1 2\n\n// skip elements\nconst [, third] = [1, 2, 3];    // 3\n\n// default values\nconst [a = 10, b = 20] = [1];   // a=1, b=20 (default)\n\n// swap variables\nlet x = 1, y = 2;\n[x, y] = [y, x];                 // x=2, y=1\n\n// object destructuring\nconst user = { name: \"Ada\", age: 36 };\nconst { name, age } = user;      // name=\"Ada\", age=36\n\n// rename\nconst { name: fullName } = user; // fullName=\"Ada\"\n\n// nested destructuring\nconst config = { db: { host: \"localhost\", port: 5432 } };\nconst { db: { host, port } } = config;<\/pre>\n\n<p>destructuring در پارامترهای تابع هم کار می‌کند — الگوی شیءِ\nگزینه‌ها:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function connect({ host = \"localhost\", port = 3000 }) {\n  console.log(`${host}:${port}`);\n}\nconnect({ port: 8080 });   // \"localhost:8080\"<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Objects, Properties & Methods","html":"\n<p>Objects are key-value collections — the fundamental data structure\nof JS. Almost everything is an object:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",              // property\n  age: 36,\n  \"has-pets\": true,         // keys with dashes need quotes\n  greet() {                 // method (shorthand)\n    return `Hi, I'm ${this.name}`;\n  },\n};\n\n// access: dot or bracket\nuser.name                  // \"Ada\"\nuser[\"age\"]                // 36\nuser[\"has-pets\"]           // true (bracket needed for dashes)\n\n// add / modify / delete\nuser.email = \"ada@x.io\";   // add\nuser.age = 37;             // modify\ndelete user.email;         // remove\n\n// check if property exists\n\"name\" in user             // true\nuser.hasOwnProperty(\"age\") // true\nuser.email?.length         // undefined (already deleted)<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>this<\/code> inside a method refers to the object the method is\ncalled on — that's how <code>this.name<\/code> works above. The value of\n<code>this<\/code> depends on HOW the function is called, not where it's\ndefined (the Advanced chapter covers this deeply).<\/p>\n","tryit":"const book = {\n  title: \"Eloquent JavaScript\",\n  author: \"Marijn Haverbeke\",\n  pages: 472,\n  read: false,\n\n  // method\n  summary() {\n    return `${this.title} by ${this.author} (${this.pages}p)`;\n  },\n\n  markRead() {\n    this.read = true;\n    return `${this.title} — marked as read!`;\n  },\n};\n\nconsole.log(book.summary());\nconsole.log(book.markRead());\nconsole.log(\"read:\", book.read);\n\n// dynamic keys\nconst key = \"publisher\";\nbook[key] = \"No Starch Press\";\nconsole.log(book.publisher);\n\n// Object.keys/values/entries\nconsole.log(\"keys:\", Object.keys(book));\nconsole.log(\"values:\", Object.values(book));\n","title_fa":"شیءها، ویژگی‌ها و متدها","html_fa":"\n<p>شیءها مجموعه‌های کلید-مقدارند — ساختار دادهٔ بنیادیِ JS. تقریباً\nهمه‌چیز شیء است:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",              // property\n  age: 36,\n  \"has-pets\": true,         // keys with dashes need quotes\n  greet() {                 // method (shorthand)\n    return `Hi, I'm ${this.name}`;\n  },\n};\n\n// access: dot or bracket\nuser.name                  // \"Ada\"\nuser[\"age\"]                // 36\nuser[\"has-pets\"]           // true (bracket needed for dashes)\n\n// add / modify / delete\nuser.email = \"ada@x.io\";   // add\nuser.age = 37;             // modify\ndelete user.email;         // remove\n\n// check if property exists\n\"name\" in user             // true\nuser.hasOwnProperty(\"age\") // true\nuser.email?.length         // undefined (already deleted)<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>this<\/code> داخل متد، به شیئی اشاره دارد که متد رویش صدا زده\nشده — این‌طور <code>this.name<\/code> بالا کار می‌کند. مقدارِ\n<code>this<\/code> به <b>چگونگیِ فراخوانی<\/b> بستگی دارد نه محلِ تعریف\n(فصل پیشرفته عمیق واردش می‌شود).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Optional Chaining & Nullish Coalescing","html":"\n<p>Two modern operators that make null-safety elegant instead of\nmessy.<\/p>\n\n<p><b><code>?.<\/code> (optional chaining)<\/b> — safely access nested\nproperties without checking each level:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// before: the pyramid of doom\nif (user &amp;&amp; user.profile &amp;&amp; user.profile.email) {\n  console.log(user.profile.email);\n}\n\n// after: one line\nconsole.log(user?.profile?.email);   // undefined, no crash!\n\n// also works with methods and array access\nconst result = data?.find?.(x =&gt; x.id === 1);\nconst first = list?.[0];<\/pre>\n\n<p><b><code>??<\/code> (nullish coalescing)<\/b> — default value for\nnull/undefined only (not 0 or \"\"):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const volume = 0;\nvolume || 50    // 50 (0 is falsy — WRONG!)\nvolume ?? 50    // 0  (0 is not nullish — correct!)\n\nconst name = null;\nname ?? \"Anonymous\"   // \"Anonymous\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>They chain: <code>user?.settings?.volume ?? 50<\/code> — safe access\nwith a sensible default. These two operators eliminate most null-check\nboilerplate.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const users = [\n  { name: \"Ada\", profile: { bio: \"Programmer\", social: { twitter: \"@ada\" } } },\n  { name: \"Grace\", profile: {} },\n  { name: \"Anonymous\" },\n];\n\n// optional chaining: safe deep access\nconsole.log(users[0]?.profile?.social?.twitter);  // \"@ada\"\nconsole.log(users[1]?.profile?.social?.twitter);  // undefined\nconsole.log(users[2]?.profile?.social?.twitter);  // undefined (no crash!)\n\n// nullish coalescing: defaults for null/undefined\nfor (const u of users) {\n  const bio = u.profile?.bio ?? \"No bio\";\n  const twitter = u.profile?.social?.twitter ?? \"no twitter\";\n  console.log(`${u.name}: ${bio} | ${twitter}`);\n}\n\n// ?? vs || — the critical difference\nconst volume = 0;\nconsole.log(volume || 50);   // 50 (0 is falsy — wrong!)\nconsole.log(volume ?? 50);   // 0 (0 is not nullish — right!)\n","title_fa":"زنجیرهٔ اختیاری و الحاقِ هیچ‌گرا","html_fa":"\n<p>دو عملگر مدرن که امنیتِ null را به‌جای کدِ شلوغ، شیک\nمی‌کنند.<\/p>\n\n<p><b><code>?.<\/code> (زنجیرهٔ اختیاری)<\/b> — دسترسیِ امن به ویژگی‌های\nتودرتو بدون چک‌کردنِ هر سطح:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// before: the pyramid of doom\nif (user &amp;&amp; user.profile &amp;&amp; user.profile.email) {\n  console.log(user.profile.email);\n}\n\n// after: one line\nconsole.log(user?.profile?.email);   // undefined, no crash!\n\n// also works with methods and array access\nconst result = data?.find?.(x =&gt; x.id === 1);\nconst first = list?.[0];<\/pre>\n\n<p><b><code>??<\/code> (الحاقِ هیچ‌گرا)<\/b> — مقدار پیش‌فرض فقط برای\nnull/undefined (نه 0 و \"\"):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const volume = 0;\nvolume || 50    // 50 (0 is falsy — WRONG!)\nvolume ?? 50    // 0  (0 is not nullish — correct!)\n\nconst name = null;\nname ?? \"Anonymous\"   // \"Anonymous\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>زنجیر می‌شوند: <code>user?.settings?.volume ?? 50<\/code> — دسترسیِ\nامن با پیش‌فرضِ معقول. این دو عملگر بیشترِ boilerplateِ چکِ null را حذف\nمی‌کنند.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"What does map() return?","options":["The original array","A new transformed array","undefined","A single value"],"answer":1,"explain":"map creates a new array by transforming each element.","fa":{"question":"map() چه برمی‌گرداند؟","options":["آرایهٔ اصلی","یک آرایهٔ تبدیل‌شدهٔ جدید","undefined","یک مقدار واحد"],"explain":"map با تبدیلِ هر عنصر آرایهٔ جدید می‌سازد."}},{"type":"blank","question":"To safely access nested properties without checking each level, use <code>____<\/code> chaining.","answers":["optional","?.","optional chaining"],"explain":"user?.profile?.email — returns undefined instead of crashing.","fa":{"question":"برای دسترسیِ امن به ویژگی‌های تودرتو بدون چکِ هر سطح، از زنجیرهٔ <code>____<\/code> استفاده کن.","explain":"‏user?.profile?.email — به‌جای کرش، undefined برمی‌گرداند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"What's the difference between ?? and ||?","options":["No difference","?? only defaults for null/undefined; || defaults for all falsy values","|| is newer","?? works only with numbers"],"answer":1,"explain":"0 ?? 50 gives 0 (0 isn't nullish); 0 || 50 gives 50 (0 is falsy).","fa":{"question":"فرق ?? با || چیست؟","options":["فرقی ندارد","?? فقط برای null/undefined پیش‌فرض می‌دهد؛ || برای همهٔ مقادیر falsy","|| جدیدتر است","?? فقط با عدد کار می‌کند"],"explain":"‏0 ?? 50 می‌دهد 0 (صفر هیچ‌گرا نیست)؛ 0 || 50 می‌دهد 50 (صفر falsy است)."}},{"type":"mc","question":"In object destructuring, { name: fullName } means:","options":["Access property 'fullName'","Extract 'name' and rename it to 'fullName'","Create a new property","It's invalid syntax"],"answer":1,"explain":"The pattern is { property: newName } — extract and rename in one step.","fa":{"question":"در destructuring شیء، یعنی { name: fullName }:","options":["دسترسی به ویژگی fullName","استخراج name و تغییر نامش به fullName","ساخت ویژگی جدید","نحوِ نامعتبر است"],"explain":"الگو { property: newName } — استخراج و تغییر نام در یک قدم."}}],"title_fa":"آرایه‌ها و شیءها"},{"id":"js05","title":"Advanced JavaScript","emoji":"🎓","lessons":[{"title":"this","html":"\n<p><code>this<\/code> is one of JS's most confusing features. Its value\ndepends on <b>how<\/b> a function is called, not where it's\ndefined:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",\n  greet() { console.log(`Hi, ${this.name}`); },\n};\nuser.greet();        // \"Hi, Ada\" — this = user\n\n// the same function, different context!\nconst greeting = user.greet;\ngreeting();          // \"Hi, undefined\" — this = global/undefined<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>Method call<\/b> (<code>obj.fn()<\/code>) — <code>this<\/code> = the\nobject before the dot<\/li>\n<li><b>Standalone call<\/b> (<code>fn()<\/code>) — <code>this<\/code> =\nundefined (strict) or global<\/li>\n<li><b>Arrow function<\/b> — <code>this<\/code> = inherited from the\nenclosing scope (no own <code>this<\/code>)<\/li>\n<li><b>new<\/b> — <code>this<\/code> = the newly created object<\/li>\n<li><b>call/apply/bind<\/b> — explicitly set <code>this<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// arrow functions inherit this — perfect for callbacks\nconst timer = {\n  seconds: 0,\n  start() {\n    setInterval(() =&gt; {\n      this.seconds++;    // this = timer (arrow inherits from start)\n      console.log(this.seconds);\n    }, 1000);\n  },\n};<\/pre>\n","tryit":"const team = {\n  name: \"Web Dev\",\n  members: [\"Ada\", \"Grace\"],\n  // regular method: this = team\n  printMembers() {\n    // arrow function inherits this from printMembers\n    this.members.forEach(member => {\n      console.log(`${member} is part of ${this.name}`);\n    });\n  },\n  // the classic bug: using a regular function inside\n  printMembersBroken() {\n    this.members.forEach(function(member) {\n      // 'this' is undefined here — NOT team!\n      console.log(`${member} is part of ${this?.name ?? \"?\"}`);\n    });\n  },\n};\n\nteam.printMembers();\nconsole.log(\"---\");\nteam.printMembersBroken();\n\n// call() and bind() — explicit this control\nfunction introduce(city) {\n  return `I'm ${this.name} from ${city}`;\n}\nconst person = { name: \"Ada\" };\nconsole.log(introduce.call(person, \"London\"));\nconsole.log(introduce.bind(person)(\"Paris\"));\n","title_fa":"this","html_fa":"\n<p><code>this<\/code> یکی از گیج‌کننده‌ترین قابلیت‌های JS است. مقدارش به\n<b>نحوهٔ فراخوانیِ<\/b> تابع بستگی دارد، نه محلِ تعریفش:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",\n  greet() { console.log(`Hi, ${this.name}`); },\n};\nuser.greet();        // \"Hi, Ada\" — this = user\n\n// the same function, different context!\nconst greeting = user.greet;\ngreeting();          // \"Hi, undefined\" — this = global/undefined<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>فراخوانی متد<\/b> (<code>obj.fn()<\/code>) — <code>this<\/code> =\nشیءِ قبلِ نقطه<\/li>\n<li><b>فراخوانی تنها<\/b> (<code>fn()<\/code>) — <code>this<\/code> =\nundefined (در strict) یا global<\/li>\n<li><b>تابع پیکانی<\/b> — <code>this<\/code> = از scope در بر گیرنده به\nارث (this خودش را ندارد)<\/li>\n<li><b>new<\/b> — <code>this<\/code> = شیءِ تازه‌ساخته<\/li>\n<li><b>call/apply/bind<\/b> — صریح this را ست کن<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// arrow functions inherit this — perfect for callbacks\nconst timer = {\n  seconds: 0,\n  start() {\n    setInterval(() =&gt; {\n      this.seconds++;    // this = timer (arrow inherits from start)\n      console.log(this.seconds);\n    }, 1000);\n  },\n};<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Prototypes & Prototype Chain","html":"\n<p>JavaScript uses <b>prototypes<\/b> for inheritance — every object has\na hidden link to a prototype object. When you access a property that\ndoesn't exist on the object, JS looks up the <b>prototype chain<\/b>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const animal = {\n  eat() { return \"eating...\"; },\n};\n\nconst dog = Object.create(animal);  // dog's prototype = animal\ndog.bark = () =&gt; \"woof!\";\n\ndog.bark();   // \"woof!\" — own property\ndog.eat();    // \"eating...\" — found on prototype!\n\n// the chain: dog → animal → Object.prototype → null<\/pre>\n\n<p>When you call <code>dog.eat()<\/code>:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Is <code>eat<\/code> on <code>dog<\/code> itself? No<\/li>\n<li>Is it on <code>dog<\/code>'s prototype (<code>animal<\/code>)? Yes! Call it<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<p>Built-in methods like <code>array.map()<\/code> work this way — they\nlive on <code>Array.prototype<\/code>, and every array inherits from\nit. That's why you can call <code>map<\/code> on any array without\ndefining it.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const vehicle = {\n  start() { return \"starting engine...\"; },\n  wheels: 4,\n};\n\nconst car = Object.create(vehicle);\ncar.brand = \"Tesla\";\ncar.drive = function() {\n  return `${this.brand} — ${this.start()}`;\n};\n\nconsole.log(car.drive());    // \"Tesla — starting engine...\"\nconsole.log(car.wheels);     // 4 (inherited from vehicle)\nconsole.log(Object.getPrototypeOf(car) === vehicle);  // true\n\n// the prototype chain\nconsole.log(Object.getPrototypeOf(Object.getPrototypeOf(\n  Object.getPrototypeOf(car))) === null);  // true — chain ends at null\n\n// method lookup: own first, then prototype\nvehicle.start = function() { return \"vroom!\"; };\nconsole.log(car.start());   // \"vroom!\" — prototype was modified!\n","title_fa":"prototypeها و زنجیرهٔ prototype","html_fa":"\n<p>جاوااسکریپت برای وراثت از <b>prototype<\/b> استفاده می‌کند — هر\nشیء پیوندی پنهان به یک شیءِ prototype دارد. وقتی به ویژگی‌ای می‌رسی\nکه روی خودِ شیء نیست، JS <b>زنجیرهٔ prototype<\/b> را بالا\nمی‌رود:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const animal = {\n  eat() { return \"eating...\"; },\n};\n\nconst dog = Object.create(animal);  // dog's prototype = animal\ndog.bark = () =&gt; \"woof!\";\n\ndog.bark();   // \"woof!\" — own property\ndog.eat();    // \"eating...\" — found on prototype!\n\n// the chain: dog → animal → Object.prototype → null<\/pre>\n\n<p>وقتی <code>dog.eat()<\/code> را صدا می‌زنی:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>آیا <code>eat<\/code> روی خودِ <code>dog<\/code> هست؟ نه<\/li>\n<li>روی prototypeِ <code>dog<\/code> (یعنی <code>animal<\/code>) هست؟\nبله! صدا بزن<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<p>متدهای داخلی مثل <code>array.map()<\/code> همین‌طور کار می‌کنند — روی\n<code>Array.prototype<\/code> زندگی می‌کنند و هر آرایه‌ای از آن‌ها به ارث\nمی‌رسد.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Constructor Functions","html":"\n<p>Before classes existed, <b>constructor functions<\/b> were how you\ncreated multiple objects with shared behaviour. They're still used in\nolder code and explain what classes do under the hood:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function Person(name, age) {\n  // 'new' creates {} and sets 'this' to it\n  this.name = name;\n  this.age = age;\n}\n\n// methods go on the prototype (shared across all instances!)\nPerson.prototype.greet = function() {\n  return `Hi, I'm ${this.name}`;\n};\n\nconst ada = new Person(\"Ada\", 36);\nconst grace = new Person(\"Grace\", 45);\n\nconsole.log(ada.greet());   // \"Hi, I'm Ada\"\nconsole.log(ada instanceof Person);  // true\n\n// shared method — both instances use the SAME function\nconsole.log(ada.greet === grace.greet);  // true (on prototype!)<\/pre>\n\n<p>The <code>new<\/code> keyword does 4 things:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Creates an empty object <code>{}<\/code><\/li>\n<li>Sets its prototype to <code>Person.prototype<\/code><\/li>\n<li>Calls the function with <code>this<\/code> = the new object<\/li>\n<li>Returns the object (unless the function returns its own object)<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n","tryit":"function Animal(name, sound) {\n  this.name = name;\n  this.sound = sound;\n}\n\nAnimal.prototype.speak = function() {\n  return `${this.name} says ${this.sound}`;\n};\n\nAnimal.prototype.info = function() {\n  return `${this.name} (${this.constructor.name})`;\n};\n\nconst cat = new Animal(\"Whiskers\", \"meow\");\nconst dog = new Animal(\"Rex\", \"woof\");\n\nconsole.log(cat.speak());  // \"Whiskers says meow\"\nconsole.log(dog.speak());  // \"Rex says woof\"\nconsole.log(dog.info());   // \"Rex (Animal)\"\n\n// both share the same speak function (on prototype)\nconsole.log(cat.speak === dog.speak);  // true\n\n// adding to prototype later affects ALL instances\nAnimal.prototype.describe = function() {\n  return `${this.name} is an animal that says ${this.sound}`;\n};\nconsole.log(cat.describe());\n","title_fa":"توابع سازنده","html_fa":"\n<p>قبل از کلاس‌ها، <b>توابع سازنده<\/b> راهِ ساختِ چند شیء با رفتارِ\nمشترک بودند. هنوز در کدهای قدیمی دیده می‌شوند و توضیح می‌دهند که\nکلاسها زیرِ کاپوت چه می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">function Person(name, age) {\n  // 'new' creates {} and sets 'this' to it\n  this.name = name;\n  this.age = age;\n}\n\n// methods go on the prototype (shared across all instances!)\nPerson.prototype.greet = function() {\n  return `Hi, I'm ${this.name}`;\n};\n\nconst ada = new Person(\"Ada\", 36);\nconst grace = new Person(\"Grace\", 45);\n\nconsole.log(ada.greet());   // \"Hi, I'm Ada\"\nconsole.log(ada instanceof Person);  // true\n\n// shared method — both instances use the SAME function\nconsole.log(ada.greet === grace.greet);  // true (on prototype!)<\/pre>\n\n<p>کلیدواژهٔ <code>new<\/code> چهار کار می‌کند:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>شیءِ خالیِ <code>{}<\/code> می‌سازد<\/li>\n<li>prototypeش را روی <code>Person.prototype<\/code> می‌گذارد<\/li>\n<li>تابع را با <code>this<\/code> = شیءِ جدید صدا می‌زند<\/li>\n<li>شیء را برمی‌گرداند (مگر تابع خودش شیء برگرداند)<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n"},{"title":"Classes","html":"\n<p><b>Classes<\/b> (ES6/ES2015) are syntactic sugar over constructor\nfunctions + prototypes — but cleaner and less error-prone:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Animal {\n  constructor(name, sound) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.sound = sound;\n  }\n\n  speak() {\n    return `${this.name} says ${this.sound}`;\n  }\n\n  static compare(a, b) {       // static: called on the CLASS\n    return a.name.localeCompare(b.name);\n  }\n}\n\nconst cat = new Animal(\"Whiskers\", \"meow\");\nconsole.log(cat.speak());\nconsole.log(Animal.compare(cat, new Animal(\"Rex\", \"woof\")));<\/pre>\n\n<p>Everything a constructor function does, a class does — but with\nenforced <code>new<\/code> (calling without <code>new<\/code> throws),\ncleaner method syntax, and support for <code>extends<\/code>,\n<code>super<\/code>, <code>static<\/code>, and private fields.<\/p>\n\n<p>Under the hood, it's still prototypes. <code>class<\/code> is\nsyntactic sugar — but it's very good sugar.<\/p>\n","tryit":"class BankAccount {\n  #balance = 0;         // private field (next lesson covers this deeply)\n\n  constructor(owner, initial = 0) {\n    this.owner = owner;\n    this.#balance = initial;\n  }\n\n  deposit(amount) {\n    this.#balance += amount;\n    return this;        // return this for chaining!\n  }\n\n  withdraw(amount) {\n    if (amount > this.#balance) throw new Error(\"Insufficient funds\");\n    this.#balance -= amount;\n    return this;\n  }\n\n  get balance() {       // getter\n    return this.#balance;\n  }\n\n  static printAll(...accounts) {\n    accounts.forEach(a => console.log(`${a.owner}: ${a.balance}`));\n  }\n}\n\nconst acct1 = new BankAccount(\"Ada\", 100);\nconst acct2 = new BankAccount(\"Grace\", 250);\n\nacct1.deposit(50).withdraw(30);   // method chaining!\nconsole.log(acct1.balance);        // 120\n\nBankAccount.printAll(acct1, acct2);\n","title_fa":"کلاس‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>کلاس‌ها<\/b> (ES6/2015) شکرِ نحوی روی توابع سازنده + prototypeها\nهستند — اما تمیزتر و کم‌خطاتر:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Animal {\n  constructor(name, sound) {\n    this.name = name;\n    this.sound = sound;\n  }\n\n  speak() {\n    return `${this.name} says ${this.sound}`;\n  }\n\n  static compare(a, b) {       // static: called on the CLASS\n    return a.name.localeCompare(b.name);\n  }\n}\n\nconst cat = new Animal(\"Whiskers\", \"meow\");\nconsole.log(cat.speak());\nconsole.log(Animal.compare(cat, new Animal(\"Rex\", \"woof\")));<\/pre>\n\n<p>هر کاری که تابع سازنده می‌کند، کلاس هم می‌کند — اما با\n<code>new<\/code> اجباری (بدون new خطا می‌دهد)، نحوِ تمیزِ متد و\nپشتیبانی از <code>extends<\/code>، <code>super<\/code>،\n<code>static<\/code> و فیلدهای خصوصی.<\/p>\n\n<p>زیرِ کاپوت هنوز prototype است. <code>class<\/code> شکرِ نحوی است —\nاما شکرِ خیلی خوبی است.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Inheritance","html":"\n<p><b>Inheritance<\/b> lets a class build on another class using\n<code>extends<\/code> and <code>super<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Animal {\n  constructor(name) {\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n  eat() {\n    return `${this.name} is eating`;\n  }\n  describe() {\n    return `${this.name} is an animal`;\n  }\n}\n\nclass Dog extends Animal {\n  constructor(name, breed) {\n    super(name);            // call parent's constructor (REQUIRED)\n    this.breed = breed;\n  }\n  speak() {\n    return `${this.name} says woof!`;\n  }\n  // override parent method\n  describe() {\n    return `${super.describe()} — specifically a ${this.breed}`;\n  }\n}\n\nconst dog = new Dog(\"Rex\", \"Golden Retriever\");\ndog.eat();        // inherited from Animal\ndog.speak();      // own method\ndog.describe();   // overridden — uses super.describe()<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>super()<\/code> must be called before using <code>this<\/code>\nin the constructor. <code>super.method()<\/code> calls the parent's\nversion. The <b>prototype chain<\/b> is set up automatically:\n<code>dog<\/code> → <code>Dog.prototype<\/code> →\n<code>Animal.prototype<\/code> → <code>Object.prototype<\/code>.<\/p>\n","tryit":"class Shape {\n  constructor(color = \"black\") {\n    this.color = color;\n  }\n  area() {\n    return 0;\n  }\n  describe() {\n    return `A ${this.color} shape with area ${this.area().toFixed(2)}`;\n  }\n}\n\nclass Circle extends Shape {\n  constructor(radius, color) {\n    super(color);\n    this.radius = radius;\n  }\n  area() { return Math.PI * this.radius ** 2; }\n}\n\nclass Rectangle extends Shape {\n  constructor(width, height, color) {\n    super(color);\n    this.width = width;\n    this.height = height;\n  }\n  area() { return this.width * this.height; }\n}\n\nconst shapes = [\n  new Circle(5, \"blue\"),\n  new Rectangle(4, 6, \"red\"),\n  new Circle(2, \"green\"),\n];\n\nshapes.forEach(s => console.log(s.describe()));\n","title_fa":"وراثت","html_fa":"\n<p><b>وراثت<\/b> با <code>extends<\/code> و <code>super<\/code> به کلاسی\nاجازه می‌دهد روی کلاس دیگری بنا شود:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Animal {\n  constructor(name) {\n    this.name = name;\n  }\n  eat() {\n    return `${this.name} is eating`;\n  }\n  describe() {\n    return `${this.name} is an animal`;\n  }\n}\n\nclass Dog extends Animal {\n  constructor(name, breed) {\n    super(name);            // call parent's constructor (REQUIRED)\n    this.breed = breed;\n  }\n  speak() {\n    return `${this.name} says woof!`;\n  }\n  // override parent method\n  describe() {\n    return `${super.describe()} — specifically a ${this.breed}`;\n  }\n}\n\nconst dog = new Dog(\"Rex\", \"Golden Retriever\");\ndog.eat();        // inherited from Animal\ndog.speak();      // own method\ndog.describe();   // overridden — uses super.describe()<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>super()<\/code> باید قبل از استفاده از <code>this<\/code> در\nسازنده صدا زده شود. <code>super.method()<\/code> نسخهٔ والد را صدا\nمی‌زند. <b>زنجیرهٔ prototype<\/b> خودکار ساخته می‌شود:\n<code>dog<\/code> → <code>Dog.prototype<\/code> →\n<code>Animal.prototype<\/code> → <code>Object.prototype<\/code>.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Getters, Setters & Private Fields","html":"\n<p><b>Getters<\/b> and <b>setters<\/b> look like properties but run code.\n<b>Private fields<\/b> (prefixed with <code>#<\/code>) are truly\ninvisible from outside the class:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Temperature {\n  #celsius = 0;              // private — invisible outside!\n\n  get celsius() {\n    return this.#celsius;\n  }\n\n  set celsius(value) {\n    if (value &lt; -273.15) {\n      throw new Error(\"Below absolute zero!\");\n    }\n    this.#celsius = value;\n  }\n\n  get fahrenheit() {         // computed getter\n    return this.#celsius * 9 / 5 + 32;\n  }\n\n  set fahrenheit(value) {\n    this.#celsius = (value - 32) * 5 / 9;\n  }\n}\n\nconst temp = new Temperature();\ntemp.celsius = 25;           // calls the setter\nconsole.log(temp.fahrenheit); // 77 — computed getter\n// temp.#celsius              // SyntaxError — truly private!<\/pre>\n\n<p>Private fields with <code>#<\/code> are enforced by the language —\nunlike the old underscore convention (<code>_private<\/code>) which was\njust a naming hint. They can't be accessed, enumerated, or seen in\nJSON.<\/p>\n","tryit":"class SecureStore {\n  #data = new Map();\n  #accessLog = [];\n\n  set(key, value) {\n    this.#data.set(key, value);\n    this.#accessLog.push(`SET ${key}`);\n    return this;\n  }\n\n  get(key) {\n    this.#accessLog.push(`GET ${key}`);\n    return this.#data.get(key);\n  }\n\n  // read-only access to the log\n  get log() {\n    return [...this.#accessLog];  // return a copy!\n  }\n\n  // computed property\n  get size() {\n    return this.#data.size;\n  }\n}\n\nconst store = new SecureStore();\nstore.set(\"name\", \"Ada\").set(\"role\", \"admin\");\nconsole.log(store.get(\"name\"));  // \"Ada\"\nconsole.log(store.size);         // 2\nconsole.log(store.log);          // [\"SET name\", \"SET role\", \"GET name\"]\n// store.#data                   // SyntaxError!\n","title_fa":"getter، setter و فیلدهای خصوصی","html_fa":"\n<p><b>getterها<\/b> و <b>setterها<\/b> شبیه ویژگی به نظر می‌رسند اما کد\nاجرا می‌کنند. <b>فیلدهای خصوصی<\/b> (با پیشوند <code>#<\/code>) واقعاً از\nبیرون کلاس نامرئی‌اند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class Temperature {\n  #celsius = 0;              // private — invisible outside!\n\n  get celsius() {\n    return this.#celsius;\n  }\n\n  set celsius(value) {\n    if (value &lt; -273.15) {\n      throw new Error(\"Below absolute zero!\");\n    }\n    this.#celsius = value;\n  }\n\n  get fahrenheit() {         // computed getter\n    return this.#celsius * 9 / 5 + 32;\n  }\n\n  set fahrenheit(value) {\n    this.#celsius = (value - 32) * 5 / 9;\n  }\n}\n\nconst temp = new Temperature();\ntemp.celsius = 25;           // calls the setter\nconsole.log(temp.fahrenheit); // 77 — computed getter\n// temp.#celsius              // SyntaxError — truly private!<\/pre>\n\n<p>فیلدهای خصوصی با <code>#<\/code> توسط خودِ زبان اجبار می‌شوند —\nبرخلاف قراردادِ قدیمیِ زیرخط (<code>_private<\/code>) که فقط نامی\nراهنما بود. نه قابل دسترس‌اند، نه قابل شمارش، نه در JSON دیده\nمی‌شوند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Static Members & Symbols","html":"\n<p><b>Static members<\/b> belong to the class itself, not to instances\n— they're utility methods and properties:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class MathHelper {\n  static PI = 3.14159;         // static property\n\n  static circleArea(r) {       // static method\n    return this.PI * r ** 2;   // 'this' = the class itself\n  }\n\n  static clamp(value, min, max) {\n    return Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max);\n  }\n}\n\n// called on the CLASS, not instances\nconsole.log(MathHelper.PI);             // 3.14159\nconsole.log(MathHelper.circleArea(2));  // 12.57\nconsole.log(MathHelper.clamp(15, 0, 10)); // 10\n\n// const m = new MathHelper();  // not useful — no constructor<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Symbols<\/b> create unique identifiers that never collide — even\ntwo symbols with the same description are different:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const id1 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconst id2 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconsole.log(id1 === id2);    // false — always unique!\n\n// use as object keys (hidden from for...in and JSON)\nconst user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",\n  [id1]: 12345,             // symbol key\n};\nconsole.log(user[id1]);      // 12345\nconsole.log(Object.keys(user)); // [\"name\"] — symbol is invisible!\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user)); // {\"name\":\"Ada\"}<\/pre>\n\n<p>Symbols are used for metaprogramming\n(<code>Symbol.iterator<\/code>, <code>Symbol.toStringTag<\/code>) and\nadding \"hidden\" properties to objects that won't interfere with other\ncode.<\/p>\n","tryit":"class Vector {\n  static ZERO = new Vector(0, 0);\n  static #instanceCount = 0;\n\n  constructor(x, y) {\n    this.x = x;\n    this.y = y;\n    Vector.#instanceCount++;\n  }\n\n  static get instanceCount() {\n    return Vector.#instanceCount;\n  }\n\n  static add(a, b) {\n    return new Vector(a.x + b.x, a.y + b.y);\n  }\n\n  toString() {\n    return `Vector(${this.x}, ${this.y})`;\n  }\n}\n\nconst v1 = new Vector(1, 2);\nconst v2 = new Vector(3, 4);\nconst v3 = Vector.add(v1, v2);\nconsole.log(v3.toString());        // \"Vector(4, 6)\"\nconsole.log(Vector.instanceCount); // 3\nconsole.log(Vector.ZERO.toString()); // \"Vector(0, 0)\"\n\n// Symbols: unique keys\nconst SECRET = Symbol(\"secret\");\nconst obj = { name: \"app\", [SECRET]: \"hidden value\" };\nconsole.log(obj[SECRET]);         // \"hidden value\"\nconsole.log(Object.keys(obj));   // [\"name\"] — symbol invisible!\n","title_fa":"اعضای static و symbolها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>اعضای static<\/b> مالِ خودِ کلاس‌اند نه نمونه‌ها — متدها و\nویژگی‌های کاربردی:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class MathHelper {\n  static PI = 3.14159;         // static property\n\n  static circleArea(r) {       // static method\n    return this.PI * r ** 2;   // 'this' = the class itself\n  }\n\n  static clamp(value, min, max) {\n    return Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max);\n  }\n}\n\n// called on the CLASS, not instances\nconsole.log(MathHelper.PI);             // 3.14159\nconsole.log(MathHelper.circleArea(2));  // 12.57\nconsole.log(MathHelper.clamp(15, 0, 10)); // 10\n\n// const m = new MathHelper();  // not useful — no constructor<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>symbolها<\/b> شناسه‌های یکتا می‌سازند که هرگز تصادم نمی‌کنند — حتی\nدو symbol با توضیحِ یکسان متفاوت‌اند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const id1 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconst id2 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconsole.log(id1 === id2);    // false — always unique!\n\n// use as object keys (hidden from for...in and JSON)\nconst user = {\n  name: \"Ada\",\n  [id1]: 12345,             // symbol key\n};\nconsole.log(user[id1]);      // 12345\nconsole.log(Object.keys(user)); // [\"name\"] — symbol is invisible!\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user)); // {\"name\":\"Ada\"}<\/pre>\n\n<p>symbolها برای فرaprogramming\n(<code>Symbol.iterator<\/code>، <code>Symbol.toStringTag<\/code>) و\nافزودن ویژگی‌های «پنهان» به شیءها که با کد دیگر تداخل نکنند استفاده\nمی‌شوند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Iterators & Generators","html":"\n<p><b>Iterators<\/b> are objects with a <code>next()<\/code> method that\nreturns <code>{ value, done }<\/code>. <b>Generators<\/b>\n(<code>function*<\/code>) create iterators with the <code>yield<\/code>\nkeyword — they can pause and resume:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// generator: lazy, pausable sequence\nfunction* countdown(from) {\n  while (from &gt; 0) {\n    yield from;     // pause here, return 'from'\n    from--;\n  }\n}\n\nconst counter = countdown(3);\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 3, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 2, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 1, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: undefined, done: true }\n\n// for...of consumes generators\nfor (const n of countdown(3)) {\n  console.log(n);     // 3 2 1\n}\n\n// infinite generator (lazy — only computes when asked)\nfunction* fibonacci() {\n  let [a, b] = [0, 1];\n  while (true) {\n    yield a;\n    [a, b] = [b, a + b];\n  }\n}\n\nconst fib = fibonacci();\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 0\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 1\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 1\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 2<\/pre>\n\n<p>Generators are memory-efficient (lazy evaluation), can represent\ninfinite sequences, and enable custom iteration protocols. Any object\nwith a <code>[Symbol.iterator]<\/code> method is iterable and works with\n<code>for...of<\/code>, spread, and destructuring.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// generator for paginated data\nfunction* pageGenerator(items, pageSize) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += pageSize) {\n    yield items.slice(i, i + pageSize);\n  }\n}\n\nconst data = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\", \"f\", \"g\"];\nconst pages = pageGenerator(data, 3);\n\nconsole.log(pages.next().value);  // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nconsole.log(pages.next().value);  // [\"d\", \"e\", \"f\"]\nconsole.log(pages.next().value);  // [\"g\"]\nconsole.log(pages.next().done);   // true\n\n// generator with delegation (yield*)\nfunction* innerGen() {\n  yield 2;\n  yield 3;\n}\n\nfunction* outerGen() {\n  yield 1;\n  yield* innerGen();  // delegate to another generator\n  yield 4;\n}\n\nconsole.log([...outerGen()]);  // [1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n// custom iterable object\nconst range = {\n  from: 1, to: 5,\n  *[Symbol.iterator]() {\n    for (let i = this.from; i <= this.to; i++) yield i;\n  },\n};\nconsole.log([...range]);  // [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n","title_fa":"iteratorها و generatorها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>iteratorها<\/b> شیءهایی با متد <code>next()<\/code> هستند که\n<code>{ value, done }<\/code> برمی‌گردانند. <b>generatorها<\/b>\n(<code>function*<\/code>) با کلیدواژهٔ <code>yield<\/code> iterator\nمی‌سازند — می‌توانند مکث و ادامه دهند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// generator: lazy, pausable sequence\nfunction* countdown(from) {\n  while (from &gt; 0) {\n    yield from;     // pause here, return 'from'\n    from--;\n  }\n}\n\nconst counter = countdown(3);\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 3, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 2, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: 1, done: false }\nconsole.log(counter.next());  // { value: undefined, done: true }\n\n// for...of consumes generators\nfor (const n of countdown(3)) {\n  console.log(n);     // 3 2 1\n}\n\n// infinite generator (lazy — only computes when asked)\nfunction* fibonacci() {\n  let [a, b] = [0, 1];\n  while (true) {\n    yield a;\n    [a, b] = [b, a + b];\n  }\n}\n\nconst fib = fibonacci();\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 0\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 1\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 1\nconsole.log(fib.next().value);  // 2<\/pre>\n\n<p>generatorها بهره‌حافظه‌ای اند (ارزیابیِ تنبل)، می‌توانند دنباله‌های\nبی‌نهایت را نمایندگی کنند و پروتکل تکرارِ سفارشی را ممکن می‌کنند. هر\nشیءی با متد <code>[Symbol.iterator]<\/code> قابلِ تکرار است و با\n<code>for...of<\/code>، spread و destructuring کار می‌کند.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"In an arrow function inside a method, 'this' refers to:","options":["The arrow function itself","The global object","The enclosing scope's this","undefined"],"answer":2,"explain":"Arrow functions inherit this from their enclosing lexical scope.","fa":{"question":"در یک تابع پیکانی داخل متد، this به چه اشاره دارد؟","options":["خودِ تابع پیکانی","شیءِ سراسری","this محیطِ دربرگیرنده","undefined"],"explain":"توابع پیکانی this را از scope واژگانیِ اطراف به ارث می‌برند."}},{"type":"blank","question":"Private class fields are prefixed with ____.","answers":["#","hash"],"explain":"#balance is truly private — inaccessible from outside the class.","fa":{"question":"فیلدهای خصوصیِ کلاس با ____ پیشوند می‌گیرند.","explain":"‏#balance واقعاً خصوصی است — از بیرون کلاس دسترس‌ناپذیر."}},{"type":"mc","question":"A generator function is declared with:","options":["function gen()","function* gen()","async function gen()","gen = () => yield"],"answer":1,"explain":"function* marks a generator; yield pauses and resumes execution.","fa":{"question":"تابع generator با چه چیزی اعلام می‌شود؟","options":["function gen()","function* gen()","async function gen()","gen = () => yield"],"explain":"function* یعنی generator؛ yield اجرا را مکث و ادامه می‌دهد."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Static members belong to:","options":["Each instance","The class itself","The prototype","The module"],"answer":1,"explain":"Static members are called on the class: MathHelper.clamp(...)","fa":{"question":"اعضای static متعلق به:","options":["هر نمونه","خودِ کلاس","prototype","ماژول"],"explain":"اعضای static روی کلاس صدا زده می‌شوند: MathHelper.clamp(...)"}}],"title_fa":"جاوااسکریپت پیشرفته"},{"id":"js06","title":"Built-in Objects","emoji":"🧰","lessons":[{"title":"Object & Array Globals","html":"\n<p>The <code>Object<\/code> and <code>Array<\/code> global objects provide\nstatic utility methods:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// Object static methods\nObject.keys({a: 1, b: 2})          // [\"a\", \"b\"]\nObject.values({a: 1, b: 2})        // [1, 2]\nObject.entries({a: 1, b: 2})       // [[\"a\",1],[\"b\",2]]\nObject.assign({}, {a: 1}, {b: 2}) // merge\nObject.freeze({a: 1})              // make immutable\n\n// Array static methods\nArray.isArray([])                   // true\nArray.from(\"abc\")                   // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nArray.from({length: 3}, (_, i) =&gt; i * 10)  // [0, 10, 20]\nArray.of(1, 2, 3)                   // [1, 2, 3]<\/pre>\n\n<p>Array instance methods you should know:\n<code>at(-1)<\/code> (last element), <code>flat()<\/code>,\n<code>flatMap()<\/code>, <code>includes()<\/code>,\n<code>indexOf()<\/code>, <code>fill()<\/code>, <code>reverse()<\/code>,\n<code>splice()<\/code> (mutates!).<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Object utilities\nconst user = { name: \"Ada\", age: 36, role: \"admin\" };\nconsole.log(Object.keys(user));\nconsole.log(Object.entries(user).map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${v}`));\n\n// frozen object — mutations are silently ignored\nconst frozen = Object.freeze({ x: 1 });\nfrozen.x = 99;\nconsole.log(frozen.x);  // still 1\n\n// Array.from with a mapping function\nconst grid = Array.from({ length: 3 }, (_, i) => `row-${i + 1}`);\nconsole.log(grid);\n\n// at() — negative indexing\nconst arr = [10, 20, 30, 40];\nconsole.log(arr.at(-1));  // 40\nconsole.log(arr.at(-2));  // 30\n","title_fa":"ابزارهای سراسری Object و Array","html_fa":"\n<p>شیءهای سراسری <code>Object<\/code> و <code>Array<\/code> متدهای\nکاربردیِ static می‌دهند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// Object static methods\nObject.keys({a: 1, b: 2})          // [\"a\", \"b\"]\nObject.values({a: 1, b: 2})        // [1, 2]\nObject.entries({a: 1, b: 2})       // [[\"a\",1],[\"b\",2]]\nObject.assign({}, {a: 1}, {b: 2}) // merge\nObject.freeze({a: 1})              // make immutable\n\n// Array static methods\nArray.isArray([])                   // true\nArray.from(\"abc\")                   // [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\nArray.from({length: 3}, (_, i) =&gt; i * 10)  // [0, 10, 20]\nArray.of(1, 2, 3)                   // [1, 2, 3]<\/pre>\n\n<p>متدهای نمونهٔ آرایه که باید بشناسی:\n<code>at(-1)<\/code> (آخرین عنصر)، <code>flat()<\/code>،\n<code>flatMap()<\/code>، <code>includes()<\/code>،\n<code>indexOf()<\/code>، <code>fill()<\/code>، <code>reverse()<\/code> و\n<code>splice()<\/code> (تغییر می‌دهد!).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"String & Number Globals","html":"\n<p><code>String<\/code> and <code>Number<\/code> global objects provide\nconversion and utility methods:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// String static\nString(42)              // \"42\"\nString.fromCharCode(72, 105)  // \"Hi\"\n\n// String instance\n\"  hello  \".trimStart()  // \"hello  \"\n\"hello\".padStart(8, \"*\") // \"***hello\"\n\"hello\".repeat(3)         // \"hellohellohello\"\n\"hello\".replaceAll(\"l\", \"L\") // \"heLLo\"\n\"hello\".at(-1)           // \"o\"\n\n// Number static\nNumber.isInteger(42)     // true\nNumber.isNaN(NaN)        // true (safer than global isNaN)\nNumber.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER  // 9007199254740991\nNumber.EPSILON           // 2.220446049250313e-16\n(42).toString(2)         // \"101010\" (binary)\n(255).toString(16)       // \"ff\" (hexadecimal)<\/pre>\n","tryit":"// String tricks\nconsole.log(\"5\".padStart(3, \"0\"));     // \"005\"\nconsole.log(\"Hello\".repeat(3));        // \"HelloHelloHello\"\nconsole.log(\"a-b-c\".replaceAll(\"-\", \"_\"));\nconsole.log([...\"hello\"].reverse().join(\"\")); // \"olleh\"\n\n// Number formatting\nconst price = 1234.567;\nconsole.log(price.toFixed(2));          // \"1234.57\"\nconsole.log(price.toLocaleString(\"en\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"USD\" }));\nconsole.log((255).toString(16));        // \"ff\"\nconsole.log(Number.parseInt(\"0x1A\", 16)); // 26\n\n// Number.isNaN vs global isNaN\nconsole.log(Number.isNaN(NaN));        // true (reliable)\nconsole.log(Number.isNaN(\"abc\"));      // false (not a NaN number)\n","title_fa":"ابزارهای سراسری String و Number","html_fa":"\n<p>شیءهای سراسری <code>String<\/code> و <code>Number<\/code> متدهای\nتبدیل و کاربردی می‌دهند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// String static\nString(42)              // \"42\"\nString.fromCharCode(72, 105)  // \"Hi\"\n\n// String instance\n\"  hello  \".trimStart()  // \"hello  \"\n\"hello\".padStart(8, \"*\") // \"***hello\"\n\"hello\".repeat(3)         // \"hellohellohello\"\n\"hello\".replaceAll(\"l\", \"L\") // \"heLLo\"\n\"hello\".at(-1)           // \"o\"\n\n// Number static\nNumber.isInteger(42)     // true\nNumber.isNaN(NaN)        // true (safer than global isNaN)\nNumber.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER  // 9007199254740991\nNumber.EPSILON           // 2.220446049250313e-16\n(42).toString(2)         // \"101010\" (binary)\n(255).toString(16)       // \"ff\" (hexadecimal)<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Math","html":"\n<p>The <code>Math<\/code> object provides mathematical constants and\nfunctions — always available, never instantiated:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">Math.PI                 // 3.14159...\nMath.E                  // 2.718...\nMath.abs(-5)            // 5\nMath.round(4.7)         // 5 (nearest)\nMath.floor(4.7)         // 4 (down)\nMath.ceil(4.2)          // 5 (up)\nMath.trunc(4.7)         // 4 (truncate decimal)\nMath.max(1, 5, 3)       // 5\nMath.min(1, 5, 3)       // 1\nMath.pow(2, 10)         // 1024\nMath.sqrt(16)           // 4\nMath.random()           // [0, 1)\nMath.sign(-3)           // -1<\/pre>\n\n<p>Common patterns:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// random integer between min and max (inclusive)\nconst random = (min, max) =&gt; Math.floor(Math.random() * (max - min + 1)) + min;\n\n// random element from array\nconst pick = arr =&gt; arr[Math.floor(Math.random() * arr.length)];<\/pre>\n","tryit":"const random = (min, max) => Math.floor(Math.random() * (max - min + 1)) + min;\n\n// dice roll\nconst die = random(1, 6);\nconsole.log(\"🎲 You rolled:\", die);\n\n// random element\nconst fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\", \"date\"];\nconsole.log(\"random fruit:\", fruits[Math.floor(Math.random() * fruits.length)]);\n\n// rounding comparison\nconst n = 4.7;\nconsole.log(\"round:\", Math.round(n), \"floor:\", Math.floor(n), \"ceil:\", Math.ceil(n));\n\n// clamp with Math\nconst clamp = (val, min, max) => Math.min(Math.max(val, min), max);\nconsole.log(\"clamped:\", clamp(15, 0, 10));  // 10\n\n// Math.hypot — hypotenuse\nconsole.log(\"hypotenuse:\", Math.hypot(3, 4)); // 5\n","title_fa":"Math","html_fa":"\n<p>شیء <code>Math<\/code> ثابت‌ها و توابع ریاضی می‌دهد — همیشه موجود و\nهرگز نمونه‌سازی نمی‌شود:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">Math.PI                 // 3.14159...\nMath.E                  // 2.718...\nMath.abs(-5)            // 5\nMath.round(4.7)         // 5 (nearest)\nMath.floor(4.7)         // 4 (down)\nMath.ceil(4.2)          // 5 (up)\nMath.trunc(4.7)         // 4 (truncate decimal)\nMath.max(1, 5, 3)       // 5\nMath.min(1, 5, 3)       // 1\nMath.pow(2, 10)         // 1024\nMath.sqrt(16)           // 4\nMath.random()           // [0, 1)\nMath.sign(-3)           // -1<\/pre>\n\n<p>الگوهای رایج:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// random integer between min and max (inclusive)\nconst random = (min, max) =&gt; Math.floor(Math.random() * (max - min + 1)) + min;\n\n// random element from array\nconst pick = arr =&gt; arr[Math.floor(Math.random() * arr.length)];<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Date","html":"\n<p>The <code>Date<\/code> object handles dates and times. Months are\n0-indexed (0 = January) — a classic trap!<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const now = new Date();\nconst specific = new Date(2026, 8, 27);     // Sep 27 2026 (month=8!)\nconst parsed = new Date(\"2026-09-27T14:30:00\");\n\nnow.getFullYear()     // 2026\nnow.getMonth()        // 0-11 (add 1!)\nnow.getDate()         // day of month\nnow.getDay()          // day of week (0 = Sunday)\nnow.getHours()\nnow.getTime()         // milliseconds since epoch\nDate.now()            // shortcut for timestamp<\/pre>\n\n<p>Formatting with <code>toLocaleString<\/code> and\n<code>Intl.DateTimeFormat<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">now.toLocaleDateString(\"en\", { weekday: \"long\", year: \"numeric\",\n  month: \"long\", day: \"numeric\" });\n// \"Saturday, September 27, 2026\"<\/pre>\n","tryit":"const now = new Date();\n\n// Date components\nconsole.log(\"Year:\", now.getFullYear());\nconsole.log(\"Month:\", now.getMonth() + 1); // add 1!\nconsole.log(\"Day:\", now.getDate());\nconsole.log(\"Day of week:\", now.getDay()); // 0=Sunday\n\n// formatting\nconsole.log(now.toLocaleDateString(\"en\", {\n  weekday: \"long\", month: \"long\", day: \"numeric\", year: \"numeric\"\n}));\n\n// date arithmetic\nconst tomorrow = new Date(now);\ntomorrow.setDate(now.getDate() + 1);\nconsole.log(\"Tomorrow:\", tomorrow.toLocaleDateString());\n\n// timestamp (ms since epoch)\nconsole.log(\"Timestamp:\", Date.now());\n","title_fa":"Date","html_fa":"\n<p>شیء <code>Date<\/code> تاریخ و زمان را مدیریت می‌کند. ماه‌ها از صفر\nشروع می‌شوند (۰ = ژانویه) — تلهٔ کلاسیک!<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const now = new Date();\nconst specific = new Date(2026, 8, 27);     // Sep 27 2026 (month=8!)\nconst parsed = new Date(\"2026-09-27T14:30:00\");\n\nnow.getFullYear()     // 2026\nnow.getMonth()        // 0-11 (add 1!)\nnow.getDate()         // day of month\nnow.getDay()          // day of week (0 = Sunday)\nnow.getHours()\nnow.getTime()         // milliseconds since epoch\nDate.now()            // shortcut for timestamp<\/pre>\n\n<p>قالب‌بندی با <code>toLocaleString<\/code> و\n<code>Intl.DateTimeFormat<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">now.toLocaleDateString(\"en\", { weekday: \"long\", year: \"numeric\",\n  month: \"long\", day: \"numeric\" });\n// \"Saturday, September 27, 2026\"<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"RegExp","html":"\n<p>Regular expressions match patterns in strings — created with a\nliteral <code>/pattern/flags<\/code> or <code>new RegExp(\"pattern\")<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// test: does the string match?\n/\\d+/.test(\"abc123\")        // true (has digits)\n\n// match: extract matches\n\"hello 42 world 99\".match(/\\d+/g)  // [\"42\", \"99\"]\n\n// replace\n\"hello world\".replace(/o/g, \"0\")   // \"hell0 w0rld\"\n\n// common patterns\n/^\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+$/       // email (simplified)\n/^\\d{3}-\\d{4}$/           // phone: 555-1234\n/^[A-Za-z0-9]+$/           // alphanumeric only\n\n// flags: g=global, i=case-insensitive, m=multiline\n/HELLO/i.test(\"hello\")     // true<\/pre>\n","tryit":"// basic matching\nconst text = \"Contact: ada@example.com or grace@mdn.org\";\nconst emails = text.match(/\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+/g);\nconsole.log(\"emails found:\", emails);\n\n// named capture groups\nconst dateStr = \"2026-09-27\";\nconst { year, month, day } = dateStr.match(\n  /(?<year>\\d{4})-(?<month>\\d{2})-(?<day>\\d{2})/\n).groups;\nconsole.log(`Day: ${day}, Month: ${month}, Year: ${year}`);\n\n// validation patterns\nconst patterns = {\n  email: /^\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+$/,\n  phone: /^\\d{3}-\\d{4}$/,\n  hex: /^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/,\n};\nconsole.log(\"is email:\", patterns.email.test(\"ada@x.io\"));\nconsole.log(\"is phone:\", patterns.phone.test(\"555-1234\"));\nconsole.log(\"is hex:\", patterns.hex.test(\"#1572b6\"));\n\n// replace with capture groups\nconst name = \"Ada Lovelace\";\nconst reversed = name.replace(/(\\w+) (\\w+)/, \"$2, $1\");\nconsole.log(reversed);  // \"Lovelace, Ada\"\n","title_fa":"RegExp","html_fa":"\n<p>عبارات باقاعده در رشته‌ها الگو می‌گیرند — با نگارهٔ\n<code>/الگو/پرچم‌ها<\/code> یا <code>new RegExp(\"الگو\")<\/code>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// test: does the string match?\n/\\d+/.test(\"abc123\")        // true (has digits)\n\n// match: extract matches\n\"hello 42 world 99\".match(/\\d+/g)  // [\"42\", \"99\"]\n\n// replace\n\"hello world\".replace(/o/g, \"0\")   // \"hell0 w0rld\"\n\n// common patterns\n/^\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+$/       // email (simplified)\n/^\\d{3}-\\d{4}$/           // phone: 555-1234\n/^[A-Za-z0-9]+$/           // alphanumeric only\n\n// flags: g=global, i=case-insensitive, m=multiline\n/HELLO/i.test(\"hello\")     // true<\/pre>\n"},{"title":"Map, Set, WeakMap & WeakSet","html":"\n<p><b>Map<\/b> is a key-value store where keys can be ANY type (not just\nstrings like in objects):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const map = new Map();\nmap.set(\"name\", \"Ada\");\nmap.set(42, \"number key\");\nmap.set(true, \"boolean key\");\nmap.get(\"name\")       // \"Ada\"\nmap.has(42)           // true\nmap.size              // 3\nmap.delete(\"name\")\nmap.clear()<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Set<\/b> is a collection of unique values:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const set = new Set([1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 1]);\nset.size              // 3 (duplicates removed!)\nset.add(4);\nset.has(2)            // true\n\n// remove duplicates from array\nconst unique = [...new Set([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3])];  // [1, 2, 3]<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>WeakMap/WeakSet<\/b> — keys must be objects and are held\n<i>weakly<\/i>: if the key object is garbage-collected, the entry\ndisappears automatically. Used for caching and metadata without memory\nleaks.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Map: any type of key\nconst userRoles = new Map();\nuserRoles.set(\"ada\", \"admin\");\nuserRoles.set(42, \"bot\");\nuserRoles.set(true, \"system\");\nconsole.log(userRoles.get(\"ada\"));   // \"admin\"\nconsole.log(userRoles.get(42));      // \"bot\"\n\n// iterate a Map\nfor (const [key, role] of userRoles) {\n  console.log(`${key} → ${role}`);\n}\n\n// Set: deduplicate\nconst tags = [\"js\", \"css\", \"html\", \"js\", \"css\"];\nconst unique = new Set(tags);\nconsole.log(\"unique tags:\", [...unique]);\n\n// Set operations\nconst setA = new Set([1, 2, 3]);\nconst setB = new Set([2, 3, 4]);\nconst intersection = [...setA].filter(x => setB.has(x));\nconsole.log(\"intersection:\", intersection);\n\n// WeakMap for private data\nconst privateData = new WeakMap();\nclass User {\n  constructor(name) { privateData.set(this, { name }); }\n  getName() { return privateData.get(this).name; }\n}\n","title_fa":"Map، Set، WeakMap و WeakSet","html_fa":"\n<p><b>Map<\/b> ذخیرهٔ کلید-مقدار است که کلیدها می‌توانند هر نوعی باشند\n(نه فقط رشته مثل شیءها):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const map = new Map();\nmap.set(\"name\", \"Ada\");\nmap.set(42, \"number key\");\nmap.set(true, \"boolean key\");\nmap.get(\"name\")       // \"Ada\"\nmap.has(42)           // true\nmap.size              // 3\nmap.delete(\"name\")\nmap.clear()<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Set<\/b> مجموعه‌ای از مقدارهای یکتاست:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const set = new Set([1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 1]);\nset.size              // 3 (duplicates removed!)\nset.add(4);\nset.has(2)            // true\n\n// remove duplicates from array\nconst unique = [...new Set([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3])];  // [1, 2, 3]<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>WeakMap/WeakSet<\/b> — کلیدها باید شیء باشند و <i>ضعیف<\/i> نگه\nداشته می‌شوند: اگر شیءِ کلید garbage-collect شود، ورودی خودکار حذف\nمی‌شود. برای کش و فراداده بدون نشتِ حافظه.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"JSON","html":"\n<p><b>JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)<\/b> is the universal data\nformat for APIs. Two methods do everything:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// serialize: object → string\nconst user = { name: \"Ada\", tags: [\"admin\", \"dev\"], active: true };\nconst json = JSON.stringify(user);\n// '{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"tags\":[\"admin\",\"dev\"],\"active\":true}'\n\n// deserialize: string → object\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(json);\nconsole.log(parsed.name);     // \"Ada\"\n\n// pretty-print with indentation\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user, null, 2));\n\n// filter keys during serialization\nJSON.stringify(user, [\"name\", \"active\"]);\n// '{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"active\":true}'<\/pre>\n\n<p>JSON limitations: no functions, no undefined, no comments, no\ncircular references (throws). Dates become strings.<\/p>\n","tryit":"const app = {\n  name: \"MyApp\",\n  version: \"1.0\",\n  config: { theme: \"dark\", lang: \"en\" },\n  tags: [\"web\", \"dev\"],\n  sayHi: () => \"hi\",      // functions are DROPPED\n};\n\n// serialize\nconst json = JSON.stringify(app, null, 2);\nconsole.log(json);\n// note: sayHi is gone!\n\n// deserialize\nconst copy = JSON.parse(json);\nconsole.log(copy.config.theme);\n\n// deep clone using JSON (simple but limited)\nconst original = { a: 1, nested: { b: 2 } };\nconst clone = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(original));\nclone.nested.b = 99;\nconsole.log(original.nested.b);  // 2 — truly separate!\n\n// modern deep clone\nconst deepCopy = structuredClone(original);\ndeepCopy.nested.b = 777;\nconsole.log(original.nested.b);  // 2 — still separate!\n","title_fa":"JSON","html_fa":"\n<p><b>JSON (نمادگذاری شیء جاوااسکریپت)<\/b> قالبِ همگانیِ داده برای\nAPIهاست. دو متد همه‌کار می‌کنند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// serialize: object → string\nconst user = { name: \"Ada\", tags: [\"admin\", \"dev\"], active: true };\nconst json = JSON.stringify(user);\n// '{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"tags\":[\"admin\",\"dev\"],\"active\":true}'\n\n// deserialize: string → object\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(json);\nconsole.log(parsed.name);     // \"Ada\"\n\n// pretty-print with indentation\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user, null, 2));\n\n// filter keys during serialization\nJSON.stringify(user, [\"name\", \"active\"]);\n// '{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"active\":true}'<\/pre>\n\n<p>محدودیت‌های JSON: بدون تابع، بدون undefined، بدون کامنت، بدون\nارجاعِ چرخه‌ای (خطا می‌دهد). تاریخ‌ها رشته می‌شوند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Error & Promise (preview)","html":"\n<p><b>Error<\/b> objects carry error information. The built-in types:\n<code>Error<\/code>, <code>TypeError<\/code>,\n<code>ReferenceError<\/code>, <code>RangeError<\/code>,\n<code>SyntaxError<\/code>. Create custom errors by extending:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class ValidationError extends Error {\n  constructor(field, message) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ValidationError\";\n    this.field = field;\n  }\n}\n\ntry {\n  throw new ValidationError(\"email\", \"Invalid email format\");\n} catch (e) {\n  if (e instanceof ValidationError) {\n    console.log(`Field \"${e.field}\": ${e.message}`);\n  }\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Promise<\/b> represents a value that will be available later —\nthe foundation of async JavaScript (Phase 7 covers it deeply). You'll\nsee promises returned from <code>fetch()<\/code>,\n<code>setTimeout()<\/code> wrappers, and every modern async\nAPI.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// custom error classes\nclass NetworkError extends Error {\n  constructor(status, message) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"NetworkError\";\n    this.status = status;\n  }\n}\n\nclass NotFoundError extends NetworkError {\n  constructor(resource) {\n    super(404, `${resource} not found`);\n  }\n}\n\n// error hierarchy in action\nfunction fetchUser(id) {\n  if (id <= 0) throw new ValidationError(\"id\", \"ID must be positive\");\n  if (id > 100) throw new NotFoundError(`User ${id}`);\n  return { id, name: `User${id}` };\n}\n\nfor (const id of [5, -1, 200]) {\n  try {\n    console.log(fetchUser(id));\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(`${e.name}: ${e.message}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// Promise preview — full coverage in Phase 7!\nconst promise = new Promise((resolve) => {\n  setTimeout(() => resolve(\"done!\"), 100);\n});\npromise.then(result => console.log(\"Promise resolved:\", result));\n","title_fa":"Error و Promise (پیش‌نمایش)","html_fa":"\n<p>شیءهای <b>Error<\/b> اطلاعاتِ خطا را حمل می‌کنند. انواع داخلی:\n<code>Error<\/code>، <code>TypeError<\/code>،\n<code>ReferenceError<\/code>، <code>RangeError<\/code> و\n<code>SyntaxError<\/code>. با extend، خطای سفارشی بساز:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">class ValidationError extends Error {\n  constructor(field, message) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ValidationError\";\n    this.field = field;\n  }\n}\n\ntry {\n  throw new ValidationError(\"email\", \"Invalid email format\");\n} catch (e) {\n  if (e instanceof ValidationError) {\n    console.log(`Field \"${e.field}\": ${e.message}`);\n  }\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Promise<\/b> مقداری را نمایندگی می‌کند که بعداً در دسترس خواهد بود\n— بنیانِ جاوااسکریپتِ ناهمگام (فصل ۷ کاملش را دارد). Promise را از\n<code>fetch()<\/code>، پوشش‌های <code>setTimeout()<\/code> و هر API\nasync مدرن برمی‌گردنده می‌بینی.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"Which method removes duplicates from an array?","options":["arr.unique()","[...new Set(arr)]","arr.distinct()","arr.filter()"],"answer":1,"explain":"Set only stores unique values; spreading back gives a deduplicated array.","fa":{"question":"کدام متد تکراری‌های آرایه را حذف می‌کند؟","options":["arr.unique()","[...new Set(arr)]","arr.distinct()","arr.filter()"],"explain":"Set فقط مقدارهای یکتا نگه می‌دارد؛ بازگستردنش آرایهٔ بدون تکرار می‌دهد."}},{"type":"blank","question":"The method to convert an object to a JSON string is <code>JSON.____<\/code>.","answers":["stringify"],"explain":"JSON.stringify serializes; JSON.parse deserializes.","fa":{"question":"متدِ تبدیل شیء به رشتهٔ JSON، <code>JSON.____<\/code> است.","explain":"JSON.stringify سریال می‌کند؛ JSON.parse برمی‌گرداند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"What is the main advantage of WeakMap over Map?","options":["It's faster","Keys can be any type","Entries are garbage-collected when the key object is destroyed","It has more methods"],"answer":2,"explain":"Weak references prevent memory leaks when key objects are no longer needed.","fa":{"question":"مزیتِ اصلی WeakMap نسبت به Map چیست؟","options":["سریع‌تر است","کلید می‌تواند هر نوعی باشد","ورودی‌ها با نابودیِ شیءِ کلید، garbage-collect می‌شوند","متدهای بیشتری دارد"],"explain":"ارجاع‌های ضعیف، وقتی شیءهای کلید دیگر لازم نیستند، از نشت حافظه جلوگیری می‌کنند."}}],"title_fa":"شیءهای داخلی"},{"id":"js07","title":"Asynchronous JavaScript","emoji":"⏳","lessons":[{"title":"Synchronous vs Asynchronous","html":"\n<p>JS is <b>single-threaded<\/b> — it can only do one thing at a time.\n<b>Synchronous<\/b> code blocks: each line waits for the previous.\n<b>Asynchronous<\/b> code schedules work for later without\nblocking:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// synchronous: each line blocks\nconsole.log(\"1\");\nconsole.log(\"2\");    // waits for \"1\" to finish\nconsole.log(\"3\");    // waits for \"2\"\n\n// asynchronous: doesn't block\nconsole.log(\"start\");\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(\"later\"), 0);\nconsole.log(\"end\");\n// output: \"start\" → \"end\" → \"later\"\n// even with delay=0, the callback runs AFTER all sync code!<\/pre>\n\n<p>The event loop: JS runs sync code first, then processes the\n<b>callback queue<\/b> (timers, events) and the <b>microtask queue<\/b>\n(promises). Microtasks always run before the next timer. This is why\npromise callbacks execute before setTimeout callbacks.<\/p>\n","tryit":"console.log(\"1: sync start\");\n\nsetTimeout(() => console.log(\"4: setTimeout (macrotask)\"), 0);\n\nPromise.resolve().then(() => console.log(\"3: promise (microtask)\"));\n\nconsole.log(\"2: sync end\");\n\n// Output order: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4\n// Microtasks (promises) always run before macrotasks (timers)!\n","title_fa":"همگام در برابر ناهمگام","html_fa":"\n<p>JS <b>تکنخی<\/b> است — فقط یک کار هم‌زمان. کدِ <b>همگام<\/b>\nمی‌بندد: هر خط منتظرِ قبلی می‌ماند. کدِ <b>ناهمگام<\/b> کار را برای بعد\nزمان‌بندی می‌کند بدون بستن:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// synchronous: each line blocks\nconsole.log(\"1\");\nconsole.log(\"2\");    // waits for \"1\" to finish\nconsole.log(\"3\");    // waits for \"2\"\n\n// asynchronous: doesn't block\nconsole.log(\"start\");\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(\"later\"), 0);\nconsole.log(\"end\");\n// output: \"start\" → \"end\" → \"later\"\n// even with delay=0, the callback runs AFTER all sync code!<\/pre>\n\n<p>حلقهٔ رخداد: JS اول کدِ sync را اجرا می‌کند، بعد <b>صفِ callback<\/b>\n(تایمرها، رخدادها) و <b>صفِ میکروتسک<\/b> (promiseها) را پردازش می‌کند.\nمیکروتسک‌ها همیشه قبل از تایمرِ بعدی اجرا می‌شوند. برای همین callbackهای\npromise قبل از callbackهای setTimeout اجرا می‌شوند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Callbacks & Promises","html":"\n<p><b>Callbacks<\/b> were the original async pattern — pass a function\nto be called when the operation completes. Nested callbacks for\nsequential operations create <b>callback hell<\/b>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// callback hell (the problem)\ngetUser(id, (user) =&gt; {\n  getPosts(user.id, (posts) =&gt; {\n    getComments(posts[0].id, (comments) =&gt; {\n      console.log(comments);   // deeply nested!\n    });\n  });\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>A <b>Promise<\/b> represents a value that will be available later. It\nhas three states: <b>pending<\/b> → <b>fulfilled<\/b> (with a value) or\n<b>rejected<\/b> (with an error). Once settled, a promise's state never\nchanges:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n  // async work here\n  setTimeout(() =&gt; {\n    const success = true;\n    if (success) resolve(\"data!\");\n    else reject(new Error(\"failed\"));\n  }, 1000);\n});\n\npromise\n  .then(value =&gt; console.log(\"got:\", value))\n  .catch(error =&gt; console.log(\"error:\", error.message));<\/pre>\n\n<p>Promises chain — each <code>.then()<\/code> receives the previous\none's return value, flattening callback hell into a readable\nchain.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// creating a promise\nfunction wait(ms) {\n  return new Promise((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(() => resolve(`waited ${ms}ms`), ms);\n  });\n}\n\n// promise chaining\nwait(100)\n  .then(msg => {\n    console.log(msg);\n    return wait(100);       // return another promise\n  })\n  .then(msg => {\n    console.log(msg);\n    return \"all done\";\n  })\n  .then(final => console.log(final));\n\n// promise states\nconst p = new Promise((resolve) => resolve(42));\nconsole.log(p instanceof Promise);  // true\n\n// settled promises\nPromise.resolve(\"instant\").then(v => console.log(v));\nPromise.reject(new Error(\"instant fail\")).catch(e => console.log(e.message));\n","title_fa":"callbackها و Promiseها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>callbackها<\/b> الگوی اصلیِ async بودند — تابعی بده که وقتی عملیات\nتمام شد صدا زده شود. callbackهای تودرتو برای عملیات ترتیبی\n<b>جهنمِ callback<\/b> می‌سازند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// callback hell (the problem)\ngetUser(id, (user) =&gt; {\n  getPosts(user.id, (posts) =&gt; {\n    getComments(posts[0].id, (comments) =&gt; {\n      console.log(comments);   // deeply nested!\n    });\n  });\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>یک <b>Promise<\/b> مقداری را نمایندگی می‌کند که بعداً در دسترس خواهد\nبود. سه وضعیت دارد: <b>pending<\/b> → <b>fulfilled<\/b> (با مقدار) یا\n<b>rejected<\/b> (با خطا). وقتی settle شد، وضعیتش دیگر هرگز عوض\nنمی‌شود:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n  // async work here\n  setTimeout(() =&gt; {\n    const success = true;\n    if (success) resolve(\"data!\");\n    else reject(new Error(\"failed\"));\n  }, 1000);\n});\n\npromise\n  .then(value =&gt; console.log(\"got:\", value))\n  .catch(error =&gt; console.log(\"error:\", error.message));<\/pre>\n\n<p>promiseها زنجیر می‌شوند — هر <code>.then()<\/code> مقدارِ برگشتیِ\nقبلی را می‌گیرد و جهنمِ callback را به زنجیره‌ای خوانا\nتخت می‌کند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"then(), catch() & finally()","html":"\n<p>The three instance methods every promise has:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">fetchData()\n  .then(data =&gt; {          // runs on success\n    console.log(data);\n    return data.id;         // return value passes to next .then()\n  })\n  .then(id =&gt; {\n    console.log(\"id:\", id);\n  })\n  .catch(error =&gt; {         // catches ANY error above\n    console.error(\"failed:\", error.message);\n  })\n  .finally(() =&gt; {          // always runs (cleanup)\n    console.log(\"done\");\n  });<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>.catch()<\/code> catches errors from ANY previous\n<code>.then()<\/code> — it's like a try/catch for the whole chain.\n<code>.finally()<\/code> doesn't receive the result; it's for cleanup\n(hide a loading spinner, close a connection).<\/p>\n","tryit":"function fetchUser(id) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      if (id <= 0) reject(new Error(\"Invalid ID\"));\n      else resolve({ id, name: `User${id}` });\n    }, 100);\n  });\n}\n\nfetchUser(1)\n  .then(user => {\n    console.log(\"got user:\", user.name);\n    return fetchUser(user.id + 1);   // chain to another promise\n  })\n  .then(user => console.log(\"and also:\", user.name))\n  .catch(err => console.log(\"error:\", err.message))\n  .finally(() => console.log(\"cleanup done\"));\n\n// error in the chain\nfetchUser(-5)\n  .then(user => console.log(user))\n  .catch(err => console.log(\"caught:\", err.message))\n  .finally(() => console.log(\"always\"));\n","title_fa":"then()‎، catch()‎ و finally()‎","html_fa":"\n<p>سه متدِ نمونه که هر promise‌ای دارد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">fetchData()\n  .then(data =&gt; {          // runs on success\n    console.log(data);\n    return data.id;         // return value passes to next .then()\n  })\n  .then(id =&gt; {\n    console.log(\"id:\", id);\n  })\n  .catch(error =&gt; {         // catches ANY error above\n    console.error(\"failed:\", error.message);\n  })\n  .finally(() =&gt; {          // always runs (cleanup)\n    console.log(\"done\");\n  });<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>.catch()<\/code> خطاها از <b>هر<\/b> then قبلی را می‌گیرد — مثل\ntry/catch برای کلِ زنجیره. <code>.finally()<\/code> نتیجه را نمی‌گیرد؛\nبرای پاک‌سازی است (پنهان‌کردن اسپینر، بستنِ اتصال).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Promise.all(), allSettled(), race() & any()","html":"\n<p>Four static methods for handling <b>multiple promises<\/b>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// all: wait for ALL to succeed (fails if ANY fails)\nconst [users, posts, comments] = await Promise.all([\n  fetchUsers(), fetchPosts(), fetchComments()\n]);\n\n// allSettled: wait for ALL to settle (success or fail)\nconst results = await Promise.allSettled([\n  fetchA(), fetchB(), fetchC()\n]);\n// results: [{status: \"fulfilled\", value: ...}, {status: \"rejected\", reason: ...}]\n\n// race: first to settle wins (success OR failure)\nconst fastest = await Promise.race([serverA(), serverB()]);\n\n// any: first to SUCCEED wins (ignores rejections)\nconst first = await Promise.any([mirror1(), mirror2(), mirror3()]);<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>all<\/b> — fail-fast: one rejection rejects the whole thing<\/li>\n<li><b>allSettled<\/b> — never rejects; gives status for each<\/li>\n<li><b>race<\/b> — first settled (even if rejected) wins<\/li>\n<li><b>any<\/b> — first fulfilled wins; rejects only if ALL reject<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n","tryit":"// create test promises\nconst makePromise = (name, ms, shouldFail = false) =>\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      shouldFail ? reject(new Error(`${name} failed`)) : resolve(`${name} done`);\n    }, ms);\n  });\n\n// Promise.all — all must succeed\nPromise.all([\n  makePromise(\"A\", 100),\n  makePromise(\"B\", 200),\n])\n  .then(results => console.log(\"all:\", results))\n  .catch(e => console.log(\"all failed:\", e.message));\n\n// Promise.allSettled — get every result\nPromise.allSettled([\n  makePromise(\"X\", 100),\n  makePromise(\"Y\", 100, true),   // this one fails\n])\n  .then(results => {\n    results.forEach(r => {\n      console.log(r.status, r.value || r.reason?.message);\n    });\n  });\n\n// Promise.race — first wins\nPromise.race([\n  makePromise(\"fast\", 50),\n  makePromise(\"slow\", 300),\n])\n  .then(winner => console.log(\"race winner:\", winner));\n","title_fa":"Promise.all()‎، allSettled()‎، race()‎ و any()‎","html_fa":"\n<p>چهار متدِ static برای مدیریتِ <b>چند promise<\/b>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// all: wait for ALL to succeed (fails if ANY fails)\nconst [users, posts, comments] = await Promise.all([\n  fetchUsers(), fetchPosts(), fetchComments()\n]);\n\n// allSettled: wait for ALL to settle (success or fail)\nconst results = await Promise.allSettled([\n  fetchA(), fetchB(), fetchC()\n]);\n// results: [{status: \"fulfilled\", value: ...}, {status: \"rejected\", reason: ...}]\n\n// race: first to settle wins (success OR failure)\nconst fastest = await Promise.race([serverA(), serverB()]);\n\n// any: first to SUCCEED wins (ignores rejections)\nconst first = await Promise.any([mirror1(), mirror2(), mirror3()]);<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>all<\/b> — سریع‌شکن: یک رد، کل را رد می‌کند<\/li>\n<li><b>allSettled<\/b> — هرگز رد نمی‌شود؛ وضعیتِ هرکدام را می‌دهد<\/li>\n<li><b>race<\/b> — اولین settleشده (حتی رد‌شده) می‌برد<\/li>\n<li><b>any<\/b> — اولین fulfilled می‌برد؛ فقط اگر همه رد شوند رد\nمی‌شود<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n"},{"title":"async & await","html":"\n<p><code>async/await<\/code> is syntactic sugar over promises that makes\nasync code <b>look and read like synchronous code<\/b>:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// async function always returns a Promise\nasync function getData() {\n  return 42;    // becomes Promise.resolve(42)\n}\n\n// await pauses INSIDE the async function until the promise settles\nasync function main() {\n  const user = await fetchUser(1);      // waits for the promise\n  const posts = await fetchPosts(user.id);\n  const comments = await fetchComments(posts[0].id);\n  console.log(comments);                 // reads like sync code!\n}\n\n// error handling with try/catch (the natural way)\nasync function safeMain() {\n  try {\n    const data = await riskyOperation();\n    console.log(data);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"failed:\", error.message);\n  } finally {\n    console.log(\"done\");\n  }\n}\n\n// run independent promises in PARALLEL with Promise.all\nasync function efficient() {\n  const [users, posts] = await Promise.all([\n    fetchUsers(),      // start both\n    fetchPosts(),      // at the same time\n  ]);                    // wait for both\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>await<\/code> can only be used inside <code>async<\/code>\nfunctions (or top-level in modules). It pauses the async function, NOT\nthe whole thread — other code continues running.<\/p>\n","tryit":"function wait(ms) {\n  return new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => resolve(ms), ms));\n}\n\n// async/await: sequential (easy to read)\nasync function sequential() {\n  console.log(\"starting...\");\n  const a = await wait(200);\n  console.log(\"step 1 done:\", a);\n  const b = await wait(200);\n  console.log(\"step 2 done:\", b);\n  return a + b;\n}\n\n// async/await: parallel (faster for independent tasks)\nasync function parallel() {\n  const start = Date.now();\n  const [a, b] = await Promise.all([wait(200), wait(200)]);\n  console.log(`both done in ${Date.now() - start}ms (not 400ms!)`);\n}\n\n// error handling with try/catch\nasync function safeOperation() {\n  try {\n    await wait(100);\n    throw new Error(\"something went wrong\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(\"caught:\", e.message);\n  } finally {\n    console.log(\"cleanup\");\n  }\n}\n\n// run them\n(async () => {\n  await sequential();\n  await parallel();\n  await safeOperation();\n})();\n","title_fa":"async و await","html_fa":"\n<p><code>async/await<\/code> شکرِ نحوی روی promiseهاست که کد async را\n<b>شبیه کد همگام<\/b> نشان می‌دهد و می‌خوانَد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// async function always returns a Promise\nasync function getData() {\n  return 42;    // becomes Promise.resolve(42)\n}\n\n// await pauses INSIDE the async function until the promise settles\nasync function main() {\n  const user = await fetchUser(1);      // waits for the promise\n  const posts = await fetchPosts(user.id);\n  const comments = await fetchComments(posts[0].id);\n  console.log(comments);                 // reads like sync code!\n}\n\n// error handling with try/catch (the natural way)\nasync function safeMain() {\n  try {\n    const data = await riskyOperation();\n    console.log(data);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"failed:\", error.message);\n  } finally {\n    console.log(\"done\");\n  }\n}\n\n// run independent promises in PARALLEL with Promise.all\nasync function efficient() {\n  const [users, posts] = await Promise.all([\n    fetchUsers(),      // start both\n    fetchPosts(),      // at the same time\n  ]);                    // wait for both\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p><code>await<\/code> فقط داخل توابع <code>async<\/code> (یا سطحِ ماژول)\nکار می‌کند. تابع async را مکث می‌دهد نه کل نخ را — بقیهٔ کد ادامه\nمی‌یابد.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Error Handling in Async Code","html":"\n<p>Async errors don't get caught by regular try/catch — they need\nspecial handling depending on the pattern:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// with promises: .catch()\nriskyOperation().catch(err =&gt; console.log(err));\n\n// with async/await: try/catch works naturally\nasync function main() {\n  try {\n    await riskyOperation();\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.log(err.message);\n  }\n}\n\n// ⚠️ common mistake: forgetting await\nasync function buggy() {\n  try {\n    riskyOperation();      // ← missing await! Error is UNHANDLED\n  } catch (e) { /* never reached */ }\n}\n\n// Promise.all fails fast — use allSettled for independent ops\nasync function fetchAll() {\n  const results = await Promise.allSettled([\n    fetchA(), fetchB(), fetchC()\n  ]);\n  const errors = results.filter(r =&gt; r.status === \"rejected\");\n  const values = results.filter(r =&gt; r.status === \"fulfilled\")\n                         .map(r =&gt; r.value);\n  return { values, errors };\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>Always handle async errors: an unhandled promise rejection crashes\nmodern Node.js and shows ugly console errors in browsers. Add a global\nhandler as a safety net:\n<code>window.addEventListener(\"unhandledrejection\", e =&gt; ...)<\/code><\/p>\n","tryit":"// the #1 mistake: forgetting await\nasync function buggy() {\n  try {\n    Promise.reject(new Error(\"unhandled!\"));  // no await!\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(\"never reached!\");  // catch can't see it\n  }\n}\n\n// the fix: await the promise\nasync function correct() {\n  try {\n    await Promise.reject(new Error(\"caught!\"));\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(\"now caught:\", e.message);\n  }\n}\n\n(async () => {\n  await buggy();\n  await correct();\n\n  // allSettled for independent operations\n  const results = await Promise.allSettled([\n    Promise.resolve(\"success 1\"),\n    Promise.reject(new Error(\"fail\")),\n    Promise.resolve(\"success 2\"),\n  ]);\n  results.forEach(r => {\n    console.log(r.status, r.value ?? r.reason?.message);\n  });\n})();\n","title_fa":"مدیریت خطا در کد async","html_fa":"\n<p>خطاهای async با try/catch معمولی گرفته نمی‌شوند — بسته به الگو،\nمدیریتِ خاص می‌خواهند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// with promises: .catch()\nriskyOperation().catch(err =&gt; console.log(err));\n\n// with async/await: try/catch works naturally\nasync function main() {\n  try {\n    await riskyOperation();\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.log(err.message);\n  }\n}\n\n// ⚠️ common mistake: forgetting await\nasync function buggy() {\n  try {\n    riskyOperation();      // ← missing await! Error is UNHANDLED\n  } catch (e) { /* never reached */ }\n}\n\n// Promise.all fails fast — use allSettled for independent ops\nasync function fetchAll() {\n  const results = await Promise.allSettled([\n    fetchA(), fetchB(), fetchC()\n  ]);\n  const errors = results.filter(r =&gt; r.status === \"rejected\");\n  const values = results.filter(r =&gt; r.status === \"fulfilled\")\n                         .map(r =&gt; r.value);\n  return { values, errors };\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>همیشه خطاهای async را هندل کن: یک rejectionِ مدیریت‌نشده، Node.js\nمدرن را کرش می‌کند و در مرورگر خطاهای زشتِ console می‌سازد. به‌عنوان\nتورِ نجات، هندلر سراسری اضافه کن:\n<code>window.addEventListener(\"unhandledrejection\", e =&gt; ...)<\/code><\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"What does an async function always return?","options":["undefined","A Promise","The resolved value","An iterator"],"answer":1,"explain":"async functions wrap their return value in Promise.resolve().","fa":{"question":"تابع async همیشه چه برمی‌گرداند؟","options":["undefined","یک Promise","مقدارِ resolveشده","یک iterator"],"explain":"توابع async مقدارِ برگشتی‌شان را در Promise.resolve() می‌پیچند."}},{"type":"blank","question":"The operator that pauses inside an async function is <code>____<\/code>.","answers":["await","await operator"],"explain":"await pauses the async function until the promise settles.","fa":{"question":"عملگری که داخل تابع async مکث می‌کند <code>____<\/code> است.","explain":"await تابع async را تا settle شدنِ promise نگه می‌دارد."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Promise.all() rejects when:","options":["All promises reject","ANY promise rejects","The first promise settles","Never"],"answer":1,"explain":"Promise.all is fail-fast: one rejection rejects the whole batch.","fa":{"question":"Promise.all() کی رد می‌شود؟","options":["وقتی همه رد شوند","وقتی هر promiseای رد شود","وقتی اولین settle شود","هرگز"],"explain":"Promise.all سریع‌شکن است: یک رد، کلِ بسته را رد می‌کند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"The #1 mistake with async/await error handling:","options":["Using try/catch","Forgetting 'await' before the promise call","Using .catch()","Throwing too many errors"],"answer":1,"explain":"Without await, the try/catch can't catch the async error — it's unhandled.","fa":{"question":"اشتباهِ شمارهٔ ۱ در مدیریت خطای async/await:","options":["استفاده از try/catch","جا انداختنِ await قبل از فراخوانی promise","استفاده از catch.()","پرتابِ خطای زیاد"],"explain":"بدون await، try/catch خطای async را نمی‌بیند — مدیریت‌نشده می‌ماند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Which Promise method never rejects?","options":["Promise.all()","Promise.race()","Promise.allSettled()","Promise.any()"],"answer":2,"explain":"allSettled always resolves with {status, value/reason} for each promise.","fa":{"question":"کدام متد Promise هرگز رد نمی‌شود؟","options":["Promise.all()","Promise.race()","Promise.allSettled()","Promise.any()"],"explain":"allSettled همیشه با {status, value/reason} برای هر promise\tresolve می‌شود."}}],"title_fa":"جاوااسکریپت ناهمگام"},{"id":"js08","title":"Modules","emoji":"📄","lessons":[{"title":"Modules: export & import","html":"\n<p><b>Modules<\/b> are self-contained files that export values for other\nfiles to import. Modern JS uses ES modules natively:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// math.js — export values\nexport const PI = 3.14159;\nexport function circleArea(r) { return PI * r ** 2; }\n\n// default export (one per module)\nexport default class Calculator { ... }\n\n// app.js — import them\nimport Calculator from './math.js';          // default import (no braces)\nimport { PI, circleArea } from './math.js';  // named imports (braces)\nimport * as math from './math.js';           // namespace import\n\nconsole.log(PI);                  // 3.14159\nconsole.log(circleArea(2));      // 12.57\nconsole.log(math.PI);            // 3.14159 (via namespace)<\/pre>\n\n<p>Modules are <b>strict mode<\/b> by default, <b>deferred<\/b> (load\nafter HTML parsing), and <b>cached<\/b> (imported once, shared by all\nimporters). They enable code organization, dependency management, and\ntree-shaking (removing unused code at build time).<\/p>\n\n<p>In the browser: <code>&lt;script type=\"module\" src=\"app.js\"&gt;<\/code>.\nIn Node.js: <code>.mjs<\/code> extension or <code>\"type\":\n\"module\"<\/code> in package.json.<\/p>\n","title_fa":"ماژول‌ها: export و import","html_fa":"\n<p><b>ماژول‌ها<\/b> فایل‌های خودبسنده‌ای هستند که مقدارها را برای import\nکردنِ فایل‌های دیگر export می‌کنند. JS مدرن ماژول‌های ES را بومی\nدارد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// math.js — export values\nexport const PI = 3.14159;\nexport function circleArea(r) { return PI * r ** 2; }\n\n// default export (one per module)\nexport default class Calculator { ... }\n\n// app.js — import them\nimport Calculator from './math.js';          // default import (no braces)\nimport { PI, circleArea } from './math.js';  // named imports (braces)\nimport * as math from './math.js';           // namespace import\n\nconsole.log(PI);                  // 3.14159\nconsole.log(circleArea(2));      // 12.57\nconsole.log(math.PI);            // 3.14159 (via namespace)<\/pre>\n\n<p>ماژول‌ها به‌طور پیش‌فرض <b>strict mode<\/b>ند، <b>deferred<\/b> (بعد از\nپارس HTML لود می‌شوند) و <b>کش<\/b> می‌شوند (یک بار import، بین همهٔ\nimporterها مشترک). سازمان‌دهی کد، مدیریت وابستگی و tree-shaking (حذف\nکد بلااستفاده هنگام build) را ممکن می‌کنند.<\/p>\n\n<p>در مرورگر: <code>&lt;script type=\"module\" src=\"app.js\"&gt;<\/code>. در\nNode.js: پسوند <code>.mjs<\/code> یا <code>\"type\": \"module\"<\/code> در\npackage.json.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Dynamic import() & Module Resolution","html":"\n<p><b>Dynamic import<\/b> loads a module on demand — returning a\nPromise. This enables code splitting and lazy loading:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// static import: loaded immediately\nimport { heavy } from './heavy.js';\n\n// dynamic import: loaded when needed\nbutton.addEventListener('click', async () =&gt; {\n  const { chart } = await import('./chart.js');\n  chart.render();     // chart.js only loaded now!\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>Module resolution: the browser resolves relative paths\n(<code>./utils.js<\/code>), bare paths need import maps, and the file\nextension is required in browsers (unlike some bundlers). MDN's guide\ncovers the details.<\/p>\n","title_fa":"import()‎ پویا و تفکیک ماژول","html_fa":"\n<p><b>import پویا<\/b> ماژول را در لحظهٔ نیاز لود می‌کند — یک Promise\nبرمی‌گرداند. همین، تقسیم کد و لودِ تنبل را ممکن می‌کند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// static import: loaded immediately\nimport { heavy } from './heavy.js';\n\n// dynamic import: loaded when needed\nbutton.addEventListener('click', async () =&gt; {\n  const { chart } = await import('./chart.js');\n  chart.render();     // chart.js only loaded now!\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>تفکیک ماژول: مرورگر مسیرهای نسبی (<code>./utils.js<\/code>) را حل\nمی‌کند، مسیرهای خالی به import map نیاز دارند و پسوند فایل در مرورگرها\nالزامی است (برخلاف بعضی bundlerها).<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"How many default exports can a module have?","options":["Zero","One","Unlimited","One per type"],"answer":1,"explain":"Each module can have exactly one default export (plus any number of named exports).","fa":{"question":"یک ماژول چند default export می‌تواند داشته باشد؟","options":["صفر","یکی","نامحدود","یکی به‌ازای هر نوع"],"explain":"هر ماژول دقیقاً یک default export دارد (به‌علاوهٔ هر تعداد named export)."}},{"type":"blank","question":"Dynamic import returns a ____.","answers":["promise","Promise"],"explain":"import() returns a Promise that resolves to the module namespace.","fa":{"question":"import پویا یک ____ برمی‌گرداند.","explain":"import() یک Promise برمی‌گرداند که به namespace ماژول resolve می‌شود."}}],"title_fa":"ماژول‌ها"},{"id":"js09","title":"Browser JavaScript","emoji":"🌐","lessons":[{"title":"DOM & Selecting Elements","html":"\n<p>The <b>DOM (Document Object Model)<\/b> is a live tree of objects\nmirroring your HTML. JavaScript reads and manipulates it to make pages\ninteractive:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// select ONE element\nconst el = document.querySelector(\".card\");       // first match\nconst byId = document.getElementById(\"header\");   // by id\n\n// select ALL matching elements (returns NodeList)\nconst items = document.querySelectorAll(\".item\");\nitems.forEach(item =&gt; console.log(item.textContent));<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>querySelector<\/code> — uses CSS selectors, returns the first\nmatch (or null)<\/li>\n<li><code>querySelectorAll<\/code> — returns a static NodeList (use\n<code>forEach<\/code> or spread to an array)<\/li>\n<li><code>getElementById<\/code> — fastest, but only for IDs<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n","tryit":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><style>\n  .highlight { background: #ffd43b; }\n  .box { padding: 8px; margin: 4px; border: 2px solid #1572b6;\n         border-radius: 6px; }\n<\/style><\/head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"app\">\n    <div class=\"box\" data-id=\"1\">Item 1<\/div>\n    <div class=\"box\" data-id=\"2\">Item 2<\/div>\n    <div class=\"box\" data-id=\"3\">Item 3<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <script>\n    // select and modify\n    const first = document.querySelector(\".box\");\n    first.textContent = \"← selected by querySelector\";\n\n    // select all and highlight\n    document.querySelectorAll(\".box\").forEach(box => {\n      box.classList.add(\"highlight\");\n    });\n\n    // by data attribute\n    const item2 = document.querySelector('[data-id=\"2\"]');\n    console.log(\"item 2:\", item2?.textContent);\n  <\/script>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n","title_fa":"DOM و انتخاب عنصرها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>DOM (Document Object Model)<\/b> درختی زنده از شیءهاست که HTML را\nآینه می‌کند. جاوااسکریپت آن را می‌خواند و دستکاری می‌کند تا صفحه‌ها\nتعاملی شوند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// select ONE element\nconst el = document.querySelector(\".card\");       // first match\nconst byId = document.getElementById(\"header\");   // by id\n\n// select ALL matching elements (returns NodeList)\nconst items = document.querySelectorAll(\".item\");\nitems.forEach(item =&gt; console.log(item.textContent));<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>querySelector<\/code> — با سلکتورهای CSS کار می‌کند، اولین\nتطبیق را می‌دهد (یا null)<\/li>\n<li><code>querySelectorAll<\/code> — یک NodeList ثابت برمی‌گرداند (با\n<code>forEach<\/code> یا spread به آرایه استفاده کن)<\/li>\n<li><code>getElementById<\/code> — سریع‌ترین، اما فقط برای IDها<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n"},{"title":"Creating & Modifying Elements","html":"\n<p>JavaScript can create, modify, and remove DOM elements dynamically:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// create\nconst div = document.createElement(\"div\");\ndiv.textContent = \"Hello!\";\ndiv.className = \"card\";\ndiv.innerHTML = \"&lt;strong&gt;Bold&lt;/strong&gt; text\";\n\n// modify existing\nel.textContent = \"new text\";        // safe (no HTML parsing)\nel.innerHTML = \"&lt;b&gt;parsed&lt;/b&gt;\";   // parses HTML (XSS risk with user data!)\nel.setAttribute(\"data-id\", \"42\");\nel.classList.add(\"active\");\nel.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\nel.classList.toggle(\"dark\");\nel.style.color = \"#1572b6\";\n\n// insert into the DOM\nparent.appendChild(el);              // add as last child\nparent.prepend(el);                  // add as first child\nel.before(newEl);                    // insert before\nel.after(newEl);                     // insert after\nel.remove();                         // delete<\/pre>\n\n<p>Always prefer <code>textContent<\/code> over <code>innerHTML<\/code>\nfor user-supplied data — innerHTML parses HTML and is the #1 XSS\nvulnerability.<\/p>\n","tryit":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><style>\n  .todo-item { padding: 6px 12px; margin: 4px 0; background: #f2f8fe;\n    border-radius: 6px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }\n  .done { text-decoration: line-through; color: #999; }\n<\/style><\/head>\n<body>\n  <h3>Dynamic Todo List<\/h3>\n  <div id=\"list\"><\/div>\n  <script>\n    const list = document.getElementById(\"list\");\n    const items = [\"Learn DOM\", \"Build projects\", \"Master JS\"];\n\n    items.forEach((text, i) => {\n      const div = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      div.className = \"todo-item\";\n      div.innerHTML = `<span>${text}<\/span><span>item ${i + 1}<\/span>`;\n      div.addEventListener(\"click\", () => div.classList.toggle(\"done\"));\n      list.appendChild(div);\n    });\n    console.log(\"Created\", items.length, \"items\");\n  <\/script>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n","title_fa":"ساخت و تغییر عنصرها","html_fa":"\n<p>جاوااسکریپت عنصرهای DOM را پویا می‌سازد، تغییر می‌دهد و حذف\nمی‌کند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// create\nconst div = document.createElement(\"div\");\ndiv.textContent = \"Hello!\";\ndiv.className = \"card\";\ndiv.innerHTML = \"&lt;strong&gt;Bold&lt;/strong&gt; text\";\n\n// modify existing\nel.textContent = \"new text\";        // safe (no HTML parsing)\nel.innerHTML = \"&lt;b&gt;parsed&lt;/b&gt;\";   // parses HTML (XSS risk with user data!)\nel.setAttribute(\"data-id\", \"42\");\nel.classList.add(\"active\");\nel.classList.remove(\"hidden\");\nel.classList.toggle(\"dark\");\nel.style.color = \"#1572b6\";\n\n// insert into the DOM\nparent.appendChild(el);              // add as last child\nparent.prepend(el);                  // add as first child\nel.before(newEl);                    // insert before\nel.after(newEl);                     // insert after\nel.remove();                         // delete<\/pre>\n\n<p>برای دادهٔ عرضه‌شده از کاربر همیشه <code>textContent<\/code> را به\n<code>innerHTML<\/code> ترجیح بده — innerHTML کد HTML را پارس می‌کند و\nشماره‌یکِ آسیب‌پذیریِ XSS است.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Events & Event Listeners","html":"\n<p><b>Events<\/b> are the user's actions: clicks, keypresses, scrolls.\n<code>addEventListener<\/code> is how you respond:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">button.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"clicked!\", event.target);\n});\n\n// common events\n\"click\"          mouse/touch press\n\"input\"          value changed per keystroke\n\"change\"         value committed\n\"submit\"         form submitted\n\"keydown\" / \"keyup\"  keyboard\n\"mouseover\" / \"mouseout\"\n\"scroll\" / \"load\" / \"resize\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>The event object has <code>event.target<\/code> (what was clicked),\n<code>event.key<\/code> (which key), and <code>event.preventDefault()<\/code>\nto stop default behaviour (form submission, link navigation).<\/p>\n","tryit":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><style>\n  .counter { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; margin: 10px; }\n  button { padding: 8px 16px; margin: 4px; cursor: pointer; }\n<\/style><\/head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"counter\" id=\"display\">0<\/div>\n  <button id=\"inc\">+1<\/button>\n  <button id=\"dec\">-1<\/button>\n  <button id=\"reset\">Reset<\/button>\n\n  <script>\n    let count = 0;\n    const display = document.getElementById(\"display\");\n\n    document.getElementById(\"inc\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      count++;\n      display.textContent = count;\n    });\n    document.getElementById(\"dec\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      count--;\n      display.textContent = count;\n    });\n    document.getElementById(\"reset\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      count = 0;\n      display.textContent = count;\n    });\n\n    // keyboard events\n    document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", (e) => {\n      if (e.key === \"ArrowUp\") { count++; display.textContent = count; }\n      if (e.key === \"ArrowDown\") { count--; display.textContent = count; }\n    });\n  <\/script>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n","title_fa":"رخدادها و Event Listenerها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>رخدادها<\/b> عمل‌های کاربرند: کلیک، فشردنِ کلید، اسکرول.\n<code>addEventListener<\/code> راهِ پاسخ‌دادن است:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">button.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"clicked!\", event.target);\n});\n\n// common events\n\"click\"          mouse/touch press\n\"input\"          value changed per keystroke\n\"change\"         value committed\n\"submit\"         form submitted\n\"keydown\" / \"keyup\"  keyboard\n\"mouseover\" / \"mouseout\"\n\"scroll\" / \"load\" / \"resize\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>شیءِ رخداد <code>event.target<\/code> دارد (چه چیزی کلیک شد)،\n<code>event.key<\/code> (کدام کلید) و\n<code>event.preventDefault()<\/code> برای توقفِ رفتار پیش‌فرض (ارسال فرم،\nناوبری لینک).<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Event Bubbling & Delegation","html":"\n<p>When you click a nested element, the event <b>bubbles up<\/b> from\nthe target through its ancestors. This enables <b>event delegation<\/b>\n— one listener on a parent handles events for all its children (present\nand future):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// instead of adding a listener to EVERY item:\nlist.addEventListener(\"click\", (e) =&gt; {\n  if (e.target.matches(\".delete-btn\")) {\n    e.target.closest(\".item\").remove();   // delegate!\n  }\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>Delegation is how dynamic lists work — items added later are\nautomatically handled. <code>event.stopPropagation()<\/code> stops\nbubbling when needed.<\/p>\n","tryit":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><style>\n  .tag { display: inline-block; padding: 6px 14px; margin: 4px;\n         background: #eaf4fd; border: 2px solid #33a9dc;\n         border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer; }\n  .tag.selected { background: #1572b6; color: white; }\n<\/style><\/head>\n<body>\n  <h3>Click tags — one delegated listener handles all!<\/h3>\n  <div id=\"container\">\n    <span class=\"tag\">js<\/span>\n    <span class=\"tag\">css<\/span>\n    <span class=\"tag\">html<\/span>\n  <\/div>\n  <button id=\"add\">Add new tag<\/button>\n\n  <script>\n    // ONE listener for all current AND future tags\n    document.getElementById(\"container\").addEventListener(\"click\", (e) => {\n      if (e.target.classList.contains(\"tag\")) {\n        e.target.classList.toggle(\"selected\");\n      }\n    });\n\n    // add new tags — they work automatically!\n    let counter = 0;\n    document.getElementById(\"add\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n      const tag = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      tag.className = \"tag\";\n      tag.textContent = `new-${++counter}`;\n      document.getElementById(\"container\").appendChild(tag);\n    });\n  <\/script>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n","title_fa":"حباب‌زدنِ رخداد و delegation","html_fa":"\n<p>وقتی روی عنصری تودرتو کلیک می‌کنی، رخداد از هدف به پدرها <b>حباب\nمی‌زند<\/b>. این <b>event delegation<\/b> را ممکن می‌کند — یک listener\nروی پدر، رخدادهای همهٔ فرزندان (حال و آینده) را هندل می‌کند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// instead of adding a listener to EVERY item:\nlist.addEventListener(\"click\", (e) =&gt; {\n  if (e.target.matches(\".delete-btn\")) {\n    e.target.closest(\".item\").remove();   // delegate!\n  }\n});<\/pre>\n\n<p>delegation چطور لیست‌های پویا کار می‌کنند — آیتم‌هایی که بعداً\nاضافه می‌شوند خودکار هندل می‌شوند. <code>event.stopPropagation()<\/code>\nوقتی لازم است حباب‌زدن را متوقف می‌کند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Fetch API & HTTP Requests","html":"\n<p><code>fetch()<\/code> makes HTTP requests — the modern replacement\nfor XMLHttpRequest:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// GET request\nconst response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\");\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n\n// POST request with body\nconst res = await fetch(\"/api/users\", {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ name: \"Ada\", email: \"ada@x.io\" }),\n});\nconst created = await res.json();<\/pre>\n\n<p>fetch returns a Promise that resolves to a Response object. You must\ncheck <code>response.ok<\/code> — fetch only rejects on network errors,\nnot HTTP errors (404, 500 still resolve!). Methods: <code>.json()<\/code>,\n<code>.text()<\/code>, <code>.blob()<\/code>.<\/p>\n","tryit":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><style>\n  .result { padding: 10px; background: #f2f8fe; border-radius: 8px;\n            margin: 8px 0; font-family: monospace; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  button { padding: 8px 16px; cursor: pointer; margin: 4px; }\n<\/style><\/head>\n<body>\n  <h3>Fetch API demo (public API)<\/h3>\n  <button onclick=\"loadData()\">Fetch a random user<\/button>\n  <div class=\"result\" id=\"output\">Click the button!<\/div>\n\n  <script>\n    async function loadData() {\n      const output = document.getElementById(\"output\");\n      output.textContent = \"Loading...\";\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(\"https://randomuser.me/api/\");\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);\n        const data = await res.json();\n        const user = data.results[0];\n        output.textContent = JSON.stringify({\n          name: `${user.name.first} ${user.name.last}`,\n          email: user.email,\n          country: user.location.country,\n        }, null, 2);\n      } catch (e) {\n        output.textContent = `Error: ${e.message}`;\n      }\n    }\n  <\/script>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n","title_fa":"Fetch API و درخواست‌های HTTP","html_fa":"\n<p><code>fetch()<\/code> درخواست‌های HTTP می‌فرستد — جایگزینِ مدرنِ\nXMLHttpRequest:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// GET request\nconst response = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\");\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\nconst data = await response.json();\n\n// POST request with body\nconst res = await fetch(\"/api/users\", {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ name: \"Ada\", email: \"ada@x.io\" }),\n});\nconst created = await res.json();<\/pre>\n\n<p>‏fetch یک Promise برمی‌گرداند که به شیءِ Response حل می‌شود. باید\n<code>response.ok<\/code> را چک کنی — fetch فقط روی خطای شبکه رد\nمی‌شود، نه خطاهای HTTP (۴۰۴ و ۵۰۰ هم resolve می‌شوند!). متدها:\n<code>.json()<\/code>، <code>.text()<\/code>، <code>.blob()<\/code>.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Web Storage & Cookies","html":"\n<p><b>Web Storage<\/b> (localStorage + sessionStorage) stores key-value\npairs in the browser — simpler than cookies:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">localStorage.setItem(\"name\", \"Ada\");\nlocalStorage.getItem(\"name\")          // \"Ada\"\nlocalStorage.removeItem(\"name\");\nlocalStorage.clear();\n\n// objects: serialize with JSON\nlocalStorage.setItem(\"user\", JSON.stringify({ name: \"Ada\" }));\nconst user = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"user\"));<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>localStorage<\/b> — persists until deleted<\/li>\n<li><b>sessionStorage<\/b> — dies with the tab<\/li>\n<li><b>Cookies<\/b> — sent to the server on every request (4KB limit,\ndated mechanism; use for auth tokens, not data)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>This app uses localStorage for your name, progress, language, and\nplayground code — check devtools → Application → Local Storage!<\/p>\n","title_fa":"Web Storage و کوکی‌ها","html_fa":"\n<p><b>Web Storage<\/b> (localStorage + sessionStorage) جفت‌های\nکلید-مقدار در مرورگر ذخیره می‌کند — از کوکی ساده‌تر:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">localStorage.setItem(\"name\", \"Ada\");\nlocalStorage.getItem(\"name\")          // \"Ada\"\nlocalStorage.removeItem(\"name\");\nlocalStorage.clear();\n\n// objects: serialize with JSON\nlocalStorage.setItem(\"user\", JSON.stringify({ name: \"Ada\" }));\nconst user = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(\"user\"));<\/pre>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>localStorage<\/b> — تا حذفِ دستی دوام دارد<\/li>\n<li><b>sessionStorage<\/b> — با بسته‌شدنِ تب می‌میرد<\/li>\n<li><b>کوکی‌ها<\/b> — با هر درخواست به سرور می‌روند (محدودیت ۴KB،\nسازوکارِ قدیمی؛ برای توکن‌های احرازِ هویت، نه داده)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>این اپ از localStorage برای نام، پیشرفت، زبان و کدِ playground\nاستفاده می‌کند — devtools → Application → Local Storage را ببین!<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Browser APIs","html":"\n<p>The browser provides many APIs beyond the DOM. The ones you'll\nencounter most:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>setTimeout / setInterval / requestAnimationFrame<\/b> — timing\nand animation<\/li>\n<li><b>Geolocation<\/b> — user's location (with permission)<\/li>\n<li><b>Clipboard<\/b> — copy/paste<\/li>\n<li><b>Intersection Observer<\/b> — detect when elements enter the\nviewport (lazy loading, animations)<\/li>\n<li><b>Notifications<\/b> — system notifications<\/li>\n<li><b>Web Workers<\/b> — background threads (covered in HTML course)<\/li>\n<li><b>History<\/b> — pushState/back (SPA routing)<\/li>\n<li><b>Console<\/b> — log, warn, error, table, time...<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>These are documented under <b>Web APIs<\/b> on MDN — separate from\nthe JavaScript language itself. Each has its own MDN page with\nbrowser support info.<\/p>\n","title_fa":"APIهای مرورگر","html_fa":"\n<p>مرورگر فراتر از DOM، APIهای زیادی می‌دهد. پرتکرارترین‌ها:<\/p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><b>setTimeout / setInterval / requestAnimationFrame<\/b> — زمان‌بندی و\nانیمیشن<\/li>\n<li><b>Geolocation<\/b> — مکانِ کاربر (با اجازه)<\/li>\n<li><b>Clipboard<\/b> — کپی/پیست<\/li>\n<li><b>Intersection Observer<\/b> — تشخیصِ ورودِ عنصر به viewport (لودِ\nتنبل، انیمیشن)<\/li>\n<li><b>Notifications<\/b> — اعلان‌های سیستم<\/li>\n<li><b>Web Workers<\/b> — نخ‌های پس‌زمینه (در فصل HTML پوشش داده\nشد)<\/li>\n<li><b>History<\/b> — pushState/back (مسیریابی SPA)<\/li>\n<li><b>Console<\/b> — log، warn، error، table، time...<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<p>اینها زیرِ <b>Web APIs<\/b> در MDN مستند شده‌اند — جدا از خودِ زبانِ\nجاوااسکریپت. هرکدام صفحهٔ MDN و اطلاعاتِ پشتیبانیِ مرورگرهای خودش را\nدارد.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"What does querySelector return?","options":["All matching elements","The first matching element","An array","A string"],"answer":1,"explain":"querySelector returns the first match; querySelectorAll returns all.","fa":{"question":"querySelector چه برمی‌گرداند؟","options":["همهٔ عنصرهای منطبق","اولین عنصرِ منطبق","یک آرایه","یک رشته"],"explain":"querySelector اولین تطبیق را می‌دهد؛ querySelectorAll همه را."}},{"type":"blank","question":"The safe way to set text content (no HTML parsing) is <code>____<\/code>.","answers":["textContent"],"explain":"textContent is safe; innerHTML parses HTML and risks XSS.","fa":{"question":"راهِ امنِ ست‌کردنِ متن (بدون پارسِ HTML) <code>____<\/code> است.","explain":"textContent امن است؛ innerHTML کد HTML را پارس می‌کند و خطرِ XSS دارد."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Event delegation means:","options":["Sending events to a server","One listener on a parent handles events for all children","Removing all listeners","Using event.target only"],"answer":1,"explain":"Events bubble to ancestors — a parent listener covers future children too.","fa":{"question":"event delegation یعنی:","options":["فرستادنِ رخداد به سرور","یک listener روی پدر، رخدادهای همهٔ فرزندان را هندل می‌کند","حذفِ همهٔ listenerها","فقط استفاده از event.target"],"explain":"رخدادها به پدرها حباب می‌زنند — listener پدری، فرزندانِ آینده را هم می‌پوشاند."}},{"type":"blank","question":"fetch() only rejects on ____ errors, not HTTP 404/500.","answers":["network"],"explain":"Always check response.ok — fetch resolves even for 404/500.","fa":{"question":"‏fetch فقط روی خطاهای ____ رد می‌شود، نه HTTP 404/500.","explain":"همیشه response.ok را چک کن — fetch حتی برای ۴۰۴/۵۰۰ هم resolve می‌شود."}}],"title_fa":"جاوااسکریپت مرورگر"},{"id":"js10","title":"Advanced Topics","emoji":"🧠","lessons":[{"title":"Memory Management & Garbage Collection","html":"\n<p>JS has automatic memory management — the <b>garbage collector (GC)<\/b>\nfinds objects that are no longer reachable and frees their memory. You\ndon't call <code>free()<\/code> like in C, but you can still leak\nmemory:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// memory leak: forgotten timer keeps a reference alive\nconst leak = setInterval(() =&gt; { ... }, 1000);\n// if you never call clearInterval(leak), the closure lives forever!\n\n// memory leak: detached DOM nodes\nconst el = document.getElementById(\"old\");\ndocument.body.removeChild(el);\n// if 'el' is still referenced in JS, the DOM node can't be GC'd\n\n// memory leak: unbounded arrays/caches\nconst cache = [];\nfunction addToCache(item) {\n  cache.push(item);    // grows forever — no eviction!\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>The GC uses the <b>mark-and-sweep<\/b> algorithm: starting from\nroots (global object, current function's locals), it marks all\nreachable objects, then sweeps unreachable ones. If an object is\nreachable from a root, it can't be collected — even if nothing\n\"uses\" it.<\/p>\n","title_fa":"مدیریت حافظه و garbage collection","html_fa":"\n<p>JS مدیریت حافظهٔ خودکار دارد — <b>garbage collector (GC)<\/b>\nشیءهایی را که دیگر قابل‌دسترس نیستند پیدا و حافظه‌شان را آزاد می‌کند.\nمثل C لازم نیست <code>free()<\/code> صدا بزنی، اما هنوز می‌توانی حافظه\nنشت بدهی:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">// memory leak: forgotten timer keeps a reference alive\nconst leak = setInterval(() =&gt; { ... }, 1000);\n// if you never call clearInterval(leak), the closure lives forever!\n\n// memory leak: detached DOM nodes\nconst el = document.getElementById(\"old\");\ndocument.body.removeChild(el);\n// if 'el' is still referenced in JS, the DOM node can't be GC'd\n\n// memory leak: unbounded arrays/caches\nconst cache = [];\nfunction addToCache(item) {\n  cache.push(item);    // grows forever — no eviction!\n}<\/pre>\n\n<p>‏GC الگوریتم <b>mark-and-sweep<\/b> را به کار می‌گیرد: از ریشه‌ها (شیء\nسراسری، متغیرهای محلیِ تابع فعلی) شروع می‌کند، همهٔ شیءهای\nقابل‌دسترس را علامت می‌زند، بعد غیرقابل‌دسترس‌ها را جارو می‌کند. اگر\nشیءی از یک ریشه قابل‌دسترس باشد، جمع‌آوری نمی‌شود — حتی اگر هیچ‌کس\n«استفاده‌اش» نکند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Proxy, Reflect & Meta Programming","html":"\n<p><b>Proxy<\/b> wraps an object and intercepts operations on it —\nproperty access, assignment, function calls. <b>Reflect<\/b> provides\nthe default behaviour for these operations:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const handler = {\n  get(target, prop) {\n    console.log(`getting ${prop}`);\n    return Reflect.get(target, prop);    // default behaviour\n  },\n  set(target, prop, value) {\n    console.log(`setting ${prop} to ${value}`);\n    return Reflect.set(target, prop, value);\n  },\n};\n\nconst obj = new Proxy({ name: \"Ada\" }, handler);\nobj.name;     // logs \"getting name\"\nobj.age = 36; // logs \"setting age to 36\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>Proxy use cases: validation, logging, access control, reactive\nsystems (Vue.js uses it!). <code>Reflect<\/code> provides the default\nimplementations so you can call them inside your interceptors.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Proxy: a reactive object (mini-Vue!)\nfunction reactive(obj) {\n  return new Proxy(obj, {\n    set(target, prop, value) {\n      const old = target[prop];\n      target[prop] = value;\n      if (old !== value) {\n        console.log(`⚡ ${prop} changed: ${old} → ${value}`);\n      }\n      return true;\n    },\n  });\n}\n\nconst state = reactive({ count: 0, message: \"hello\" });\nstate.count = 5;       // ⚡ count changed: 0 → 5\nstate.count = 5;       // no log (same value)\nstate.message = \"world\"; // ⚡ message changed\n\n// Reflect: default behaviour with clean API\nconst obj = { a: 1 };\nReflect.set(obj, \"b\", 2);\nconsole.log(Reflect.get(obj, \"b\"));       // 2\nconsole.log(Reflect.has(obj, \"a\"));       // true\nconsole.log(Reflect.ownKeys(obj));        // [\"a\", \"b\"]\n","title_fa":"Proxy، Reflect و فرaprogramming","html_fa":"\n<p><b>Proxy<\/b> یک شیء را می‌پیچد و عملیات‌های رویش را رهگیری می‌کند —\nدسترسی به ویژگی، انتساب، فراخوانی تابع. <b>Reflect<\/b> رفتارِ\nپیش‌فرضِ این عملیات‌ها را می‌دهد:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const handler = {\n  get(target, prop) {\n    console.log(`getting ${prop}`);\n    return Reflect.get(target, prop);    // default behaviour\n  },\n  set(target, prop, value) {\n    console.log(`setting ${prop} to ${value}`);\n    return Reflect.set(target, prop, value);\n  },\n};\n\nconst obj = new Proxy({ name: \"Ada\" }, handler);\nobj.name;     // logs \"getting name\"\nobj.age = 36; // logs \"setting age to 36\"<\/pre>\n\n<p>کاربردهای Proxy: اعتبارسنجی، لاگ، کنترل دسترسی، سیستم‌های\nreactive (‏Vue.js از آن استفاده می‌کند!). <code>Reflect<\/code>\nپیاده‌سازی‌های پیش‌فرض را می‌دهد تا داخل رهگیرهایت صدا بزنی.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Property Descriptors & Immutability","html":"\n<p>Every object property has a <b>descriptor<\/b> with attributes:\n<code>value<\/code>, <code>writable<\/code>, <code>enumerable<\/code>,\n<code>configurable<\/code>. You can inspect and change them:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const obj = { x: 1 };\nconst desc = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(obj, \"x\");\n// { value: 1, writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true }\n\n// make a property read-only\nObject.defineProperty(obj, \"x\", { writable: false });\nobj.x = 99;              // silently fails (strict mode: throws)\nconsole.log(obj.x);      // still 1\n\n// immutability levels\nconst frozen = Object.freeze({ a: 1 });   // can't add, modify, or delete\nconst sealed = Object.seal({ a: 1 });     // can modify, can't add/delete\nconst extensible = Object.preventExtensions({ a: 1 }); // can't add<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Enumerability<\/b> determines if a property shows up in\n<code>for...in<\/code>, <code>Object.keys()<\/code>, and JSON. Built-in\nmethods (like <code>toString<\/code>) are non-enumerable — that's why\nthey don't clutter your loops.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// property descriptors\nconst obj = { visible: true, hidden: false };\nObject.defineProperty(obj, \"secret\", {\n  value: \"classified\",\n  enumerable: false,      // invisible in loops!\n  writable: false,\n});\nconsole.log(obj.secret);             // \"classified\"\nconsole.log(Object.keys(obj));       // [\"visible\", \"hidden\"] — no secret!\nconsole.log(\"secret\" in obj);        // true — still exists\n\n// freeze vs seal\nconst frozen = Object.freeze({ a: 1 });\nconst sealed = Object.seal({ b: 2 });\n\ntry { frozen.a = 99; } catch(e) { /* strict mode throws */ }\nconsole.log(frozen.a);  // 1 (unchanged)\n\nsealed.b = 99;           // ✓ can modify\n// sealed.c = 3;        // ✗ can't add\nconsole.log(sealed.b);  // 99\n\n// deep freeze (freeze nested objects too)\nfunction deepFreeze(obj) {\n  Object.getOwnPropertyNames(obj).forEach(prop => {\n    const val = obj[prop];\n    if (val && typeof val === \"object\") deepFreeze(val);\n  });\n  return Object.freeze(obj);\n}\n","title_fa":"descriptorهای ویژگی و تغییرناپذیری","html_fa":"\n<p>هر ویژگیِ شیء یک <b>descriptor<\/b> دارد با صفات:\n<code>value<\/code>، <code>writable<\/code>، <code>enumerable<\/code> و\n<code>configurable<\/code>. می‌توانی آن‌ها را ببینی و عوض کنی:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const obj = { x: 1 };\nconst desc = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(obj, \"x\");\n// { value: 1, writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true }\n\n// make a property read-only\nObject.defineProperty(obj, \"x\", { writable: false });\nobj.x = 99;              // silently fails (strict mode: throws)\nconsole.log(obj.x);      // still 1\n\n// immutability levels\nconst frozen = Object.freeze({ a: 1 });   // can't add, modify, or delete\nconst sealed = Object.seal({ a: 1 });     // can modify, can't add/delete\nconst extensible = Object.preventExtensions({ a: 1 }); // can't add<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>enumerability<\/b> تعیین می‌کند که ویژگی در <code>for...in<\/code>،\n<code>Object.keys()<\/code> و JSON دیده شود یا نه. متدهای داخلی (مثل\n<code>toString<\/code>) غیرقابل‌شمارش‌اند — برای همین حلقه‌هایت را\nشلوغ نمی‌کنند.<\/p>\n"},{"title":"Internationalization, Typed Arrays & More","html":"\n<p><b>Internationalization (i18n)<\/b> — the <code>Intl<\/code> object\nformats dates, numbers, and strings for different locales:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"USD\" })\n  .format(1234.56);   // \"$1,234.56\"\nnew Intl.NumberFormat(\"de-DE\").format(1234.56);  // \"1.234,56\"\n\nnew Intl.DateTimeFormat(\"fa\", { dateStyle: \"full\" }).format(new Date());\n// Persian date format!\n\nnew Intl.Collator(\"fa\").compare(\"ا\", \"ب\");   // locale-aware sorting<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Typed Arrays<\/b> — binary data with fixed-size numeric types for\nperformance-critical code (canvas, WebGL, file handling):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(16);     // 16 bytes\nconst view = new Int32Array(buffer);     // 4 x 32-bit integers\nview[0] = 42;\nconst f64 = new Float64Array(buffer);    // same bytes, different lens<\/pre>\n\n<p>These topics round out your JS education. MDN's guides cover them in\ndepth — you now have the foundation to understand them all.<\/p>\n","tryit":"// Internationalization\nconsole.log(new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"USD\" }).format(1234.56));\nconsole.log(new Intl.NumberFormat(\"de-DE\").format(1234.56));\nconsole.log(new Intl.NumberFormat(\"fa\").format(1234.56));\n\n// date formatting in different locales\nconst date = new Date();\nconsole.log(date.toLocaleDateString(\"en\", { dateStyle: \"full\" }));\nconsole.log(date.toLocaleDateString(\"fa\", { dateStyle: \"full\" }));\n\n// Typed arrays: binary precision\nconst f32 = new Float32Array(4);\nf32[0] = 3.14159;\nconsole.log(f32[0]);  // 3.141590118408203 (32-bit precision)\nconst f64 = new Float64Array(4);\nf64[0] = 3.14159;\nconsole.log(f64[0]);  // 3.14159 (64-bit — full precision)\n","title_fa":"بین‌المللی‌سازی، Typed Arrayها و بیشتر","html_fa":"\n<p><b>بین‌المللی‌سازی (i18n)<\/b> — شیء <code>Intl<\/code> تاریخ، اعداد و\nرشته‌ها را برای localeهای مختلف قالب‌بندی می‌کند:<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"USD\" })\n  .format(1234.56);   // \"$1,234.56\"\nnew Intl.NumberFormat(\"de-DE\").format(1234.56);  // \"1.234,56\"\n\nnew Intl.DateTimeFormat(\"fa\", { dateStyle: \"full\" }).format(new Date());\n// Persian date format!\n\nnew Intl.Collator(\"fa\").compare(\"ا\", \"ب\");   // locale-aware sorting<\/pre>\n\n<p><b>Typed Arrayها<\/b> — دادهٔ باینری با نوع‌های عددیِ اندازه‌ثابت برای\nکدهای حساس به کارایی (canvas، WebGL، مدیریت فایل):<\/p>\n\n<pre class=\"code\">const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(16);     // 16 bytes\nconst view = new Int32Array(buffer);     // 4 x 32-bit integers\nview[0] = 42;\nconst f64 = new Float64Array(buffer);    // same bytes, different lens<\/pre>\n\n<p>این موضوعات تحصیلاتِ JS تو را کامل می‌کنند. راهنماهای MDN عمیق\nپوشششان می‌دهند — تو حالا بنیادی داری که همه‌شان را بفهمی.<\/p>\n"}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","question":"The JS garbage collector uses which algorithm?","options":["Reference counting only","Mark-and-sweep","Manual free()","Copy collection"],"answer":1,"explain":"Mark reachable objects from roots, sweep unreachable ones.","fa":{"question":"garbage collectorِ JS از کدام الگوریتم استفاده می‌کند؟","options":["فقط شمارشِ ارجاع","Mark-and-sweep","free() دستی","کپی collection"],"explain":"شیءهای قابل‌دسترس را از ریشه‌ها علامت می‌زند، غیرقابل‌دسترس‌ها را جارو می‌کند."}},{"type":"mc","question":"Proxy can intercept:","options":["Only property reads","Property reads, writes, function calls, and more","Only network requests","Only DOM events"],"answer":1,"explain":"Proxy handlers can intercept get, set, apply, has, delete, and more.","fa":{"question":"Proxy می‌تواند چه چیزی را رهگیری کند؟","options":["فقط خواندنِ ویژگی","خواندن، نوشتن، فراخوانی تابع و بیشتر","فقط درخواست‌های شبکه","فقط رخدادهای DOM"],"explain":"هندلرهای Proxy می‌توانند get، set، apply، has، delete و بیشتر را رهگیری کنند."}},{"type":"blank","question":"Object.____ makes an object completely immutable (no add, modify, or delete).","answers":["freeze"],"explain":"Object.freeze is the strictest; Object.seal allows modification but not add/delete.","fa":{"question":"Object.____ شیء را کاملاً تغییرناپذیر می‌کند (نه افزودن، نه تغییر، نه حذف).","explain":"Object.freeze سخت‌گیرانه‌ترین است؛ Object.seal اجازهٔ تغییر می‌دهد اما نه افزودن/حذف."}}],"title_fa":"موضوعات پیشرفته"}]};
